026,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(170,4,9,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Veganism】\nI became interested in vegan lifestyle months ago. As I was surfing videos on the Internet, I came across a woman called Freelee. She claimed to regularly eat around fifty bananas a day to stay healthy. Fifty bananas! I quickly realized that this was not the diet for me. However, what she was saying about veganism did pique my interest. And I went on to watch many more vegan videos. Eventually, I switched to veganism about six months ago.\n\n12. The author knew the vegan lifestyle through ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"online videos\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"her friends\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"vegan books\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"TV programs\"}]','A',NULL,'原文说他在网上刷视频时接触到 vegan 生活方式。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(171,4,9,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Veganism】\nI became interested in vegan lifestyle months ago. As I was surfing videos on the Internet, I came across a woman called Freelee. She claimed to regularly eat around fifty bananas a day to stay healthy. Fifty bananas! I quickly realized that this was not the diet for me. However, what she was saying about veganism did pique my interest. And I went on to watch many more vegan videos. Eventually, I switched to veganism about six months ago.\n\n13. The word \"pique\" (Para. 2) probably means \"________\".','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"express\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"arouse\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"expand\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"protect\"}]','B',NULL,'pique one\'s interest 意为激起兴趣,与 arouse 最接近。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(172,4,9,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Veganism】\nWhile veganism is often associated with physical weakness, that is certainly not the case for me. I have discovered many delicious vegan products, which one might never consider as vegan.\n\nPersonally, eating this way has given me a much more positive outlook on life. Another vegan Kristina\'s story is even more amazing. Kristina was bitten by a deadly spider. She was not given the medicines required to survive the bite. Yet she made a full and speedy recovery. She attributes it to the magic power of a vegan lifestyle.\n\n14. The author believes that the vegan diet is ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"healthy\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"cheap\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"sugar-free\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"low-salt\"}]','A',NULL,'原文说素食没有让他虚弱,反而让他更积极,认为有益健康。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(173,4,9,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Veganism】\nWhile veganism is often associated with physical weakness, that is certainly not the case for me. I have discovered many delicious vegan products, which one might never consider as vegan.\n\nPersonally, eating this way has given me a much more positive outlook on life. Another vegan Kristina\'s story is even more amazing. Kristina was bitten by a deadly spider. She was not given the medicines required to survive the bite. Yet she made a full and speedy recovery. She attributes it to the magic power of a vegan lifestyle.\n\n15. Kristina is mentioned because she ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"attracted a lot of fans\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"had a positive attitude toward life\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"went on a special fruit-based diet\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"quickly recovered from a spider bite\"}]','D',NULL,'克里斯蒂娜被毒蜘蛛咬后迅速痊愈,作者归因于素食。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(174,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第①段】\nOver the last 15 years, more and more people in the US have been drinking bottled water. There is no sign of slowing down. In fact, sales of bottled water are going up faster than other kind of drink. It is true even in cities where it is safe to drink tap water. This has been a disaster for the environment and for our health.\n\n请为第 ① 段选择正确的小标题:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Making droughts worse\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Harmful elements in bottled water\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Need for a better image of tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Growing attention to tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Causing waste and pollution\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Increasing sales of bottled water\"}]','F',NULL,'第①段讲瓶装水销量持续上升。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(175,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第②段】\nMost bottled water comes from underground water. Much of this underground water have flowed into rivers and lakes. Using this water can make droughts (干旱) more serious. Many companies use water from mountain glaciers (冰川), but this is not much better. When the glacier melts, the water usually flows to areas like rivers or wetlands. When companies take glacier water, they take it from areas that need it.\n\n请为第 ② 段选择正确的小标题:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Making droughts worse\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Harmful elements in bottled water\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Need for a better image of tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Growing attention to tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Causing waste and pollution\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Increasing sales of bottled water\"}]','A',NULL,'第②段讲取水加剧干旱。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(176,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第③段】\nIt takes about 1.6 liters of water to make one liter of bottled water. This wastes a lot of water. Also transporting the bottled water to stores burns fuel and creates pollution. The problems do not stop when the water reaches people who buy it. Water bottles are made from plastic which does not break down. Although it can be recycled, people usually do not put it in the recycle can.\n\n请为第 ③ 段选择正确的小标题:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Making droughts worse\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Harmful elements in bottled water\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Need for a better image of tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Growing attention to tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Causing waste and pollution\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Increasing sales of bottled water\"}]','E',NULL,'第③段讲生产运输浪费水并造成污染。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(177,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第④段】\nSome may say that bottled water is safer and healthier than tap water. But that is not true. Sometimes chemicals or bacteria get into bottled water, and companies have to destroy them. Actually, tap water is often healthier than bottled water. Bottled water may lack fluoride (氟化物) which helps protect our teeth. Fluoride is found in tiny amounts in tap water.\n\n请为第 ④ 段选择正确的小标题:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Making droughts worse\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Harmful elements in bottled water\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Need for a better image of tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Growing attention to tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Causing waste and pollution\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Increasing sales of bottled water\"}]','B',NULL,'第④段讲瓶装水也可能含有害物质。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(178,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第⑤段】\nObviously, more people need to know that tap water is safer and healthier. Unfortunately, tap water cannot advertise itself. When a product that is cheaper and better does not win, that is bad news. When the product is water, we all lose.\n\n请为第 ⑤ 段选择正确的小标题:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Making droughts worse\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Harmful elements in bottled water\"}, {\"key