\": \"brings more health benefits\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"with the problem of drought\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"despite the safety of tap water\"}]','E',NULL,'第②段说取冰川水会加剧取水地区的干旱。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(181,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第③段】\nIt takes about 1.6 liters of water to make one liter of bottled water. This wastes a lot of water. Also transporting the bottled water to stores burns fuel and creates pollution. The problems do not stop when the water reaches people who buy it. Water bottles are made from plastic which does not break down. Although it can be recycled, people usually do not put it in the recycle can.\n\n补全句子:Transportation of bottled water ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in tiny amounts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"towards tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"does harm to the environment\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"brings more health benefits\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"with the problem of drought\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"despite the safety of tap water\"}]','C',NULL,'第③段说运输瓶装水要烧燃料、造成污染。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(182,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第④段】\nSome may say that bottled water is safer and healthier than tap water. But that is not true. Sometimes chemicals or bacteria get into bottled water, and companies have to destroy them. Actually, tap water is often healthier than bottled water. Bottled water may lack fluoride (氟化物) which helps protect our teeth. Fluoride is found in tiny amounts in tap water.\n\n补全句子:Compared with bottled water, tap water ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in tiny amounts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"towards tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"does harm to the environment\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"brings more health benefits\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"with the problem of drought\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"despite the safety of tap water\"}]','D',NULL,'第④段说自来水往往更健康。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(183,4,12,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Bottled Water 第⑤段】\nObviously, more people need to know that tap water is safer and healthier. Unfortunately, tap water cannot advertise itself. When a product that is cheaper and better does not win, that is bad news. When the product is water, we all lose.\n\n补全句子:People need to change their attitude ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in tiny amounts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"towards tap water\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"does harm to the environment\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"brings more health benefits\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"with the problem of drought\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"despite the safety of tap water\"}]','B',NULL,'第⑤段说要让更多人知道自来水更安全,即改变对自来水的态度。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(184,4,13,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Bird Maps and Compasses】\nEvery year hundreds of species of birds take long trips. ___ In the fall, they fly to warmer climates where food is plentiful all winter.\n\n第 26 空应填入:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The bands contained a name and address.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Birds use the earth\'s magnetic field to navigate too.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"A map and a compass are often helpful for long trips.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"They fly thousands of miles from one home to another.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"They learn the route that the older geese have traveled before.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"They have answered many questions about how birds navigate.\"}]','D',NULL,'空格后讲秋季与春季的迁徙,前面应先说它们飞越数千英里。',2,'2026年4月英语(专升本)真题',2026,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-16 07:54:55','2026-10-16 07:54:55'),(185,4,13,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Bird Maps and Compasses】\nIn the 1800s, scientists started putt