RAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1111,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Ambition Can Lead to Success】Since his early years Reid had been thinking (think) of changing the world. As he grew __ (old) he became interested in the Internet and the tech industry. At first, he started a social network. But __ (fortunately) he faced big problems that forced him to stop.\nOne day Reid got an idea. It was to provide a __(43)__ (solve) for people to pay online.','[]','solution',NULL,'provide a solution，提供解决方案。名词形式。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1112,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','They could use their emails instead of credit __(44)__ (card).','[]','cards',NULL,'credit card 意为信用卡，此处泛指使用电子邮件代替信用卡，应用复数形式 cards。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1113,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','PayPal faced tough competition from large credit card companies. It was hardly __(45)__ (profit), but after a long struggle, it became __46__.','[]','profitable',NULL,'was 后接形容词作表语，hardly profitable 意为几乎没有利润。',2,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1114,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','It was hardly __45__, but after a long struggle, it became __(46)__ (success).','[]','successful',NULL,'became 是系动词，后接形容词 successful 作表语。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1115,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','Reid was not __(47)__ (satisfy). He kept searching for the next big thing that can help him improve people\'s lives.','[]','satisfied',NULL,'be satisfied 表示感到满足的（修饰人），be satisfying 表示令人满足的（修饰物）。主语是 Reid，故用 satisfied。',2,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1116,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','One day he __(48)__ (find) that people spend a lot of time __49__.','[]','found',NULL,'根据 One day 和上下文语境（讲述过去发生的事），句子时态为一般过去时，find 的过去式为 found。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1117,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','One day he __48__ that people spend a lot of time __(49)__ (look) for jobs online.','[]','looking',NULL,'spend time (in) doing sth. 为固定搭配，意为花费时间做某事。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1118,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','So he decided to create a website that connects employers with job seekers and __(50)__ (name) it LinkedIn.','[]','named',NULL,'and 连接两个并列的动作 decided 和 named，故此处应填过去式 named。',2,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1119,4,NULL,'WRITING','请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇 100 词左右的英文写作任务。\n\n某英文报社正在举办题为“My Goal for Next Year”的征文活动。请你根据下述写作要点提交一篇英文短文应征。\n● 你明年的目标是什么？\n● 你打算如何实现这一目标？','[]',NULL,'[\"明确写出明年的具体目标（如通过考试、学习新技能等）\", \"详细阐述实现该目标的具体计划或步骤\", \"语言表达流畅，符合英语写作规范，字数在100词左右\"]','',3,'英语二1',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1120,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】\nYou may find it crazy that your dog buries his favorite bone or chew toy, only to dig it up a day or two later, but there is actually a reason behind it—it is simply in their nature. For thousands of years, dogs have buried their bones. The practice itself started long before dogs were even pets when they had to bury bones to survive.\n\nWhen dogs lived in the wild, sometimes food was scarce. If they were able to find food, dogs became very protective of it. Sometimes they would have more bones than they could eat for one meal. To keep other dogs and animals from stealing their bones, dogs would bury them in the ground. When it was time for the next meal, they would dig up their bones and enjoy them again. This would continue until the bones were gone.\n\nEven though most dogs have plenty of food to eat today, their instincts still tell them to bury their bones and favorite toys. They do this to keep other dogs and animals from stealing them, just like their ancestors did. Some dogs keep at least two bones buried at once. When they want to dig up one, they will bury one more. This may leave a backyard full of holes and bones.\n\nHow do dogs decide where to bury their bones? A dog cannot bury a bone just anywhere. He must first find the perfect spot. This involves using his nose to find a spot that is free from other dogs and animals. Often it is near a tree or a large rock, but it could be anywhere in the yard. Once the dog finds the perfect spot, he uses his front paws to dig a hole, drops the bone in and covers up the hole to protect his treasure.\n\nDogs bury their favorite bones or chew toys by nature.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第一段 \'but there is actually a reason behind it—it is simply in their nature\'（但这背后其实有一个原因——这纯粹是它们的天性），可知题目表述正确。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1121,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】The practice itself started long before dogs were even pets when they had to bury bones to survive.\n\nDogs started to bury their bones when they became pets.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文中提到“The practice itself started long before dogs were even pets”，说明狗在成为宠物之前就开始埋骨头了，故该陈述错误。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1122,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】When dogs lived in the wild, sometimes food was scarce.\n\nDogs in the wild occasionally had enough food.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中说“sometimes food was scarce”（有时食物短缺），暗示其他时候是有食物的；且后文提到“If they were able to find food... Sometimes they would have more bones than they could eat”，说明它们确实偶尔会有足够的食物。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1123,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】To keep other dogs and animals from stealing their bones, dogs would bury them in the ground.\n\nDogs would bury their extra food for their babies.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文中明确指出狗埋骨头是为了“To keep other dogs and animals from stealing their bones”（防止被偷），而不是为了留给幼崽（babies）。虽然未提及幼崽，但给出的理由与题干不符，通常此类情况判为 False。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1124,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】To keep other dogs and animals from stealing their bones, dogs would bury them in the ground.\n\nAnimals would start a fierce fight over food in ancient times.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中只提到狗为了防止被偷而埋骨头，并没有描述动物之间是否发生过激烈的打斗（fierce fight）。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1125,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】Some dogs keep at least two bones buried at once.\n\nSome dogs tend to store up more than one bone at the same time.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中提到“Some dogs keep at least two bones buried at once”，即有些狗同时埋藏至少两根骨头，这与题干意思一致。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1126,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】This may leave a backyard full of holes and bones.\n\nThe backyard of a dog owner may be full of holes dug by his dog.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中最后一句提到这种行为可能会让后院满是洞和骨头（full of holes and bones），符合题干描述。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1127,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】Often it is near a tree or a large rock, but it could be anywhere in the yard.\n\nDogs often bury their bones far away from trees.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文中说“Often it is near a tree...”（经常在树附近），题干说是“far away from trees”（远离树木），两者相反。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1128,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】This involves using his nose to find a spot that is free from other dogs and animals.\n\nDogs use their paws to find spots for burying bones.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文中指出找地点是用鼻子（using his nose to find a spot），爪子是用来挖洞的（uses his front paws to dig a hole）。题干混淆了功能。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1129,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Why Dogs Bury Their Favorite Bones】your dog buries his favorite bone or chew toy...\n\nDogs bury more bones than chew toys.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到了狗会埋骨头或咀嚼玩具，但没有比较哪种埋得更多。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1130,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Public Wi-Fi Users Neglect Safety】A recent survey shows that 25% of Internet users have done online banking through public Wi-Fi in the last three months. It also shows that 27% have bought a product or service with a credit card this way.\n\nExperts worry that hackers (黑客) will take advantage of these practices. Doug Shadel said that hackers usually attack in two ways. They may create Wi-Fi hotspots that have the same name of the ones you trust, such as a hotel or a coffee shop. They may also provide a stronger Wi-Fi signal to get between you and the safe hotspot. In either case, the hackers can see your email, credit card information, user names and passwords.\n\nSometimes hackers just set up their electronic traps near a business where people enjoy the free Wi-Fi. \"In most cases they are after your personal information\", Shadel said. \"If you use the same user name and password for many accounts, they can get into them all. It\'s possible for any hacker to do it. The software to hack into a Wi-Fi network is available at little or no cost.\"\n\n\"It\'s difficult for people to know if a Wi-Fi network is safe,\" Shadel said. \"So you should just think they are not. Any shared Internet access, free or paid, carries the same level of risk. It is safe only when you or someone you trust directly controls it.\"\n\nShadel sometimes checks email through public Wi-Fi. But he never does any banking that way. In an unfamiliar place, he uses a Virtual Private Network (VPN). \"This service creates a passage between your device and a safe place on the Internet,\" he said.\n\n11. A recent survey finds that 25% of Internet users use public Wi-Fi to ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"do banking\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"buy things\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"provide service\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"play cards\"}]','A',NULL,'根据文章第一段第一句 \'A recent survey shows that 25% of Internet users have done online banking through public Wi-Fi...\' 可知，25%的用户通过公共Wi-Fi进行银行业务。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1131,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Public Wi-Fi Users Neglect Safety】A recent survey shows that 25% of Internet users have done online banking through public Wi-Fi in the last three months. It also shows that 27% have bought a product or service with a credit card this way.\n\nExperts worry that hackers (黑客) will take advantage of these practices. Doug Shadel said that hackers usually attack in two ways. They may create Wi-Fi hotspots that have the same name of the ones you trust, such as a hotel or a coffee shop. They may also provide a stronger Wi-Fi signal to get between you and the safe hotspot. In either case, the hackers can see your email, credit card information, user names and passwords.\n\nSometimes hackers just set up their electronic traps near a business where people enjoy the free Wi-Fi. \"In most cases they are after your personal information\", Shadel said. \"If you use the same user name and password for many accounts, they can get into them all. It\'s possible for any hacker to do it. The software to hack into a Wi-Fi network is available at little or no cost.\"\n\n\"It\'s difficult for people to know if a Wi-Fi network is safe,\" Shadel said. \"So you should just think they are not. Any shared Internet access, free or paid, carries the same level of risk. It is safe only when you or someone you trust directly controls it.\"\n\nShadel sometimes checks email through public Wi-Fi. But he never does any banking that way. In an unfamiliar place, he uses a Virtual Private Network (VPN). \"This service creates a passage between your device and a safe place on the Internet,\" he said.\n\n12. The phrase \"take advantage of\" (Para. 2) can best be replaced by \"______\".','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"adjust to\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"benefit from\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"lead to\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"result from\"}]','B',NULL,'\'take advantage of\' 意为利用、占便宜。在文中指黑客利用用户的行为获利。选项 B \'benefit from\' (从...获益/利用) 意思最接近。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1132,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Public Wi-Fi Users Neglect Safety】A recent survey shows that 25% of Internet users have done online banking through public Wi-Fi in the last three months. It also shows that 27% have bought a product or service with a credit card this way.\n\nExperts worry that hackers (黑客) will take advantage of these practices. Doug Shadel said that hackers usually attack in two ways. They may create Wi-Fi hotspots that have the same name of the ones you trust, such as a hotel or a coffee shop. They may also provide a stronger Wi-Fi signal to get between you and the safe hotspot. In either case, the hackers can see your email, credit card information, user names and passwords.\n\nSometimes hackers just set up their electronic traps near a business where people enjoy the free Wi-Fi. \"In most cases they are after your personal information\", Shadel said. \"If you use the same user name and password for many accounts, they can get into them all. It\'s possible for any hacker to do it. The software to hack into a Wi-Fi network is available at little or no cost.\"\n\n\"It\'s difficult for people to know if a Wi-Fi network is safe,\" Shadel said. \"So you should just think they are not. Any shared Internet access, free or paid, carries the same level of risk. It is safe only when you or someone you trust directly controls it.\"\n\nShadel sometimes checks email through public Wi-Fi. But he never does any banking that way. In an unfamiliar place, he uses a Virtual Private Network (VPN). \"This service creates a passage between your device and a safe place on the Internet,\" he said.\n\n13. According to Shadel, any hacker can ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"create different passwords\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"open an electronic account\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"steal people\'s information\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"write software for businesses\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第三段 Shadel 的话 \'In most cases they are after your personal information\' (大多数情况下他们是在窃取你的个人信息)，以及前文提到的黑客可以看到 email, credit card information 等，可知黑客可以窃取人们的信息。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1133,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Public Wi-Fi Users Neglect Safety】A recent survey shows that 25% of Internet users have done online banking through public Wi-Fi in the last three months. It also shows that 27% have bought a product or service with a credit card this way.\n\nExperts worry that hackers (黑客) will take advantage of these practices. Doug Shadel said that hackers usually attack in two ways. They may create Wi-Fi hotspots that have the same name of the ones you trust, such as a hotel or a coffee shop. They may also provide a stronger Wi-Fi signal to get between you and the safe hotspot. In either case, the hackers can see your email, credit card information, user names and passwords.\n\nSometimes hackers just set up their electronic traps near a business where people enjoy the free Wi-Fi. \"In most cases they are after your personal information\", Shadel said. \"If you use the same user name and password for many accounts, they can get into them all. It\'s possible for any hacker to do it. The software to hack into a Wi-Fi network is available at little or no cost.\"\n\n\"It\'s difficult for people to know if a Wi-Fi network is safe,\" Shadel said. \"So you should just think they are not. Any shared Internet access, free or paid, carries the same level of risk. It is safe only when you or someone you trust directly controls it.\"\n\nShadel sometimes checks email through public Wi-Fi. But he never does any banking that way. In an unfamiliar place, he uses a Virtual Private Network (VPN). \"This service creates a passage between your device and a safe place on the Internet,\" he said.\n\n14. For the sake of safety, Internet users are advised to ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"test shared Internet access\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"rely on paid Internet access\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"look for free Internet access\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"avoid shared Internet access\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第四段 Shadel 的建议 \'Any shared Internet access, free or paid, carries the same level of risk. It is safe only when you or someone you trust directly controls it.\' 可知，为了安全起见，应避免使用共享的网络接入（shared Internet access）。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1134,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Public Wi-Fi Users Neglect Safety】A recent survey shows that 25% of Internet users have done online banking through public Wi-Fi in the last three months. It also shows that 27% have bought a product or service with a credit card this way.\n\nExperts worry that hackers (黑客) will take advantage of these practices. Doug Shadel said that hackers usually attack in two ways. They may create Wi-Fi hotspots that have the same name of the ones you trust, such as a hotel or a coffee shop. They may also provide a stronger Wi-Fi signal to get between you and the safe hotspot. In either case, the hackers can see your email, credit card information, user names and passwords.\n\nSometimes hackers just set up their electronic traps near a business where people enjoy the free Wi-Fi. \"In most cases they are after your personal information\", Shadel said. \"If you use the same user name and password for many accounts, they can get into them all. It\'s possible for any hacker to do it. The software to hack into a Wi-Fi network is available at little or no cost.\"\n\n\"It\'s difficult for people to know if a Wi-Fi network is safe,\" Shadel said. \"So you should just think they are not. Any shared Internet access, free or paid, carries the same level of risk. It is safe only when you or someone you trust directly controls it.\"\n\nShadel sometimes checks email through public Wi-Fi. But he never does any banking that way. In an unfamiliar place, he uses a Virtual Private Network (VPN). \"This service creates a passage between your device and a safe place on the Internet,\" he said.\n\n15. Shadel uses public Wi-Fi to ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"learn about VPN\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"deal with his emails\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"keep his account safe\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"handle financial matters\"}]','B',NULL,'根据最后一段第一句 \'Shadel sometimes checks email through public Wi-Fi.\' 可知他用公共Wi-Fi查看邮件。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1135,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nI wake up at 6 a. m. every day. The first thing I do when I wake up is grab my smartphone and take it to the bathroom with me, where I start my day by consuming quite a lot of information. I go to some websites, but the main site that I focus on during this time is Nuzzel, a collector of headlines and links. I recommend everyone look into it if they feel they don\'t have time to properly focus on every website individually.\n\nParagraph ①:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I do some morning exercise.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I phone my parents or sister.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"I prepare my kids for school.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I communicate with others online.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"I help my kids with their homework.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"I visit websites to get information.\"}]','F',NULL,'第一段主要讲述作者起床后通过浏览网站（如Nuzzel）获取信息，对应选项 F。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1136,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nAfter visiting those sites, I head to Twitter, my No. 1 outlet for communication with the public. Twitter is becoming a listening platform. There is such a volume of information on the platform that you need pay attention to. So I spend a great amount of my morning responding to people and starting conversations.\n\nParagraph ②:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I do some morning exercise.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I phone my parents or sister.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"I prepare my kids for school.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I communicate with others online.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"I help my kids with their homework.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"I visit websites to get information.\"}]','D',NULL,'第二段主要讲述作者在Twitter上与人交流、回应他人，对应选项 D。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1137,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nAfter all this comes my workout (锻炼) with my trainer. I usually work out for about 45 minutes. The specific workout routine varies depending on the day of the week, what I ate, and how much I\'ve been traveling.\n\nParagraph ③:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I do some morning exercise.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I phone my parents or sister.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"I prepare my kids for school.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I communicate with others online.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"I help my kids with their homework.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"I visit websites to get information.\"}]','A',NULL,'第三段主要讲述作者的晨练（workout），对应选项 A。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1138,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nAfter the workout, I head back home to get my children ready for school. I say bye to them and give them each a kiss before they leave. Then, I\'m off to my office, often before 9 a. m.\n\nParagraph ④:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I do some morning exercise.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I phone my parents or sister.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"I prepare my kids for school.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I communicate with others online.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"I help my kids with their homework.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"I visit websites to get information.\"}]','C',NULL,'第四段主要讲述作者送孩子上学前的准备，对应选项 C。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1139,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nIn the car to my office, I call my mom, dad or sister. I talk to them just to learn what they\'re up to. I really value those small moments. By the time I step into my office, so much is going through my head. My day starts the minute I open my eyes.\n\nParagraph ⑤:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I do some morning exercise.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I phone my parents or sister.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"I prepare my kids for school.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I communicate with others online.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"I help my kids with their homework.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"I visit websites to get information.\"}]','B',NULL,'第五段主要讲述作者在去办公室的路上给家人打电话，对应选项 B。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1140,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nI wake up at 6 a. m. every day. The first thing I do when I wake up is grab my smartphone and take it to the bathroom with me, where I start my day by consuming quite a lot of information. I go to some websites, but the main site that I focus on during this time is Nuzzel, a collector of headlines and links. I recommend everyone look into it if they feel they don\'t have time to properly focus on every website individually.\n\nNuzzel helps me ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"to listen to others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"step into my office\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"kiss them goodbye\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"affect my workout routine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to learn how they are doing\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to surf the Internet efficiently\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第一段，Nuzzel是一个收集标题和链接的网站，帮助那些没有时间逐个浏览网站的人，即帮助高效上网。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1141,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nAfter visiting those sites, I head to Twitter, my No. 1 outlet for communication with the public. Twitter is becoming a listening platform. There is such a volume of information on the platform that you need pay attention to. So I spend a great amount of my morning responding to people and starting conversations.\n\nOn Twitter I am able ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"to listen to others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"step into my office\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"kiss them goodbye\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"affect my workout routine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to learn how they are doing\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to surf the Internet efficiently\"}]','A',NULL,'根据第二段，Twitter正在成为一个倾听平台（listening platform）。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1142,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nAfter all this comes my workout (锻炼) with my trainer. I usually work out for about 45 minutes. The specific workout routine varies depending on the day of the week, what I ate, and how much I\'ve been traveling.\n\nThere are several factors that ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"to listen to others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"step into my office\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"kiss them goodbye\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"affect my workout routine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to learn how they are doing\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to surf the Internet efficiently\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第三段，具体的锻炼计划取决于星期几、吃了什么以及旅行多少等因素，这些因素影响了锻炼常规。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1143,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nAfter the workout, I head back home to get my children ready for school. I say bye to them and give them each a kiss before they leave. Then, I\'m off to my office, often before 9 a. m.\n\nBefore my kids go to school, I ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"to listen to others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"step into my office\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"kiss them goodbye\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"affect my workout routine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to learn how they are doing\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to surf the Internet efficiently\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第四段，在孩子离开前，我会跟他们说再见并亲吻他们（give them each a kiss before they leave）。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1144,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · I Use Every Second Before I Go to Work】\nIn the car to my office, I call my mom, dad or sister. I talk to them just to learn what they\'re up to. I really value those small moments. By the time I step into my office, so much is going through my head. My day starts the minute I open my eyes.\n\nI call my parents ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"to listen to others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"step into my office\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"kiss them goodbye\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"affect my workout routine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to learn how they are doing\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to surf the Internet efficiently\"}]','E',NULL,'根据第五段，我给父母或姐妹打电话只是为了了解他们在做什么（learn what they\'re up to），即了解他们的近况。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1145,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Banning Mobile Phones at School】It is a question that keeps some parents awake at night. Should children be allowed to take mobile phones to school? __(26)__ For parents who want their children to do well at school, it is no.\n\nBanning mobile phones at school is effective. According to a UK study, after schools banned mobile phones, the test scores of students improved by 6.4%. The findings will influence the debate about children and mobile phones. In the UK, more than 90% of teenagers own a mobile phone; in the US, 75% have one. The popular mobile phone is a problem in the eye of teachers. _27_ In a 2001 survey, no school banned mobiles. By 2007, this had risen to 50%. By 2012, 98% of schools had taken action. Some did not allow phones. The others required them to be handed in at the beginning of the day.\n\n_28_ New York City has lifted a 10-year ban on phones at school. It says that lifting the ban will promote equality. \"This view is wrong,\" the researchers of the UK study write. \"We found that the ban led to improvements in test scores among students. Low-achieving students gained the most. _29_ Allowing phones into schools will harm the lowest-achieving students the most.\"\n\nThe UK study was carried out at Birmingham, London, Leicester and Manchester schools before and after bans were introduced. \"Technology is commonly viewed as increasing efficiency,\" the researchers write. \"Modern technology is used in the classroom to improve student performance. _30_ Some students will pay no attention to their class.\"','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They are worried about the trend.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The mobile phone is a good example.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"However, there are potential problems.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Now researchers say that they have an answer.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Therefore, lifting the ban may in fact lead to the opposite.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"However, some schools are starting to allow limited use of mobile phones.\"}]','D',NULL,'前文提出了一个问题“Should children be allowed...?”，后文给出了回答“it is no”，选项 D“现在研究人员说他们有了答案”承上启下。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1146,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · Failing Forward】There are several key abilities that allow successful people to fail forward instead of taking each setback personally. First, successful people don\'t blame themselves when they fail. They take __(31)__ for each setback, but they don\'t take the failure personally. Second, successful people don\'t __32__ themselves by individual failures. They __33__ that each setback is a small __34__ of the whole. Third, achievers are __35__ to vary their approaches to problems. That\'s important in every walk of life. If one __36__ doesn\'t work for you, if it brings repeated failures, __37__ try something else. To fail forward, you must do what works for you, not __38__ what works for other people. Finally, successful people are __39__. They don\'t let one error keep them down. They learn from their mistakes and __40__ on.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"lucky\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"move\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"responsibility\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"then\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"necessarily\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"part\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"tough\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"willing\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"approach\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"recognize\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"easily\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"define\"}]','C',NULL,'take responsibility for... 为……承担责任。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1147,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Achieving Success in a Presentation】The success of a presentation (present) is leaving your audience with something of value. What do they get from __(41)__ (spend) time listening to your presentation? Many people think that they need to be brilliant to present well. They think that they need to be smart, witty and __42__ (charm) before they start to write a speech. Those qualities can come __43__ (natural), but most often, they come as a result of the passion and knowledge of the __44__ (speak).\n\nOne of the vital factors in having an __45__ (effect) presentation is serving the needs of your audience. Caring for your audience\'s needs __46__ (require) no perfection. You can','[]','spending',NULL,'from 是介词，后接动名词形式。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1148,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Achieving Success in a Presentation】The success of a presentation (present) is leaving your audience with something of value. What do they get from __41__ (spend) time listening to your presentation? Many people think that they need to be brilliant to present well. They think that they need to be smart, witty and __42__ (charm) before they start to write a speech. Those qualities can come __43__ (natural), but most often, they come as a result of the passion and knowledge of the __44__ (speak).\n\nOne of the vital factors in having an __45__ (effect) presentation is serving the needs of your audience. Caring for your audience\'s needs __46__ (require) no perfection. You can make __(47)__ (mistake) and it\'s going to be OK. The __48__ (equip) can fail and it\'s still going to be OK. You don\'t have to use humor to be a __49__ (win). With that in mind, the real point is more like being successful at __50__ (reach) your audience.','[]','mistakes',NULL,'make mistakes 是固定搭配，意为“犯错误”，mistake 为可数名词，此处用复数形式。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1149,4,NULL,'WRITING','请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇 100 词左右的英文写作任务。\n\n假设你刚找到一份满意的工作。请给你的美国朋友 Tom 写一封英文电子邮件，分享你的喜悦，内容包括：\n● 你找了一份什么工作。\n● 你为什么喜欢这份工作？\n请以 Li Ke 署名。','[]',NULL,'[\"邮件格式正确（称呼、正文、落款）\", \"明确说明找到了什么工作\", \"阐述喜欢这份工作的原因（如薪资、兴趣、发展前景等）\", \"语言流畅，字数符合要求\"]','',2,'英语二1',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1150,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychological and educational theories, self-esteem is essential for a successful life. Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem, and that this deficiency is central to any problems they may have in making their way in the world.\n\nWell, guess what? A new research has found that self-esteem can be just as high among grade D students and drunk drivers as it is among Nobel Prize winners and former presidents. In fact, people with high self-esteem can engage in far more anti-social behavior than those with low self-esteem. \"We used to believe that high self-esteem would cause all sorts of positive consequences and that if we raised self-esteem, people would do better in life,\" a researcher said. \"Mostly, the data have failed to support that.\" Racists, street thugs (恶棍) and school bullies (恶霸) all have high scores on the self-esteem tests. And you can see why. If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way. So you hit out or commit crimes to defend your pride. After all, who are they to suggest that you could be doing something wrong? What do they know?\n\nSelf-esteem can also be an educational concern. College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students. When every grade in the school is assessed so as to make the kid feel good rather than to give an accurate measure of his work, the kid can develop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nIt is believed that minority kids often have self-esteem problems.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第一段最后一句 \'Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem...\'，可知人们认为少数族裔儿童往往有自尊问题。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1151,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychological and educational theories, self-esteem is essential for a successful life. Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem, and that this deficiency is central to any problems they may have in making their way in the world.\n\nWell, guess what? A new research has found that self-esteem can be just as high among grade D students and drunk drivers as it is among Nobel Prize winners and former presidents. In fact, people with high self-esteem can engage in far more anti-social behavior than those with low self-esteem. \"We used to believe that high self-esteem would cause all sorts of positive consequences and that if we raised self-esteem, people would do better in life,\" a researcher said. \"Mostly, the data have failed to support that.\" Racists, street thugs (恶棍) and school bullies (恶霸) all have high scores on the self-esteem tests. And you can see why. If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way. So you hit out or commit crimes to defend your pride. After all, who are they to suggest that you could be doing something wrong? What do they know?\n\nSelf-esteem can also be an educational concern. College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students. When every grade in the school is assessed so as to make the kid feel good rather than to give an accurate measure of his work, the kid can develop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nA new research shows that high self-esteem is essential to success.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第二段，新的研究发现高自尊的人可能从事更多的反社会行为，且数据未能支持高自尊会导致积极后果的观点。因此新研究并未显示高自尊对成功至关重要，而是反驳了这一观点。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1152,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychological and educational theories, self-esteem is essential for a successful life. Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem, and that this deficiency is central to any problems they may have in making their way in the world.\n\nWell, guess what? A new research has found that self-esteem can be just as high among grade D students and drunk drivers as it is among Nobel Prize winners and former presidents. In fact, people with high self-esteem can engage in far more anti-social behavior than those with low self-esteem. \"We used to believe that high self-esteem would cause all sorts of positive consequences and that if we raised self-esteem, people would do better in life,\" a researcher said. \"Mostly, the data have failed to support that.\" Racists, street thugs (恶棍) and school bullies (恶霸) all have high scores on the self-esteem tests. And you can see why. If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way. So you hit out or commit crimes to defend your pride. After all, who are they to suggest that you could be doing something wrong? What do they know?\n\nSelf-esteem can also be an educational concern. College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students. When every grade in the school is assessed so as to make the kid feel good rather than to give an accurate measure of his work, the kid can develop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nParents are responsible for their children\'s self-esteem.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章中提到了孩子接受的教育理论以及大学教师对学生的抱怨，但并未提及父母是否对孩子的自尊心负责。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1153,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychologic