evelop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nPeople with high self-esteem are hurt more easily.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第二段最后部分 \'If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way.\'，可知高自尊的人如果别人不那样对待他们，他们会特别感到被冒犯（受伤），即更容易受伤害。',3,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1156,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychological and educational theories, self-esteem is essential for a successful life. Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem, and that this deficiency is central to any problems they may have in making their way in the world.\n\nWell, guess what? A new research has found that self-esteem can be just as high among grade D students and drunk drivers as it is among Nobel Prize winners and former presidents. In fact, people with high self-esteem can engage in far more anti-social behavior than those with low self-esteem. \"We used to believe that high self-esteem would cause all sorts of positive consequences and that if we raised self-esteem, people would do better in life,\" a researcher said. \"Mostly, the data have failed to support that.\" Racists, street thugs (恶棍) and school bullies (恶霸) all have high scores on the self-esteem tests. And you can see why. If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way. So you hit out or commit crimes to defend your pride. After all, who are they to suggest that you could be doing something wrong? What do they know?\n\nSelf-esteem can also be an educational concern. College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students. When every grade in the school is assessed so as to make the kid feel good rather than to give an accurate measure of his work, the kid can develop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nCollege students are faced with high economic pressure.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章主要讨论的是自尊和教育评价的问题，完全没有提到大学生面临的经济压力。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1157,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychological and educational theories, self-esteem is essential for a successful life. Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem, and that this deficiency is central to any problems they may have in making their way in the world.\n\nWell, guess what? A new research has found that self-esteem can be just as high among grade D students and drunk drivers as it is among Nobel Prize winners and former presidents. In fact, people with high self-esteem can engage in far more anti-social behavior than those with low self-esteem. \"We used to believe that high self-esteem would cause all sorts of positive consequences and that if we raised self-esteem, people would do better in life,\" a researcher said. \"Mostly, the data have failed to support that.\" Racists, street thugs (恶棍) and school bullies (恶霸) all have high scores on the self-esteem tests. And you can see why. If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way. So you hit out or commit crimes to defend your pride. After all, who are they to suggest that you could be doing something wrong? What do they know?\n\nSelf-esteem can also be an educational concern. College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students. When every grade in the school is assessed so as to make the kid feel good rather than to give an accurate measure of his work, the kid can develop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nCollege teachers are often annoyed with students\' high self-esteem.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第三段第一句 \'College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students.\'，可知大学老师经常抱怨学生的高自尊，即对此感到恼火。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1158,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychological and educational theories, self-esteem is essential for a successful life. Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem, and that this deficiency is central to any problems they may have in making their way in the world.\n\nWell, guess what? A new research has found that self-esteem can be just as high among grade D students and drunk drivers as it is among Nobel Prize winners and former presidents. In fact, people with high self-esteem can engage in far more anti-social behavior than those with low self-esteem. \"We used to believe that high self-esteem would cause all sorts of positive consequences and that if we raised self-esteem, people would do better in life,\" a researcher said. \"Mostly, the data have failed to support that.\" Racists, street thugs (恶棍) and school bullies (恶霸) all have high scores on the self-esteem tests. And you can see why. If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way. So you hit out or commit crimes to defend your pride. After all, who are they to suggest that you could be doing something wrong? What do they know?\n\nSelf-esteem can also be an educational concern. College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students. When every grade in the school is assessed so as to make the kid feel good rather than to give an accurate measure of his work, the kid can develop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nHigh grades help students know the truth of themselves.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第三段中间部分，当分数是为了让孩子感觉良好而不是准确衡量工作时，孩子会发展出与事实危险地无关的自尊。这意味着高分（grade inflation）反而阻碍了学生了解真实的自己。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1159,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Lacking in Self-Esteem(自尊)? Good for you!】According to psychological and educational theories, self-esteem is essential for a successful life. Generations of children, especially minority kids, have been educated according to the theory that they lack self-esteem, and that this deficiency is central to any problems they may have in making their way in the world.\n\nWell, guess what? A new research has found that self-esteem can be just as high among grade D students and drunk drivers as it is among Nobel Prize winners and former presidents. In fact, people with high self-esteem can engage in far more anti-social behavior than those with low self-esteem. \"We used to believe that high self-esteem would cause all sorts of positive consequences and that if we raised self-esteem, people would do better in life,\" a researcher said. \"Mostly, the data have failed to support that.\" Racists, street thugs (恶棍) and school bullies (恶霸) all have high scores on the self-esteem tests. And you can see why. If you think you\'re highly gifted, you\'re particularly offended if other people don\'t treat you that way. So you hit out or commit crimes to defend your pride. After all, who are they to suggest that you could be doing something wrong? What do they know?\n\nSelf-esteem can also be an educational concern. College teachers are constantly complaining about the high self-esteem of their students. When every grade in the school is assessed so as to make the kid feel good rather than to give an accurate measure of his work, the kid can develop self-esteem dangerously unrelated to the truth. When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry. Weak professors give in to the pressure—hence, grade inflation, which results in their students\' vague touch with reality.\n\nSome college students may find a C grade offending.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第三段倒数第二句 \'When he\'s told he is getting a C grade in college, he can then get deeply offended or extremely angry.\'，可知有些大学生可能会觉得C等是一种冒犯。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1160,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Organic Farming】farmers have been returning to organic farming.\n\nIn organic farming, farm products are produced in more natural ways. Crops, meat and other food are produced without chemicals. Chemical fertilizers, pesticides, and growth hormones (激素) are forbidden. Farmers enrich the soil with natural fertilizers. They pull out weeds by hand. Hay and straw are put between the rows of plants to stop weeding. They rely on the natural enemies of pests to control pests. Animals are fed organically and can eat grass outdoors. Cows, for example, are kept in pastures (草场) and fields. Vegetables and fruit are also produced with organic methods.\n\nOrganic farming enjoys many advantages. For example, crop rotation can preserve the good qualities of soils. The growing of different crops can keep soils healthy and fertile. Organic farming is healthier for farm workers, and there are fewer remains of chemicals in food. In the long term, organic farms save energy and protect the environment. It can slow down global warming and reduce the pollution of ground water.\n\nMeanwhile, there are some disadvantages. Organic food is more expensive. Organic products may cost up to 40% more. Production costs are higher as farmers need more workers, and the land output is much less. Marketing and distribution is not efficient because organic food is produced in smaller amounts. Crop illness may happen very often. Besides, organic farming cannot produce enough food for the world\'s population to survive. This could lead to starvation in countries that can produce enough food today.\n\n11. Organic farming _______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"started in the 1950s\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"had a short history\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"has become popular in recent years\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"was promoted by World War II\"}]','C',NULL,'文章开头提到 \'farmers have been returning to organic farming\'（农民们一直在回归有机农业），暗示这是一种近年来的趋势。虽然本页未显示第一段完整内容，但根据上下文逻辑及常识推断，C选项最符合文意。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1161,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Organic Farming】...Animals are fed organically and can eat grass outdoors. Cows, for example, are kept in pastures (草场) and fields...\n\n12. In organic farming, _______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"cows can move around in fields\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"natural enemies of pests are scarce\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"chemicals are used to kill pests\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"machines are used to pull out weeds\"}]','A',NULL,'根据第二段最后一句 \'Cows, for example, are kept in pastures (草场) and fields.\' 可知奶牛被圈养在牧场和田野里，意味着它们可以在田野间活动。B项文中说是依赖害虫的天敌，并未说天敌稀缺；C项文中明确说禁止使用化学杀虫剂；D项文中说 \'They pull out weeds by hand\'（手工拔除杂草）。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1162,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Organic Farming】Organic farming enjoys many advantages. For example, crop rotation can preserve the good qualities of soils. The growing of different crops can keep soils healthy and fertile.\n\n13. The phrase \"crop rotation\" (Para. 3) probably means \"_______\".','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"growing high-yielding crops\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"seasonal growing of crops\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"planting soil-enriching crops\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"regular changing of crops\"}]','D',NULL,'词义猜测题。根据后一句 \'The growing of different crops can keep soils healthy and fertile\'（种植不同的作物可以保持土壤健康和肥沃）可知，crop rotation 指的是轮作，即定期更换种植的作物种类。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1163,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Organic Farming】In the long term, organic farms save energy and protect the environment. It can slow down global warming and reduce the pollution of ground water.\n\n14. One advantage of organic farming is that it is _______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"water-saving\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"labor-saving\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"market-friendly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"environment-friendly\"}]','D',NULL,'细节理解题。第三段末尾明确指出 \'organic farms save energy and protect the environment\'（有机农场节约能源并保护环境），即对环境友好。B项错误，因为第四段提到需要更多工人；C项错误，因为第四段提到市场营销效率不高。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1164,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Health Benefits of Honey with Milk】\nHoney and milk get along well. Since ancient times this mix is known for its amazing health benefits.\n\n❶ Take a glass of honey with milk before you set out for your day in the morning, and you are guaranteed enough energy to get through the morning rush. Milk provides you the proteins required while honey helps you get the energy by breaking down these proteins. No wonder this drink is meant for all ages alike.\n\n❷ Milk is known for providing calcium (钙), which, in right levels, helps in preventing bone diseases as we age. Research has indicated that honey does a good job of carrying nutrients (营养成分) in the food through the blood to various parts of the body. In particular, honey helps in the absorption of calcium, the vital part of milk.\n\n❸ If you ask doctors or your grandmother for a solution to your sleeplessness, you are bound to get the same answer—a glass of warm milk with honey. It is best known to induce sleep. So take it regularly if you have sleeping problems.\n\n❹ Milk and honey not only help in preventing aging by keeping the skin glowing, but also improve your body as a whole as they contain antioxidants (抗氧化物). These help keep the body young and flexible. For a very long time, this has been an open secret in keeping your body look and feel young.\n\n❺ Both milk and honey are known to ward off harmful bacteria in our body, but their combined strength is more effective in achieving this effect. Cough and cold can be prevented by taking this drink regularly. It also aids in digestion and treating bowel disorders.\n\nTask 1: Match the headings with paragraphs.\n16. Paragraph ❶:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for digestion\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a youthful glow\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for stronger bones\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for energy\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a sound sleep\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for antibacterial benefits\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第一段中 \'guaranteed enough energy\' 可知该段主要讲蜂蜜牛奶提供能量。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1165,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','17. Paragraph ❷:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for digestion\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a youthful glow\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for stronger bones\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for energy\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a sound sleep\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for antibacterial benefits\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第二段中 \'preventing bone diseases\' 和 \'absorption of calcium\' 可知该段主要讲强健骨骼。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1166,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','18. Paragraph ❸:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for digestion\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a youthful glow\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for stronger bones\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for energy\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a sound sleep\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for antibacterial benefits\"}]','E',NULL,'根据第三段中 \'solution to your sleeplessness\' 和 \'induce sleep\' 可知该段主要讲助眠。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1167,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','19. Paragraph ❹:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for digestion\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a youthful glow\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for stronger bones\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for energy\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a sound sleep\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for antibacterial benefits\"}]','B',NULL,'根据第四段中 \'keeping the skin glowing\' 和 \'keep the body young\' 可知该段主要讲保持年轻光泽。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1168,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','20. Paragraph ❺:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for digestion\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a youthful glow\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for stronger bones\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for energy\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for a sound sleep\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Honey milk for antibacterial benefits\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第五段中 \'ward off harmful bacteria\' 可知该段主要讲抗菌功效。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1169,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','Task 2: Complete the sentences based on the passage.\n21. Milk is rich ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in proteins and calcium\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"fat and sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cough and cold\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"keep off harmful bacteria\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"drink milk with honey\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"of calcium in milk\"}]','A',NULL,'文中提到 \'Milk provides you the proteins\' 和 \'Milk is known for providing calcium\'。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1170,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','22. Milk and honey help ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in proteins and calcium\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"fat and sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cough and cold\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"keep off harmful bacteria\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"drink milk with honey\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"of calcium in milk\"}]','D',NULL,'文中最后一段提到 \'Both milk and honey are known to ward off harmful bacteria\'，help后接动词原形或名词短语，此处选项D符合语境（ward off = keep off）。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1171,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','23. Honey helps the absorption ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in proteins and calcium\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"fat and sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cough and cold\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"keep off harmful bacteria\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"drink milk with honey\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"of calcium in milk\"}]','F',NULL,'文中第二段提到 \'honey helps in the absorption of calcium\'。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1172,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','24. Your body may bend or move easily if you ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in proteins and calcium\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"fat and sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cough and cold\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"keep off harmful bacteria\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"drink milk with honey\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"of calcium in milk\"}]','E',NULL,'文中第四段提到喝蜂蜜牛奶能保持身体年轻灵活（flexible），即容易弯曲移动。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1173,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','25. Drinking honey milk regularly can prevent ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in proteins and calcium\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"fat and sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cough and cold\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"keep off harmful bacteria\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"drink milk with honey\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"of calcium in milk\"}]','C',NULL,'文中最后一段提到 \'Cough and cold can be prevented by taking this drink regularly\'。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1174,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Insomnia】I just could not fall asleep the other night. I just didn\'t feel sleepy. I can\'t explain why, but it was really annoying.\n\nI got very bored lying in bed, so I decided to read a book. __(26)__ But even when I finished reading, I still didn\'t feel tired. So I listened to some peaceful music. That didn\'t work, either. I have heard people say if you have a warm drink before bedtime it will help you drift off to sleep. So I went downstairs and made myself a cup of tea. __(27)__ Still, I couldn\'t sleep. I was getting very frustrated by this point!\n\nIt felt strange to be awake while everyone else was asleep. __(28)__ In fact, it was a little bit frightening. When you go to sleep, it feels like one day ends and another begins. But if you stay up late, you realize that day and night are just a gentle transition (转变), a cycle which has no end and no beginning. At 4 a.m., I noticed a faint light coming through my curtains. The sun had started to rise!\n\nNormally, I\'m a very heavy sleeper. __(29)__ So on this occasion I considered myself lucky to see a beautiful sunrise. As the sum came up in the east, the birds started to sing their morning songs. I knew I needed to get some rest, but it seemed the harder I tried to force myself asleep, the more difficult it was.\n\nEventually, I just let my mind go free. __(30)__ I listened to the birdsong... and the next thing I knew it was 11 a.m.! I was happy that I had managed to get some sleep! I have never struggled with sleeping before, so this was my first experience of insomnia. Fortunately, I have been sleeping well since then.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The world seemed so quiet.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I stopped forcing myself to sleep.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"After my tea, I got back into bed.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I didn\'t want to wake up my family.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"I thought reading would help me get to sleep.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"I had never been awake at this time in the morning.\"}]','F',NULL,'根据上文 \'At 4 a.m.\' 和下文 \'So on this occasion I considered myself lucky\'，可知作者平时睡得很沉，从未在早上这个时候醒过。选项 F 符合语境。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1175,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · The Importance of Friendship for School-age Children】\nFriends are very important to school-age children\'s healthy (health) development. Research has __(41)__ (show) that children who lack friends can suffer from emotional and mental difficulties later in life. They have also found that children with friends have a __42__ (great) sense of happiness, better self-esteem and fewer problems as they grow up.\nFriendships provide children with more than just fun __43__ (playmate). They help children develop emotionally and __44__ (moral). In interacting with friends, children learn many __45__ (society) skills, such as how to communicate, and how to cooperate. They practice __46__ (control) their emotions and responding to the emotions of others. They develop the __47__ (able) to think through and negotiate different situations in their relationships. Having friends __48__ (affect) children in many ways, even their school __49__ (perform). Children tend to have better attitudes about school and learning when they have friends there. In short, friendships are not just a luxury; they are a __50__ (necessary) for children.','[]','shown',NULL,'根据句意“研究表明……”，此处为现在完成时，have后接过去分词。show的过去分词是shown。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1176,4,NULL,'WRITING','请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇100词左右的英文写作任务。\n\n某英文报社正在举办题为“My Dream Trip”的征文活动，请你根据下述写作要点提交一篇英文短文应征。\n• 你最想去哪里旅游？\n• 为什么你最想去那里？','[]',NULL,'[\"明确写出目的地（如Paris, Beijing等）。\", \"阐述理由（如风景优美、历史悠久、美食丰富等）。\", \"表达期待之情。\"]','',3,'英语二1',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:18:59','2026-10-18 19:18:59'),(1177,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Famous Brands】Why do we always buy certain shoes or clothes that have a famous brand? Why do we have to copy other people? The people we often admire the most are those who have their own styles. They don\'t want to copy someone else\'s.\nBig companies give free products to famous people, such as sportsmen and movie stars. They intend to get people like you to buy their products. When you spend a lot of money on an expensive pair of shoes, they may not suit you. You might enjoy more if you buy something else at the same price! Besides the brand, you may want to know why they are asking that price. The brand may sometimes have nothing to do with the quality of the product.\nIt can be of bad quality and badly made. This makes you think why it has the designer\'s name on it. It\'s very important for designers to use their creative talent to make something beautiful. But today the making of money has become more important. So they just copy other products and their standards fall.\nCreative products should be available to people at a reasonable price. In this way, big companies wouldn\'t be able to dominate (控制) the market and encourage people to spend too much money on their products.\nThey are dominating the market by telling us what to buy. If you go into a toy shop or children\'s clothes shop, you\'ll find the whole section for girls is almost all pink. Because of the domination of big companies, the original arts and crafts are beginning to die out. It would be a real shame if these arts and crafts were to disappear.\n\nWe like the people with their own styles.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第一段第二句 \'The people we often admire the most are those who have their own styles.\'（我们最崇拜的人往往是那些有自己风格的人），admire 意为钦佩、羡慕，即喜欢这类人。题干表述正确。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1178,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Famous Brands】Why do we always buy certain shoes or clothes that have a famous brand? Why do we have to copy other people? The people we often admire the most are those who have their own styles. They don\'t want to copy someone else\'s.\nBig companies give free products to famous people, such as sportsmen and movie stars. They intend to get people like you to buy their products. When you spend a lot of money on an expensive pair of shoes, they may not suit you. You might enjoy more if you buy something else at the same price! Besides the brand, you may want to know why they are asking that price. The brand may sometimes have nothing to do with the quality of the product.\nIt can be of bad quality and badly made. This makes you think why it has the designer\'s name on it. It\'s very important for designers to use their creative talent to make something beautiful. But today the making of money has become more important. So they just copy other products and their standards fall.\nCreative products should be available to people at a reasonable price. In this way, big companies wouldn\'t be able to dominate (控制) the market and encourage people to spend too much money on their products.\nThey are dominating the market by telling us what to buy. If you go into a toy shop or children\'s clothes shop, you\'ll find the whole section for girls is almost all pink. Because of the domination of big companies, the original arts and crafts are beginning to die out. It would be a real shame if these arts and crafts were to disappear.\n\n2. Big companies give famous people free products to attract buyers.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据原文第二段第一句 \'Big companies give free products to famous people... They intend to get people like you to buy their products.\' 可知大公司给名人免费产品是为了吸引买家，表述正确。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1179,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','3. Expensive products often suit people better.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据原文第二段 \'When you spend a lot of money on an expensive pair of shoes, they may not suit you.\' 可知昂贵的产品不一定更适合人们，题目说 \'often suit people better\'（通常更适合）与文意相反。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1180,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','4. Famous brand products are of better quality.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据原文第二段末尾及第三段开头 \'The brand may sometimes have nothing to do with the quality of the product. It can be of bad quality...\' 可知名牌产品的质量不一定更好，甚至可能很差。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1181,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','5. Creativity is important in making good products.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据原文第三段 \'It\'s very important for designers to use their creative talent to make something beautiful.\' 可知创造力对于制造好产品很重要。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1182,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','6. Famous designers work overtime.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到了设计师和创造力，但没有提及著名设计师是否加班工作。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1183,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','7. Young people like creative products.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到孩子们的衣服区全是粉色，以及大公司控制市场，但并未明确说明年轻人喜欢有创意的产品这一观点。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1184,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','8. Big companies price their products reasonably.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据原文第四段 \'Creative products should be available to people at a reasonable price. In this way, big companies wouldn\'t be able to... encourage people to spend too much money...\' 暗示大公司目前并没有以合理的价格销售，而是鼓励人们花太多钱。',2,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1185,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','9. Mothers prefer to shop for children\'s clothes.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到了去玩具店或童装店看到的情况，但没有提及母亲购物偏好的信息。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1186,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','10. The domination of big companies does harm to creativity.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据原文最后一段 \'Because of the domination of big companies, the original arts and crafts are beginning to die out.\' 可知大公司的统治对原创艺术和工艺（即创造力的一种体现）造成了伤害。',2,'英语二1',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1187,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Self-esteem (自尊) and Body Image】Self-esteem is all about what people think of themselves. It is important because feeling good about yourself can affect how you act. People who have high self-esteem will make friends easily. They are more in control of their behavior, and will enjoy life more.\n\nSome teenagers struggle with their self-esteem when they grow into adults because the body goes through many changes. Along with the changes comes a natural desire to feel accepted. What\'s more, they can\'t help but compare themselves with others. They may compare themselves with the people around them or with actors and other famous people they see on TV, in movies, or in magazines.\n\nThe physical changes can affect how both girls and boys feel about themselves. Some girls may feel uncomfortable about their growing bodies. Others may wish that they were developing faster. Girls may feel like being thin but boys may feel like they don\'t look big enough.\n\nIt\'s not just body development that affects self-esteem. Many other factors can affect a person\'s body image too. Family life, for example, can sometimes influence self-esteem. Some parents spend more time criticizing their kids and the way they look than praising them. This can reduce kids\' ability to develop good self-esteem. Also their classmates and peers may tease them about the way they look. These sometimes can affect their self-esteem.\n\nIf there are things about yourself that you want to change and you can change, do this by making goals for yourself. If there are things that you can\'t change, recognize that your body is your own. It\'s no one\'s business but your own what your body is like. Actually, to be happy with yourself, all you need to do is to change the way you see your body.\n\n11. People with high self-esteem often ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"control others\' behavior\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"think highly of others\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"have lots of friends\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"work very hard\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第一段第三句 \'People who have high self-esteem will make friends easily.\' 可知，自尊心强的人容易交朋友，即有很多朋友。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1188,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Self-esteem (自尊) and Body Image】(同上)\n\n12. Some teenagers struggle with their self-esteem because ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"their teachers don\'t like them\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"their bodies have changed a lot\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"they cannot accept famous people\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"they need more time to watch TV\"}]','B',NULL,'根据第二段第一句 \'Some teenagers struggle with their self-esteem when they grow into adults because the body goes through many changes.\' 可知，青少年因为身体发生很多变化而在此方面挣扎。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1189,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Self-esteem (自尊) and Body Image】(同上)\n\n13. The word \"tease\" (Line 5, Para. 4) most probably means ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"laugh at\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"talk about\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"argue with\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"look at\"}]','A',NULL,'根据上下文，前文提到父母批评孩子外貌会降低自尊心，后文说同学和同龄人也会 \'tease\' 他们的外貌，这同样会影响自尊心。\'tease\' 意为取笑、戏弄，与 \'laugh at\'（嘲笑）意思最接近。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1190,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Self-esteem (自尊) and Body Image】(同上)\n\n14. To help kids develop good self-esteem, parents should ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"compare them with others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"make goals for them\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"criticize their peers\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"praise them\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第四段第二、三句 \'Family life... can sometimes influence self-esteem. Some parents spend more time criticizing their kids... than praising them. This can reduce kids\' ability to develop good self-esteem.\' 反之，为了帮助孩子建立良好的自尊心，父母应该多表扬（praise）他们。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1191,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Self-esteem (自尊) and Body Image】(同上)\n\n15. To be happy with yourself you should ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"do business\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"love your body\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"find new friends\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"change your behavior\"}]','B',NULL,'根据最后一段 \'Actually, to be happy with yourself, all you need to do is to change the way you see your body.\' 以及前文 \'recognize that your body is your own\'，要对自己感到满意/快乐，需要改变看待身体的方式，即接纳并爱护自己的身体。选项 B \'love your body\' 符合文意。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1192,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❶: ...are too difficult for them to deal with. While they may not talk about their troubles, they do want their parents to reach out and help them.\n\nTask 1\n16. Paragraph ❶:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help your child deal with stress\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Show your concern and care\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Be patient with your child\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Stories help children\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Listen to your child\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Children have stress\"}]','F',NULL,'根据上下文逻辑，第一段通常引入话题。虽然本段文字不全，但结合后文“Children deal with stress...”以及选项内容，第一段主旨应为指出孩子也有压力（Children have stress）。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1193,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❷: Children deal with stress in both healthy and unhealthy ways. As a parent, you can\'t protect your children from stress, but you can help them develop healthy ways to cope with stress and solve everyday problems. By doing so, you not only help your children handle their current stresses, but also prepare them to deal with future stresses. Here are a few tips for you.\n\nTask 1\n17. Paragraph ❷:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help your child deal with stress\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Show your concern and care\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Be patient with your child\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Stories help children\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Listen to your child\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Children have stress\"}]','A',NULL,'该段主要讲述父母无法保护孩子免受压力，但可以帮助孩子发展应对压力的健康方式（help them develop healthy ways...），即帮助孩子处理压力。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1194,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❸: When you notice that something is upsetting your child, you need to tell your child about it. If you can, name the feeling you think your child is experiencing. This shouldn\'t sound like blame. It\'s just a casual observation, and you\'re interested in hearing more about your child\'s concern. Be sympathetic and show that you care and want to understand.\n\nTask 1\n18. Paragraph ❸:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help your child deal with stress\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Show your concern and care\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Be patient with your child\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Stories help children\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Listen to your child\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Children have stress\"}]','B',NULL,'该段最后一句明确提到“show that you care”（表现出你的关心），且整段都在讲要同情、理解孩子的感受，对应选项 B。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1195,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❹: Also ask your child to tell you what\'s wrong. Listen attentively and calmly—with interest, patience, openness, and caring. Don\'t hurry to make judgements. Do not blame or criticize your child for what he or she has done. The idea is to listen to your child\'s concerns and feelings. Try to get the whole story by patiently asking questions. Take your time. And let your child take his or her time, too.\n\nTask 1\n19. Paragraph ❹:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help your child deal with stress\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Show your concern and care\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Be patient with your child\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Stories help children\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Listen to your child\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Children have stress\"}]','E',NULL,'该段核心动词是“Listen”，多次出现“ask your child to tell you”、“Listen attentively”、“listen to your child\'s concerns”，对应选项 E。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1196,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❺: Remember to be patient. As a parent, it hurts to see your child unhappy or stressed. But you should not try to solve every problem for your child. Instead, try to help your child grow into a good problem-solver—a child who knows how to deal with life\'s ups and downs, express feelings in words, calm down when needed, and never give in to difficulties.\n\nTask 1\n20. Paragraph ❺:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help your child deal with stress\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Show your concern and care\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Be patient with your child\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Stories help children\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Listen to your child\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Children have stress\"}]','C',NULL,'该段首句即为“Remember to be patient.”（记住要有耐心），对应选项 C。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1197,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】\n\nTask 2\n21. Children can meet pressures ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in trouble\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in healthy ways\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to forget their problems\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"what he/she has done\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"from school and their social life\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to solve problems themselves\"}]','E',NULL,'根据常识及文章背景（虽未显示第一段全文，但此类文章通常提及压力来源），孩子们面临的压力来自学校和社会生活。选项 E 符合语境。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1198,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❷: Children deal with stress in both healthy and unhealthy ways...\n\nTask 2\n22. Parents can help their children cope with stress ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in trouble\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in healthy ways\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to forget their problems\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"what he/she has done\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"from school and their social life\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to solve problems themselves\"}]','B',NULL,'根据第二段“you can help them develop healthy ways to cope with stress”，父母可以帮助孩子以健康的方式应对压力。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1199,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❸: When you notice that something is upsetting your child...\n\nTask 2\n23. Talk to your child when he/she is ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in trouble\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in healthy ways\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to forget their problems\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"what he/she has done\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"from school and their social life\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to solve problems themselves\"}]','A',NULL,'根据第三段“When you notice that something is upsetting your child”，当孩子遇到麻烦或心烦意乱时（in trouble/upsetting），应该与其交谈。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1200,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❹: Do not blame or criticize your child for what he or she has done.\n\nTask 2\n24. Don\'t blame your child for ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in trouble\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in healthy ways\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to forget their problems\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"what he/she has done\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"from school and their social life\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to solve problems themselves\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第四段原句“Do not blame or criticize your child for what he or she has done”，直接对应选项 D。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1201,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Children and Stress】Paragraph ❺: ...try to help your child grow into a good problem-solver...\n\nTask 2\n25. Parents should teach their children ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in trouble\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in healthy ways\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to forget their problems\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"what he/she has done\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"from school and their social life\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to solve problems themselves\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第五段“help your child grow into a good problem-solver”，即教导孩子自己解决问题（to solve problems themselves）。',2,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1202,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · The Coyote】The coyote is a relative of the dog and the wolf. Like its relatives, it mostly feeds on other animals. It will, however, eat a wide variety of foods, including insects, fruits and vegetables.\nCoyotes are found throughout most of North America, from Mexico and Central America to Canada and Alaska. The color of its coat depends on where it lives. __(26)__\nLike the wolf, coyotes live in groups, or packs. The coyote pack is usually smaller than a wolf pack. _27_ The pack will often divide into pairs to hunt. Female coyotes give birth to baby coyotes once a year. Over half of the babies will die before they reach adulthood. Male babies usually leave the pack to find their own territory. _28_\nWolves and coyotes compete for the same animals for food. Since the coyote is smaller than the wolf, wolves will usually drive the coyote out of any shared living areas.\nThe coyote adapts easily to new areas. Unlike the wolf, the coyote\'s living area increased when more and more people settled across North America. _29_ Once the New England settlers eliminated wolves, the coyote moved in. Scientists who have studied the coyote believe it is better than the wolf at living in human areas.\n_30_ They find enough supply of food in these areas, since coyotes are willing to eat garbage, rodents (such as rabbits and mice) and even small pets. Scientists estimate that as many as 2,000 coyotes may be living in the Chicago area.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Female babies stay with the parent\'s pack.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The coyote is not an endangered species.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Coyotes are now found in most large cities.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"All members of the pack are usually related.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Mountain coyotes are darker than those living in the desert.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"For example, the coyote was not native to New England.\"}]','E',NULL,'前一句提到毛色取决于居住地，选项 E 举例说明山区的郊狼比沙漠里的颜色深，符合语境。',1,'英语二1',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1203,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · Slavery in the United States】\nIn most parts of the United States in the early 1800s, blacks had no rights at all. They did not have the right to vote. It was against the __(31)__ for them to go to school with whites. In some states, it was even __32__ for them to learn to read and write. Free people had the right to come and go as they __33__, but slaves had to have a pass, or paper, from their __34__ in order to leave the master\'s land. Slaves were often __35__ from their families when they were sold. They had to work very __36__ hours, but were not paid. If they did not do as they were told, they could be beaten. If they tried to escape, they were hunted down with dogs, and could be tortured or even __37__ when caught.\nUntil about 1800, there were slaves in __38__ every state in the United States. But slaves were not a big part of the Northern way of __39__. Northern factories hired workers and did not use slaves. By 1850, all Northern states had made slavery illegal.\nIn the Southern states, however, most of the field workers were slaves; one out of every four families __40__ slaves. These people were often rich and had large farms.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"seldom\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"master\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"separated\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"illegal\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"killed\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"life\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"owned\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"law\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"long\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"almost\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"liked\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"played\"}]','H',NULL,'根据句意“他们和白人一起上学是违反法律的”，against the law 为固定搭配。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1204,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Rubbish: Easy to Produce, but Hard to Get Rid of】\nWe produce a lot of rubbish. There is no question about it. The amount of rubbish we throw away is surprising (surprise). Scientists report that Americans produce about five __(41)__ (pound) of rubbish per person every day. Forty years ago, each person __42__ (produce) only half of it each day. There are __43__ (near) 300 million people in the US.','[]','pounds',NULL,'five 后面接名词复数形式。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1205,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Rubbish: Easy to Produce, but Hard to Get Rid of】You do the math. How much rubbish do we produce every day?\nIn __(44)__ (add) to the amount of rubbish we produce, how we get rid of it is another problem. The plastic bags that we place outside of our homes need to be __(45)__ (carry) away every week. These bags are not __(46)__ (friend) to the environment at all.\nNobody is sure how long a plastic bag takes to totally break down, because we\'ve only been __(47)__ (use) plastic as a business for about 90 years. It is __(48)__ (believe), however, that it may take 100 years for a plastic bag to completely break down. I am sure that you will feel __(49)__ (happy) to think that a plastic bag can live longer than the __(50)__ (major) of people on earth.','[]','addition',NULL,'in addition to 为固定搭配，意为“除……之外”。',1,'英语二1',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1206,4,NULL,'WRITING','假设你的外国朋友 John 想学习汉语，征求你的意见。请给他写一封电子邮件，内容包括：\n• 支持他学汉语；\n• 给出学习建议。\n请以 Li Ke 署名。','[]',NULL,'[\"邮件格式正确（称呼、正文、落款）\", \"明确表达对John学习汉语的支持\", \"提出具体的学习建议（如看中文电影、交中国朋友、使用APP等）\", \"语言通顺，字数符合要求\"]','',3,'英语二1',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:19:00','2026-10-18 19:19:00'),(1207,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Who Is James Bond?】The latest Bond film is an enormous box-office (票房) hit. But who is James Bond? Where does he come from? Author Ian Fleming, the creator of James Bond, told us something about the origins of the world\'s most famous secret agent.\n\nIn the first Bond novel, Ian Fleming told us that James Bond was the son of a Scottish father and an Asian mother. But perhaps this was not really true. The title of the 19th Bond film, \"The World Is Not Enough,\" was based on the Latin motto of the Bond family, which is mentioned in one of the early novels. However, it now appears that the motto is not that of the Scottish Bonds, but that of a different Bond family, who came from England. So perhaps Bond is English, not Scottish.\n\nBond went to Eton College, the same school as his creator Ian Fleming. This is a school where young people learn how to move in high society, like Bond does so well.\n\nAfter leaving school, Bond did not go to university. He joined the British Secret Service. He soon got promoted to the top. From then on he was 007, \"licensed to kill\", and so began a career which would take him to all the corners of the earth.\n\nIn the early days, Bond\'s role was quite clear. He was working for the West. His main enemies were men from the KGB and other dangerous organizations. Since the end of the Cold War, the role of the Service has changed, and Bond\'s job profile has changed with it. Now his main enemies are the big bosses of organized crime and international terrorism.\n\nUnlike the Cold War, organized crime is unlikely to come to an end. We can therefore be sure that James Bond, the best-known English fictional hero of the 20th century, has many more adventures ahead of him.\n\n1. The new Bond film made much money for its producer.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第一段第一句 \'The latest Bond film is an enormous box-office (票房) hit.\'（最新的邦德电影在票房上取得了巨大的成功），可知该说法正确。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1208,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Who Is James Bond?】The latest Bond film is an enormous box-office (票房) hit. But who is James Bond? Where does he come from? Author Ian Fleming, the creator of James Bond, told us something about the origins of the world\'s most famous secret agent.\n\nIn the first Bond novel, Ian Fleming told us that James Bond was the son of a Scottish father and an Asian mother. But perhaps this was not really true. The title of the 19th Bond film, \"The World Is Not Enough,\" was based on the Latin motto of the Bond family, which is mentioned in one of the early novels. However, it now appears that the motto is not that of the Scottish Bonds, but that of a different Bond family, who came from England. So perhaps Bond is English, not Scottish.\n\nBond went to Eton College, the same school as his creator Ian Fleming. This is a school where young people learn how to move in high society, like Bond does so well.\n\nAfter leaving school, Bond did not go to university. He joined the British Secret Service. He soon got promoted to the top. From then on he was 007, \"licensed to kill\", and so began a career which would take him to all the corners of the earth.\n\nIn the early days, Bond\'s role was quite clear. He was working for the West. His main enemies were men from the KGB and other dangerous organizations. Since the end of the Cold War, the role of the Service has changed, and Bond\'s job profile has changed with it. Now his main enemies are the big bosses of organized crime and international terrorism.\n\nUnlike the Cold War, organized crime is unlikely to come to an end. We can therefore be sure that James Bond, the best-known English fictional hero of the 20th century, has many more adventures ahead of him.\n\n2. Ian Fleming directed the latest film about James Bond.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第一段第三句 \'Author Ian Fleming, the creator of James Bond...\'，Ian Fleming 是詹姆斯·邦德的作者和创造者，而不是导演。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1209,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Who Is James Bond?】The latest Bond film is an enormous box-office (票房) hit. But who is James Bond? Where does he come from? Author Ian Fleming, the creator of James Bond, told us something about the origins of the world\'s most famous secret agent.\n\nIn the first Bond novel, Ian Fleming told us that James Bond was the son of a Scottish father and an Asian