be sure that James Bond, the best-known English fictional hero of the 20th century, has many more adventures ahead of him.\n\n9. We can expect more adventurous stories about Bond.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章最后一段 \'We can therefore be sure that James Bond... has many more adventures ahead of him.\'，我们可以确信邦德还有更多的冒险故事。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1216,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Who Is James Bond?】The latest Bond film is an enormous box-office (票房) hit. But who is James Bond? Where does he come from? Author Ian Fleming, the creator of James Bond, told us something about the origins of the world\'s most famous secret agent.\n\nIn the first Bond novel, Ian Fleming told us that James Bond was the son of a Scottish father and an Asian mother. But perhaps this was not really true. The title of the 19th Bond film, \"The World Is Not Enough,\" was based on the Latin motto of the Bond family, which is mentioned in one of the early novels. However, it now appears that the motto is not that of the Scottish Bonds, but that of a different Bond family, who came from England. So perhaps Bond is English, not Scottish.\n\nBond went to Eton College, the same school as his creator Ian Fleming. This is a school where young people learn how to move in high society, like Bond does so well.\n\nAfter leaving school, Bond did not go to university. He joined the British Secret Service. He soon got promoted to the top. From then on he was 007, \"licensed to kill\", and so began a career which would take him to all the corners of the earth.\n\nIn the early days, Bond\'s role was quite clear. He was working for the West. His main enemies were men from the KGB and other dangerous organizations. Since the end of the Cold War, the role of the Service has changed, and Bond\'s job profile has changed with it. Now his main enemies are the big bosses of organized crime and international terrorism.\n\nUnlike the Cold War, organized crime is unlikely to come to an end. We can therefore be sure that James Bond, the best-known English fictional hero of the 20th century, has many more adventures ahead of him.\n\n10. This text tells about the personality of James Bond.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'通读全文，文章主要介绍了詹姆斯·邦德的出身背景、教育经历、职业变化等，并没有重点描写他的性格特征（personality）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1217,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Body Language and Anxiety】\nin the moment.\n\nIn times of strong anxiety, people will twist their hands to calm themselves. Ulrich said it is a reaction people often have when they are in front of an audience or nervous. \"It\'s a comfort for them that they\'ll get through it,\" said Ulrich. He relates that gesture to a parent trying to calm a child.\n\nMost athletes react to victories or defeats with specific behaviors. A 2008 study examined pictures of judo (柔道) competitors during the 2008 Olympic Games. They were from different countries, but they showed similar behaviors when they won a match. The winners would throw their head back or raise their hands in triumph. Ulrich said these victory behaviors are a way winners \"explode\" out and take up more space.\n\nHowever, if an athlete suffers a loss, he will act in a way that makes him physically smaller, such as hanging his head. \"When you lose, you want to disappear,\" said Ulrich. The study also found that the judo competitors had the same behavior when they lost.\n\n11. People put their hands over their mouth to ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"avoid a danger\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"gain self-comfort\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"hide their shock\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"show their anxiety\"}]','B',NULL,'根据文中提到的 \'It\'s a comfort for them...\' 以及将手势比作父母安抚孩子，可知这是一种自我安慰的行为。虽然本段主要讲扭手，但此类题目通常考察对文章主旨（肢体语言用于自我安抚）的理解。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1218,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Body Language and Anxiety】\nin the moment.\n\nIn times of strong anxiety, people will twist their hands to calm themselves. Ulrich said it is a reaction people often have when they are in front of an audience or nervous. \"It\'s a comfort for them that they\'ll get through it,\" said Ulrich. He relates that gesture to a parent trying to calm a child.\n\nMost athletes react to victories or defeats with specific behaviors. A 2008 study examined pictures of judo (柔道) competitors during the 2008 Olympic Games. They were from different countries, but they showed similar behaviors when they won a match. The winners would throw their head back or raise their hands in triumph. Ulrich said these victory behaviors are a way winners \"explode\" out and take up more space.\n\nHowever, if an athlete suffers a loss, he will act in a way that makes him physically smaller, such as hanging his head. \"When you lose, you want to disappear,\" said Ulrich. The study also found that the judo competitors had the same behavior when they lost.\n\n12. People tend to twist their hands when they are ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"depressed\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"angry\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"shocked\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"nervous\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第一段第二句 \'Ulrich said it is a reaction people often have when they are in front of an audience or nervous.\' 可知，人们在紧张时会扭手。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1219,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Body Language and Anxiety】\nin the moment.\n\nIn times of strong anxiety, people will twist their hands to calm themselves. Ulrich said it is a reaction people often have when they are in front of an audience or nervous. \"It\'s a comfort for them that they\'ll get through it,\" said Ulrich. He relates that gesture to a parent trying to calm a child.\n\nMost athletes react to victories or defeats with specific behaviors. A 2008 study examined pictures of judo (柔道) competitors during the 2008 Olympic Games. They were from different countries, but they showed similar behaviors when they won a match. The winners would throw their head back or raise their hands in triumph. Ulrich said these victory behaviors are a way winners \"explode\" out and take up more space.\n\nHowever, if an athlete suffers a loss, he will act in a way that makes him physically smaller, such as hanging his head. \"When you lose, you want to disappear,\" said Ulrich. The study also found that the judo competitors had the same behavior when they lost.\n\n13. In Paragraph 4, \"that gesture\" refers to ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"shaking one\'s hands\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"covering one\'s face\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"twisting one\'s hands\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"rubbing one\'s face\"}]','C',NULL,'根据上下文逻辑，\'He relates that gesture to a parent trying to calm a child\' 中的 \'that gesture\' 指代前文提到的 \'twist their hands\'（扭手）。注意：虽然题干说Paragraph 4，但根据可见文本，该句位于第一段末尾或紧接其后的段落中，指代明确为扭手。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1220,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Body Language and Anxiety】\nin the moment.\n\nIn times of strong anxiety, people will twist their hands to calm themselves. Ulrich said it is a reaction people often have when they are in front of an audience or nervous. \"It\'s a comfort for them that they\'ll get through it,\" said Ulrich. He relates that gesture to a parent trying to calm a child.\n\nMost athletes react to victories or defeats with specific behaviors. A 2008 study examined pictures of judo (柔道) competitors during the 2008 Olympic Games. They were from different countries, but they showed similar behaviors when they won a match. The winners would throw their head back or raise their hands in triumph. Ulrich said these victory behaviors are a way winners \"explode\" out and take up more space.\n\nHowever, if an athlete suffers a loss, he will act in a way that makes him physically smaller, such as hanging his head. \"When you lose, you want to disappear,\" said Ulrich. The study also found that the judo competitors had the same behavior when they lost.\n\n14. Judo winners often act in a way that makes them ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"occupy more space\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"appear physically smaller\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"obtain more respect\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"become more competitive\"}]','A',NULL,'根据第二段最后一句 \'Ulrich said these victory behaviors are a way winners \"explode\" out and take up more space.\' 可知获胜者会占据更多空间。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1221,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Body Language and Anxiety】\nin the moment.\n\nIn times of strong anxiety, people will twist their hands to calm themselves. Ulrich said it is a reaction people often have when they are in front of an audience or nervous. \"It\'s a comfort for them that they\'ll get through it,\" said Ulrich. He relates that gesture to a parent trying to calm a child.\n\nMost athletes react to victories or defeats with specific behaviors. A 2008 study examined pictures of judo (柔道) competitors during the 2008 Olympic Games. They were from different countries, but they showed similar behaviors when they won a match. The winners would throw their head back or raise their hands in triumph. Ulrich said these victory behaviors are a way winners \"explode\" out and take up more space.\n\nHowever, if an athlete suffers a loss, he will act in a way that makes him physically smaller, such as hanging his head. \"When you lose, you want to disappear,\" said Ulrich. The study also found that the judo competitors had the same behavior when they lost.\n\n15. The judo losers would ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"raise their arms\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"lower their heads\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"beat their chests\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"sit on their knees\"}]','B',NULL,'根据第三段第一句 \'However, if an athlete suffers a loss, he will act in a way that makes him physically smaller, such as hanging his head.\' 可知失败者会垂头（hanging his head = lower their heads）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1222,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Little Steps, Big Reward】\nParagraph 1: More than 145 million Americans take walking as part of their exercise, according to a recent report. That\'s 15 million more people walking than last year. Many places in America have reported an increase in walking. But most of the walkers are found in big cities like New York.\n\n16. Paragraph ①:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The key to walking is getting started.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Walking is the first step to making changes.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The advantage of walking is its simplicity.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Walking is a great way for health improvement\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"More Americans take up walking than before.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Modern lifestyle affects our health negatively.\"}]','E',NULL,'第一段主要讲述了美国人步行锻炼的人数增加了，比以前更多。对应选项 E。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1223,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Little Steps, Big Reward】\nParagraph 2: Despite the increase in walking, only about 30% of Americans say they have at least 3 hours to take exercise a week. Our society has been conditioned to be inactive. People rely on modern conveniences and become lazy. The inactive lifestyle has a negative aspect. We are more likely to be in poor health like overweight, which will threaten our life span. That\'s where walking comes in.\n\n17. Paragraph ②:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The key to walking is getting started.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Walking is the first step to making changes.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The advantage of walking is its simplicity.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Walking is a great way for health improvement\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"More Americans take up walking than before.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Modern lifestyle affects our health negatively.\"}]','F',NULL,'第二段指出不活跃的生活方式（现代便利导致）对健康有负面影响。对应选项 F。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1224,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Little Steps, Big Reward】\nParagraph 3: Walking is the best way to improve our health. Just 30 minutes of regular quick walking can help lose weight. At the same time, it can help lower the risk of heart disease and some cancers, and improve our blood pressure. If 30 minutes is too much, we may divide it into three 10-minute parts during the day. Most of us can find 10 minutes if we really try.\n\n18. Paragraph ③:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The key to walking is getting started.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Walking is the first step to making changes.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The advantage of walking is its simplicity.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Walking is a great way for health improvement\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"More Americans take up walking than before.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Modern lifestyle affects our health negatively.\"}]','D',NULL,'第三段首句即主题句：散步是改善健康的最佳方式。对应选项 D。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1225,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Little Steps, Big Reward】\nParagraph 4: Walking requires only a pair of shoes and suits any schedules. Keep a pair of sport shoes at work. If you have a few minutes of free time, make use of them to take a quick walk. Even if you go to a health club several times a week, you can still look for ways to be active while at work. It may be walking downstairs for a direct talk rather than sending an email.\n\n19. Paragraph ④:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The key to walking is getting started.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Walking is the first step to making changes.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The advantage of walking is its simplicity.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Walking is a great way for health improvement\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"More Americans take up walking than before.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Modern lifestyle affects our health negatively.\"}]','C',NULL,'第四段提到散步只需要一双鞋，适合任何日程，强调其简单性。对应选项 C。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1226,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Little Steps, Big Reward】\nParagraph 5: Small efforts can make a big difference. But the hardest part for us is getting started. It\'s usually like this. When people get to a comfort level of walking for 10 minutes, they might think about trying 11 minutes. That first step is really worthy.\n\n20. Paragraph ⑤:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The key to walking is getting started.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Walking is the first step to making changes.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The advantage of walking is its simplicity.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Walking is a great way for health improvement\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"More Americans take up walking than before.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Modern lifestyle affects our health negatively.\"}]','A',NULL,'第五段指出最难的部分是开始（getting started），第一步很有价值。对应选项 A。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1227,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','Reports say that the walkers are mostly from __(21)__.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"we divide a 30-minute walk into 3 parts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"our inactiveness\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"we may like to try a longer one\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"big cities in America\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"a daily 30- minute quick walk\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a face-to-face talk\"}]','D',NULL,'根据文章第一段最后一句 \'But most of the walkers are found in big cities like New York.\' 可知答案选 D。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1228,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','Many diseases are largely caused by __(22)__.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"we divide a 30-minute walk into 3 parts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"our inactiveness\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"we may like to try a longer one\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"big cities in America\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"a daily 30- minute quick walk\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a face-to-face talk\"}]','B',NULL,'根据文章第二段 \'Our society has been conditioned to be inactive... The inactive lifestyle has a negative aspect. We are more likely to be in poor health...\' 可知疾病主要由不活跃引起。答案选 B。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1229,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','We can keep healthy by taking __(23)__.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"we divide a 30-minute walk into 3 parts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"our inactiveness\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"we may like to try a longer one\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"big cities in America\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"a daily 30- minute quick walk\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a face-to-face talk\"}]','E',NULL,'根据文章第三段 \'Just 30 minutes of regular quick walking can help lose weight... improve our blood pressure\' 可知每天快走30分钟能保持健康。答案选 E。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1230,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','We can take a quick walk downstairs for __(24)__.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"we divide a 30-minute walk into 3 parts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"our inactiveness\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"we may like to try a longer one\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"big cities in America\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"a daily 30- minute quick walk\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a face-to-face talk\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第四段最后一句 \'It may be walking downstairs for a direct talk rather than sending an email.\' 可知是为了面对面交谈。答案选 F。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1231,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','When feeling good after a 10-minute walk, __(25)__.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"we divide a 30-minute walk into 3 parts\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"our inactiveness\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"we may like to try a longer one\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"big cities in America\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"a daily 30- minute quick walk\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a face-to-face talk\"}]','C',NULL,'根据文章最后一段 \'When people get to a comfort level of walking for 10 minutes, they might think about trying 11 minutes.\' 可知可能会尝试更长时间。答案选 C。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1232,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · North Africa】Africa is the second largest continent on Earth. It is about 8,000 kilometers long from north to south. It can be divided into three major regions: northern Africa, central Africa, and southern Africa. __(26)__\n\nAfrica is separated from Europe by the Mediterranean Sea (地中海). It is connected to Asia in the east. For this reason, it has been easy for people from Europe, Asia and other areas to come to North Africa. __27__\n\nMost of North Africa is covered by the Sahara Desert. __28__ There is little rainfall here. The few people who live in the desert live in oases (绿洲). The valley of the Nile River forms one of the oases that stretch across the desert in the east.\n\nMany North African nations have a very important resource. They have large deposits of petroleum. __29__ In return, these nations receive a lot of money. They are spending some of this money to make life better for their people.\n\nEgypt is an important nation in North Africa. __30__ It has served as a bridge between Africa and Asia. People from many nations have passed through Egypt. Today, it controls the Suez Canal. The canal connects the Mediterranean Sea and the Red Sea. It is important for ships traveling between nations in Europe and Asia.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It has always been a great barrier to people traveling south.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"This oil is shipped to many parts of the world,\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Each region has its special geography and history.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Asia is much larger than Europe.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"All these people have left their influence there.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"About 40 million people live there today.\"}]','C',NULL,'前一句提到非洲分为三个主要区域，选项 C“每个地区都有独特的地理和历史”承接上文，符合逻辑。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1233,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · Learning from Mistakes】Lots of people don\'t dare to make mistakes. They fear that they will be blamed by others or lose their money and __(31)__. Therefore, they are under a lot of stress. But risks are unavoidable and they do __32__ the way towards success. Have you ever heard of someone who achieves success without making any mistakes?\n\nSo it is __33__ that making mistakes in your effort to realize your __34__ is considered a must. You shouldn\'t worry about making mistakes as you may get a lot of __35__ from them. By making mistakes you can __36__ between the correct and the __37__ things you did. Anthony D\'Angelo said, \"In order to succeed you must fail, so that you know what to do the next time.\" Robert Stevenson even went to the __38__ as to say, \"Our business in life is not to succeed, but to continue to __39__ in good spirits.\"\n\nYou needn\'t worry about anything as long as you keep on going by __40__ learning from your mistakes and trying even harder.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"extreme\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"discover\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"distinguish\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"advantages\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"fail\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"belongings\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"recently\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"natural\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"pave\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"incorrect\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"wisely\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"dreams\"}]','F',NULL,'根据句意“害怕被责备或失去金钱和财物”，此处应填名词 belongings。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1234,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Interlaken, Switzerland】The sound of cow bells ringing across Interlaken\'s grassland is comforting (comfort). Climbing up the nearby mountains is also __(41)__ (enjoy). So is skiing down them. The town of Interlaken is __42__ (locate) in a beautiful setting between two lakes. It is also close to the __43__ (mountain) villages. The outdoor possibilities are __44__ (end) around Interlaken in summer and winter. They range from sailing, skiing, to climbing or just __45__ (relax) in a','[]','enjoyable',NULL,'be动词后接形容词作表语，enjoy的形容词形式为enjoyable。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1235,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Interlaken, Switzerland】The sound of cow bells ringing across Interlaken\'s grassland is comforting (comfort). Climbing up the nearby mountains is also __41__ (enjoy). So is skiing down them. The town of Interlaken is __42__ (locate) in a beautiful setting between two lakes. It is also close to the __43__ (mountain) villages. The outdoor possibilities are __44__ (end) around Interlaken in summer and winter. They range from sailing, skiing, to climbing or just __45__ (relax) in a pool. People can enjoy boating in the summer. They can also take __(46)__ (please) in skiing in the winter. This place is a perfect choice for people if they like ice climbing or __47__ (roll) down a hill inside a ball. It meets __48__ (near) everyone\'s needs.\n\nForeigners are not allowed to buy __49__ (house) in Interlaken. But they can buy one in nearby villages. Many __50__ (retire) people consider Interlaken a great place to settle around.','[]','pleasure',NULL,'take pleasure in doing sth. 是固定搭配，意为“以……为乐”，此处需填名词形式。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1236,4,NULL,'WRITING','某英语学习报征集一篇题为“My Favorite Chinese Festival”的稿件。请就此题目写一篇英文短文应征，内容包括：\n• 你最喜欢的中国节日是什么？\n• 你为什么喜欢这个节日？','[]',NULL,'[\"明确写出最喜欢的中国节日名称（如Spring Festival, Mid-Autumn Festival等）。\", \"阐述喜欢该节日的原因（如家庭团聚、传统美食、文化活动等）。\", \"语言流畅，结构清晰，字数在100词左右。\"]','',2,'英语二2',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1237,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Animals in the City】Recently, there have been many reports in newspapers and on TV about big animals coming into towns and cities. What happens when big animals come into our cities? Is it a good thing or is it dangerous for us and the animals?\n\nWild animals usually come into cities to look for food. In Cape Town, South Africa, baboons (狒狒) sometimes come into the suburbs. They eat fruit from gardens and go into people\'s kitchens! Baboons are strong animals and sometimes they scare children and fight with pet dogs. Many people do not like them, but the city can be dangerous for baboons too. Sometimes, baboons are hurt in car accidents. The city council in Cape Town has a team of Baboon Monitors. Their job is to find baboons in the city and take them back to the countryside. The problem is that a lot of baboons will come back to the city to find food again.\n\nIn Berlin Germany, groups of wild pigs sometimes come into the city to look for food. They eat flowers and plants and dig in gardens and parks in the city. They also walk in the street and cause traffic accidents. Some city residents like the pigs and give them food. But the city council is worried about the traffic accidents. They have told people to stop giving the pigs food and have put up fences to stop the pigs from coming into the city.\n\nIn Moscow, Russia, there are 35,000 wild dogs. They live in parks, empty houses, markets and train stations. Some of the dogs were pets that people did not want, so they left them on the streets. Others were born on the streets and have always lived there. A lot of people like them and are used to seeing them on the streets. They give the dogs food and water. They even build small huts for the dogs to live in during the very cold winter.\n\nMany news reports concern big animals in the city.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文章第一段提到 \'there have been many reports in newspapers and on TV about big animals coming into towns and cities\'，与题干表述一致。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1238,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Wild animals often come into cities for the winter.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文章第二段开头明确指出 \'Wild animals usually come into cities to look for food\'（寻找食物），而不是为了过冬。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1239,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','The food in kitchens can be bad for baboons.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章提到狒狒会进厨房吃东西 (\'go into people\'s kitchens\')，但没有提及厨房里的食物对它们是否有害。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1240,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Cape Town is a safe place for baboons.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文章第二段提到 \'the city can be dangerous for baboons too\' 以及它们会在车祸中受伤，说明开普敦对狒狒来说并不安全。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1241,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Many baboons will return after being sent away from the city.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文章第二段末尾提到 \'a lot of baboons will come back to the city to find food again\'，与题干意思相符。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1242,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','There are more wild pigs in Berlin now than in the past.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章第三段提到了柏林有野猪进城，但并未将现在的数量与过去进行比较。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1243,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Wild pigs sometimes cause traffic problems in Berlin.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文章第三段提到野猪 \'walk in the street and cause traffic accidents\'（在街上行走并造成交通事故）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1244,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Wild pigs started to come into Berlin years ago.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章未提及野猪开始进入柏林的具体时间。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1245,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','No one knows the number of wild dogs in Moscow.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文章第四段明确给出了数字 \'there are 35,000 wild dogs\'，说明人们知道其数量。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1246,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Some people help the wild dogs survive the cold winter.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文章最后一段提到人们给狗食物和水，甚至建造小屋让它们度过寒冬 (\'build small huts for the dogs to live in during the very cold winter\')。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1247,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Being sick away from home】Pampering (娇惯) yourself is always a good start: If you feel so ill and tired that you can\'t even get out of bed, then don\'t! Make a trip to the kitchen and stock up on fluids and try to make yourself some hot food. The key to getting better is to drink lots of fluids. Water and hot drinks such as green tea and soup are usually the best things.\n\n16. Paragraph ❶:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Taking good care of yourself\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Staying in bed for the entire day\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Taking your attention away from illness\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Knowing where and how to get medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Informing friends and family or your illness\"}]','A',NULL,'该段主要建议生病时要照顾自己（Pampering yourself），如喝流食、吃热食等，对应选项 A。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1248,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Being sick away from home】Try to distract yourself from feeling horrible. If you have a TV, watch one of your favorite films or TV series. If you don\'t have a TV, maybe put the radio on. If you have a headache and all the noise is too much to handle, try reading the book you\'ve always wanted to read but never had the time to. Being ill doesn\'t have to be the worst day in the world!\n\n17. Paragraph ❷:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Taking good care of yourself\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Staying in bed for the entire day\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Taking your attention away from illness\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Knowing where and how to get medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Informing friends and family or your illness\"}]','C',NULL,'该段建议通过看电视、读书等方式分散注意力（distract yourself），对应选项 C。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1249,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Being sick away from home】Tell your friends and family that you are ill. Sometimes there is nothing better than hearing words of comfort from loved ones who feel sorry for you and want to cheer you up and make you happy. There is nothing wrong with a little attention from others when you\'re ill. Who knows, they might even be willing to travel and visit you with lots of \"Get Well\" presents like your favorite food, magazine or flowers.\n\n18. Paragraph ❸:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Taking good care of yourself\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Staying in bed for the entire day\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Taking your attention away from illness\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Knowing where and how to get medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Informing friends and family or your illness\"}]','E',NULL,'该段建议告诉朋友和家人你生病了（Tell your friends and family），对应选项 E。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1250,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Being sick away from home】When you do arrive at a new place where you will be staying for a few months, make sure you know exactly where the nearest drugstore is. If you are in a foreign country, it might be best to translate a few useful phrases before you start asking for a cure.\n\n19. Paragraph ❹:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Taking good care of yourself\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Staying in bed for the entire day\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Taking your attention away from illness\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Knowing where and how to get medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Informing friends and family or your illness\"}]','D',NULL,'该段建议确认药店位置并学习相关短语以便买药（know exactly where the nearest drugstore is... asking for a cure），对应选项 D。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1251,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Being sick away from home】(文章开头部分缺失，根据语境推断为引入话题)\n\n20. Being sick away from home is ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"ask for medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"at your own pace\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"water and hot drinks\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"a terrible experience\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"at a nearby drugstore\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"read your favorite book\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"suffer from a cold\"}]','D',NULL,'根据常识及下文提到的各种应对措施，离家在外生病通常被描述为一种糟糕的经历（terrible experience）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1252,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Being sick away from home】If you\'re living away from home or abroad, it\'s important to get better at your own pace in order to ensure you can enjoy the rest of your time away.\n\n21. You are advised to recover ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"ask for medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"at your own pace\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"water and hot drinks\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"a terrible experience\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"at a nearby drugstore\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"read your favorite book\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"suffer from a cold\"}]','B',NULL,'原文提到 \'get better at your own pace\'，即按自己的节奏康复。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1253,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Being sick away from home】The key to getting better is to drink lots of fluids. Water and hot drinks such as green tea and soup are usually the best things.\n\n22. The best cure for illness is ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"ask for medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"at your own pace\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"water and hot drinks\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"a terrible experience\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"at a nearby drugstore\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"read your favorite book\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"suffer from a cold\"}]','C',NULL,'原文指出最好的治疗方式是多喝水和热饮（Water and hot drinks... are usually the best things）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1254,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Being sick away from home】If you have a headache and all the noise is too much to handle, try reading the book you\'ve always wanted to read but never had the time to.\n\n23. If you cannot bear the noise from TV, ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"ask for medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"at your own pace\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"water and hot drinks\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"a terrible experience\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"at a nearby drugstore\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"read your favorite book\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"suffer from a cold\"}]','F',NULL,'原文建议如果噪音太大无法忍受，可以尝试读喜欢的书（try reading the book...）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1255,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Being sick away from home】If you are in a foreign country, it might be best to translate a few useful phrases before you start asking for a cure.\n\n24. A few useful translated phrases help you ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"ask for medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"at your own pace\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"water and hot drinks\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"a terrible experience\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"at a nearby drugstore\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"read your favorite book\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"suffer from a cold\"}]','A',NULL,'原文提到翻译一些有用的短语是为了开始寻求治疗/药物（asking for a cure），对应选项 A ask for medicine。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1256,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Being sick away from home】make sure you know exactly where the nearest drugstore is.\n\n25. You can buy medicine ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"ask for medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"at your own pace\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"water and hot drinks\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"a terrible experience\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"at a nearby drugstore\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"read your favorite book\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"suffer from a cold\"}]','E',NULL,'原文提到要确保知道最近的药店在哪里（nearest drugstore），暗示可以在那里买药。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1257,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Swiss Banks】Switzerland is well-known for chocolate and its watch-making industry. It is even more famous for its unique banking and financial system. __(26)__\n\nBanking in Switzerland goes back to the 18th century. In the past, not only rich people but also dictators (独裁者) kept their money in Swiss banks. During World War II German Nazis (纳粹) put much of their money in Switzerland. _27_\n\nSwiss banks are popular for many reasons. _28_ It enjoys one of the highest per capita (人均) incomes in the world. It has been neutral for many centuries, especially during the two world wars. In addition, the Swiss franc is one of the most stable currencies in the world.\n\nMost importantly, Swiss banks follow very strict privacy rules. In 1934, a law was passed that forbade Swiss banks to reveal the names of account holders. _29_ If a Swiss banker reveals a person\'s bank account without permission, he or she commits a crime. Such regulations have made Switzerland a popular destination for many people.\n\nLately, however, the Swiss government has been under heavy pressure from other countries. _30_ They want the banks to reveal the names of possible criminals.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They urge it to change its bank laws.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Banks strictly protect the privacy of their clients.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Private banking has a long tradition in the country.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Banks play an important role in Switzerland\'s economy.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Foreigners in troubled areas also kept money in Swiss banks.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"For one, the country has a very stable and prosperous economy.\"}]','D',NULL,'第一段提到瑞士以巧克力、钟表业闻名，但更因独特的银行金融体系出名。空格处应承接上文说明银行业的重要性，选项 D“银行在瑞士经济中扮演重要角色”符合语境。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1258,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · Education in New Zealand】...children between these ages must __(31)__ school. Most children begin their schooling at 5. This period includes primary and secondary education, and it is __32__.\n\nEarly childhood covers the period from birth to 6 years old. This period may include both care and education. There are many __33__ such as play centers and kindergartens. More and more people are realizing the __34__ of early childhood education. Now 60 percent of children under 5 join in some form of pre-school education.\n\nChildren go to primary school for 8 years or up to the age of about 13. They __35__ go to secondary schools for a further 5 years. Some students may decide to leave school at 16.\n\nHigher education __36__ any education or training that takes place after secondary school. In New Zealand, this includes universities, __37__, and training schools.\n\nNew Zealand is __38__ becoming multi-cultural. More and more international __39__ are studying there. The education system is adapting to __40__ the needs of different cultural groups.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"meet\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"students\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"quickly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"means\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"free\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"wisely\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"then\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"value\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"choices\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"quit\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"attend\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"colleges\"}]','K',NULL,'根据句意“这个年龄段的孩子必须上学”，动词 attend (参加/上) 符合语境。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1259,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · Education in New Zealand】...Most children begin their schooling at 5. This period includes primary and secondary 