手术), diet plans, or diet pills.\n\nHowever, to build a positive body image __42__ (require) a balanced diet and a __43__ (health) lifestyle. In our daily life, to eat more fruits and __44__ (vegetable) than meat will help us keep fit, and the best way to keep ourselves in shape is to do some vigorous exercise every day.\n\nBesides, a correct attitude is __45__ (equal) important. We should not feel __46__ (embarrass) about our bodies. We should not believe our body is a shame of personal __47__ (fail). We do not need to be as __48__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','encouraged',NULL,'被动语态，be encouraged to do sth. 被鼓励做某事。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1269,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Body Image】...However, to build a positive body image __(42)__ (require) a balanced diet and a __43__ (health) lifestyle. In our daily life, to eat more fruits and __44__ (vegetable) than meat will help us keep fit, and the best way to keep ourselves in shape is to do some vigorous exercise every day.\n\nBesides, a correct attitude is __45__ (equal) important. We should not feel __46__ (embarrass) about our bodies. We should not believe our body is a shame of personal __47__ (fail). We do not need to be as __48__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','requires',NULL,'不定式短语作主语，谓语动词用单数形式 requires。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1270,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Body Image】...a balanced diet and a __(43)__ (health) lifestyle. In our daily life, to eat more fruits and __44__ (vegetable) than meat will help us keep fit, and the best way to keep ourselves in shape is to do some vigorous exercise every day.\n\nBesides, a correct attitude is __45__ (equal) important. We should not feel __46__ (embarrass) about our bodies. We should not believe our body is a shame of personal __47__ (fail). We do not need to be as __48__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','healthy',NULL,'修饰名词 lifestyle，需用形容词 healthy。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1271,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Body Image】...to eat more fruits and __(44)__ (vegetable) than meat will help us keep fit, and the best way to keep ourselves in shape is to do some vigorous exercise every day.\n\nBesides, a correct attitude is __45__ (equal) important. We should not feel __46__ (embarrass) about our bodies. We should not believe our body is a shame of personal __47__ (fail). We do not need to be as __48__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','vegetables',NULL,'与前面的 fruits 并列，且 vegetable 为可数名词，故用复数形式 vegetables。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1272,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Body Image】...Besides, a correct attitude is __(45)__ (equal) important. We should not feel __46__ (embarrass) about our bodies. We should not believe our body is a shame of personal __47__ (fail). We do not need to be as __48__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','equally',NULL,'修饰形容词 important，需用副词 equally。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1273,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Body Image】...We should not feel __(46)__ (embarrass) about our bodies. We should not believe our body is a shame of personal __47__ (fail). We do not need to be as __48__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','embarrassed',NULL,'feel embarrassed about... 对...感到尴尬/难堪，形容人的感受用 -ed 结尾的形容词。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1274,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Body Image】...We should not believe our body is a shame of personal __(47)__ (fail). We do not need to be as __48__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','failure',NULL,'介词 of 后接名词，personal failure 个人失败。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1275,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Body Image】...We do not need to be as __(48)__ (attract) as everyone else. Instead, we should love...','[]','attractive',NULL,'as + adj. + as 结构，此处需填 attract 的形容词形式 attractive。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1276,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','ourselves rather than desire for __(49)__ (possible) standards. We should have a real and clear understanding of our body parts, and appreciate our body for the way it is. In this way, we will feel __50__ (comfort) and confident.','[]','impossible',NULL,'根据句意“与其渴望不可能的标准，不如接受自己”，此处应填 possible 的反义词 impossible。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1277,4,NULL,'WRITING','请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇 100 词左右的英文短文。\n\n假设你的美国朋友 John 给你发来一封电子邮件,表示他对中国传统文化很感兴趣,希望你能为他简要介绍一个中国的传统节日(Traditional Chinese Festival)。以下是你给他回复邮件的主要内容:\n● 节日名称。\n● 节日由来。\n● 人们如何庆祝这一节日。\n请以 Li Ke 署名。','[]',NULL,'[\"格式正确（书信/邮件格式），包含称呼、正文、落款。\", \"内容完整：介绍了节日名称（如 Spring Festival, Mid-Autumn Festival 等）。\", \"解释了节日的由来或背景。\", \"描述了人们如何庆祝该节日（习俗、活动等）。\", \"语言通顺，词数符合要求（约 100 词）。\"]','',3,'英语二2',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1278,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Booking Online and Saving the Environment】When you are looking to book a holiday, it is unlikely that you will think about how green your booking decision is, but it is something that you should think about. By \"green\" we mean the impact on the environment.\n\nWhen looking to book a holiday, you will probably find that you are faced with two main decisions. The first is to go into a travel agency, pick up brochures (宣传册), read through them and go back with just one and book with the travel agents directly or over the phone. The second is to go onto the Internet.\n\nThe Internet holds many advantages over the travel agencies. The main one is convenience. You can go online to look at holidays at any time of the day. The travel agents, however, are usually very busy at times when people can actually go, i. e. lunch hours or at the weekend. You could use the telephone, but you wouldn\'t be able to see the pictures or the details of the holidays, So you would probably be sent a brochure anyway.\n\nThere are websites on the Internet that make shopping for holiday deals much easier. These websites are known as price comparison websites. They search through lots of different tour operators, and the results are displayed on one page, from which you can choose.\n\nCompared with the travel agencies, booking online is greener. The piles of brochures are definitely not green, and the amount of unnecessary paper used can\'t be good for the environment. In the days of the Internet, there is really no need for such a large amount of paper to be wasted. So booking online will not only save you time and effort, it will do a little bit towards saving the environment, too!\n\n1. When planning holidays, few people will think about being green.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第一段 \'it is unlikely that you will think about how green your booking decision is\'（你不太可能考虑预订决定的环保程度），可知题目陈述正确。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1279,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','2. There are two main choices when people look to book their holidays.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第二段 \'you will probably find that you are faced with two main decisions\'，可知题目陈述正确。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1280,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','3. People go to travel agencies and make their decisions directly.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第二段 \'go into a travel agency... go back with just one and book...\'，说明人们去旅行社通常是拿宣传册回去看后再决定，而不是直接做决定。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1281,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','4. The main advantage of booking online is saving money.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第三段 \'The main one is convenience.\'，网上预订的主要优势是便利，而非省钱。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1282,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','5. Many people go to travel agencies at lunchtime.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第三段 \'travel agents, however, are usually very busy at times when people can actually go, i. e. lunch hours\'，可知午餐时间很多人去旅行社。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1283,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','6. Booking holidays by telephone requires less communicative skills.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到了电话预订，但并未提及它是否需要更少的沟通技巧。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1284,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','7. There are limited choices at price comparison websites.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第四段 \'They search through lots of different tour operators\'，说明选择很多，并非有限。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1285,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','8. Travel agencies make the best use of price comparison websites.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到价格比较网站是为了让购物更容易，并未提及旅行社是否充分利用了这些网站。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1286,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','9. Travelers collect brochures as a hobby.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到人们去旅行社拿宣传册，但没说是作为一种爱好收集。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1287,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','10. Booking online is a way to save the environment.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据最后一段 \'booking online is greener... it will do a little bit towards saving the environment\'，可知网上预订是保护环境的一种方式。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1288,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Urban Gardening】(见上文)\n\n11. Urban gardening came into being as a result of ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"the lack of land for gardening\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"new technology\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"government encouragement\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"the increasing population\"}]','A',NULL,'根据文章第三段第一句 \'Community gardening could be an option for anyone who does not have space for a garden at home.\'（社区园艺对于那些家里没有花园空间的人来说是一个选择），可知城市园艺的兴起是因为缺乏用于园艺的土地。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1289,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Urban Gardening】(见上文)\n\n12. The word \"confined\" (Para. 2) means ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"open\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"empty\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"limited\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"occupied\"}]','C',NULL,'虽然本页未显示包含该词的第二段完整内容，但根据上下文语境及常见词汇题规律，\'confined\' 通常意为 \'restricted\' 或 \'limited\'（受限制的、狭窄的）。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1290,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Urban Gardening】(见上文)\n\n13. Plants grown on windowsills require a lot of ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"water\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"space\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"soil\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"sunlight\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第一段第二句 \'Plants grown on a windowsill should usually receive at least six to eight hours of sunlight daily.\'（窗台上种植的植物通常每天至少需要接受六到八小时的阳光照射），可知它们需要很多阳光。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1291,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Urban Gardening】(见上文)\n\n14. Raised beds are popular because they ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"are efficient\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"are cheap\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"last long\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"contain fertilizers\"}]','B',NULL,'根据第二段最后一句 \'People like them because the beds often cost much less than most other methods of gardening.\'（人们喜欢它们是因为这些苗床的成本通常比大多数其他园艺方法低得多），可知是因为便宜。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1292,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Urban Gardening】(见上文)\n\n15. Community gardening is beneficial because it ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"saves more land\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"requires less work\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"increases output\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"connects people\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第三段最后两句 \'...some cities allow everyone in the neighborhood to share and work on the same land. This method could be beneficial for people in the neighborhood who share the passion for growing things.\'（……允许邻居们共同分享和耕种同一块土地。这种方法对于有共同种植热情的邻居来说是有益的），暗示了这种模式能连接邻里关系。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1293,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Lack of Sleep Is Dangerous】Do you know that if you miss out too much sleep you will die? It\'s true! If you stay awake for a long, long time, your brain and body will break down.\nThe unofficial world record for staying awake is 11 days, and it\'s held by Randy Gardner. __(26)__ He also had help from TV and radio reporters, a sleep researcher and a doctor.\nWhat happened? _27_ Then his brain started to lose sense. On day 4, he thought a street sign was really a person. On day 6, he began to speak very slowly. On day 9, he couldn\'t finish sentences. On day 10, Randy thought he saw a forest in the next room. _28_ Eventually, after he\'d broken the world record, Randy was told to go to sleep. Experiments that keep people awake for dangerously long periods are always stopped before the patients break down.\nRats, however, aren\'t so well cared for. _29_. That\'s sooner than if they\'d been allowed to sleep but were given no food. They get really thin. But that\'s not because they stop eating — quite the opposite. Even though these rats are eating food, their bodies can\'t process it in the normal way. On top of that, their little bodies lose more heat than normal, which makes them weak. This means that they need more food to stay at a healthy temperature. _30_\nAnd that\'s what lack of sleep does for you.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"In fact, he went a bit crazy.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Normally rats wouldn\'t catch a cold.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Towards the end, the health of these rats is failing.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"When kept from sleeping, they die within three weeks.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Randy asked two of his friends to stop him falling asleep.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"First of all, staying awake long made Randy bad-tempered.\"}]','E',NULL,'根据后文 \'He also had help from...\' (他也得到了...的帮助)，可知前文提到了其他人对他的帮助。选项 E \'Randy asked two of his friends to stop him falling asleep\' (Randy让两个朋友阻止他睡着) 符合语境，且与后文的 \'also\' 构成并列关系。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1294,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · Talking Counts!】Most words in a child\'s vocabulary come from everyday encounters with language. Children __(31)__ up language from books, media, and conversations.\nYou can increase your child\'s vocabulary and __32__ knowledge by having conversations with them. With babies, you can talk to them about what you\'re doing so they can begin to __33__ words with concepts. As your baby begins to speak, start asking, \"What\'s that?\" when __34__ to objects or pictures. Elaborate on their __35__ answers as a way to have them listening to more words. \"Yes, that is a banana! It\'s __36__ and smooth.\"\nWith young children, you can talk about the things you see in your __37__ on trips around town, or on television. These conversations help build a child\'s __38__ of his world. When reading, pause to ask questions on the story, Ask, \"Why do you think he did that?\" or \"What do you think is going to happen __39__ ?\" Tell your children stories from your own life, or about the day they were __40__. This helps develop their personal and cultural identity.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"link\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"simple\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"secondly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"neighborhood\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"yellow\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"build\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"understanding\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"pointing\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"pick\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"born\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"background\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"next\"}]','I',NULL,'固定搭配 pick up，意为“学会（语言）”。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1295,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Water Shortage】Getting water seems (seem) so easy for many people. You will be __(41)__ (mistake) if you think there is an __42__ (end) supply of water. In fact, the world has a water shortage. Seventy percent of the world is __43__ (cover) in water. But most of it is salt water. Only a small __44__ (percent) is fresh drinking water. Countries __45__ (include) Spain, Italy and South Africa actually import water from countries such as the United States and Australia.','[]','mistaken',NULL,'be mistaken 意为“弄错了，搞错了”，形容词短语作表语。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1296,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Water Shortage】Getting water seems (seem) so easy for many people. You will be __41__ (mistake) if you think there is an __42__ (end) supply of water. In fact, the world has a water shortage. Seventy percent of the world is __43__ (cover) in water. But most of it is salt water. Only a small __44__ (percent) is fresh drinking water. Countries __45__ (include) Spain, Italy and South Africa actually import water from countries such as the United States and Australia.\n\n__(46)__ (surprising), 1.1 billion people on earth have difficulty __47__ (get) clean drinking water. This global problem is predicted to get __48__ (bad) as the atmosphere becomes warmer.\n\nEvery person in Britain __49__ (use) about 150 litres of water a day. In some countries people only have 5 to 10 litres a day! They would be __50__ (shock) to learn how we waste drinking water.','[]','Surprisingly',NULL,'此处修饰整句话，应用副词形式。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1297,4,NULL,'WRITING','请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇 100 词左右的英文短文。\n\n某英文报社正在举办题为“An Unforgettable Holiday”的征文活动。请就此题目写一篇英文短文应征，内容包括：\n• 哪个假期令你难忘？\n• 为什么令你难忘？','[]',NULL,'[\"明确点出令自己难忘的假期名称或时间地点。\", \"详细描述该假期的经历（如去了哪里、做了什么）。\", \"阐述为什么这个假期令人难忘（如学到了什么、感受到了什么、发生了什么特别的事）。\", \"语言流畅，符合字数要求。\"]','',3,'英语二2',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1298,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】I may not be a movie star, best-selling author, or millionaire when I grow up, but one thing I will be known for, at least locally, is commuting by bicycle. It\'s sad to see how few people do even though many could. Lots of people eagerly campaign for the reduction of greenhouse gases, but by driving cars, they\'re still contributing to the problem.\n\nYou might be picturing me as an extreme environmentalist (环保主义者), but I\'m not one of those teenagers who wear shirts that say \"Help save the world: Recycle.\" Actually, my interest in exercise, health, and fitness led me to cycling.\n\nCycling can help you lose weight, improve your health, and prevent many diseases. Cycling also carries a relatively low chance of injury.\n\nWhile being good for your body, bicycle commuting is also a great way to cut greenhouse gases. Many environmentalists recycle, plant trees, and drive hybrid cars (混合动力汽车), but bicycle commuting could be even more effective than all of those combined. You could cut down the amount of greenhouse gases just by commuting by bicycle a few times a week.\n\nBicycle commuting saves money too. When you buy your bicycle and the things that usually go with it, you might be shocked by the cost. But if you think about the increasingly high gas prices, you will know for sure that you can save a significant amount each year by not driving a car.\n\nYou might think that you don\'t have time for bicycle commuting. Actually, you probably do. You could cut back on your TV time and pick up this activity. It helps you care for the environment, save money, and most importantly get fit.\n\n1. I will write a best-selling book on cycling.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到作者可能不会成为畅销书作家（best-selling author），但并未提及是否会写关于骑行的书。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1299,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n2. Many local people commute by bicycle.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第一段 \'It\'s sad to see how few people do\' 可知，骑自行车通勤的人很少，与题干中的 \'Many\' 矛盾。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1300,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n3. I am devoted to environmental protection.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'虽然作者通过骑行支持环保，但第二段明确说 \'I\'m not one of those...extreme environmentalist\'，且未提及是否致力于（devoted to）环境保护事业，属于未提及或推断过度。',2,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1301,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n4. I started cycling to improve my health.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第二段 \'my interest in exercise, health, and fitness led me to cycling\' 可知，作者是因为对健康和健身感兴趣才开始骑行的。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1302,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n5. People are less likely to get injured while cycling.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第三段 \'Cycling also carries a relatively low chance of injury\' 可知，骑行受伤几率较低。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1303,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n6. People drive to work for convenience.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到了人们开车上班（driving cars），但没有说明他们是为了方便（convenience）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1304,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n7. Bicycle commuting could be more effective in reducing greenhouse gases.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第四段 \'bicycle commuting could be even more effective than all of those combined\'（指回收、种树等）可知，骑行在减少温室气体方面更有效。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1305,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n8. People are in a good mood while cycling.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到了身体健康和省钱，但未提及骑行时的心情（mood）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1306,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n9. Gas prices keep going up.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第五段 \'increasingly high gas prices\' 可知油价在不断上涨。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1307,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Bicycle Commuting】(同上)\n\n10. Bikes are inexpensive to most people.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第五段 \'you might be shocked by the cost\' 可知自行车购买成本可能较高，并不便宜。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1308,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The Scientist and the Milk】...The scientist remarked that it was then that he knew he didn\'t need to be afraid to make mistakes. Instead, mistakes were just opportunities for learning something new, which is, after all, what scientific experiments are all about. Even if the experiment \"doesn\'t work\", we usually learn something valuable from it.\n\n11. This story is about a scientist who ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"was extraordinary when he was young\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"became well-known after an interview\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"was smarter than the average person\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"achieved great success in the medical field\"}]','B',NULL,'虽然本页未显示文章开头，但根据题目选项及常见故事版本（Dr. Robert Sternberg），科学家通常是在接受采访后变得出名。选项 A \'extraordinary\' 过于笼统且文中强调的是他处理错误的方式；选项 C 和 D 文中无依据。结合上下文语境，B 是最符合此类传记类阅读理解的推断。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1309,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The Scientist and the Milk】...He chose the sponge and together they cleaned up the spilt milk.\n\n12. He got the milk spilt all over the kitchen floor because he ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"dropped the bottle\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"was naughty\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"slipped and fell\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"was weak\"}]','A',NULL,'根据文中母亲的话 \"what we have here is a failed experiment in how to effectively carry a big milk bottle... see if you can discover a way to carry it without dropping it\"，可知牛奶洒了是因为他把瓶子掉了（dropped）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1310,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The Scientist and the Milk】...Would you like to play in the milk for a few minutes before we clean it up?\"\nIndeed, he did...\n\n13. After seeing the spilt milk, his mother ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"shouted at him\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"cleaned the floor herself\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"encouraged him to play in the milk\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"forced him to clean the kitchen\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第一段结尾和第二段开头 \"Would you like to play in the milk for a few minutes before we clean it up?\" \"Indeed, he did.\"，可知母亲鼓励他在清理之前先玩一会儿牛奶。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1311,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The Scientist and the Milk】Let\'s go out in the back yard and fill the bottle with water and see if you can discover a way to carry it without dropping it.\"\n\n14. The mother and the son went out in the back yard to ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"fill the bottle with milk\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"clean the bottle\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"find a way to carry the bottle\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"search for a new bottle\"}]','C',NULL,'根据文中 \"see if you can discover a way to carry it without dropping it\"，他们去后院是为了寻找一种不掉落瓶子的携带方法。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1312,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The Scientist and the Milk】Instead, mistakes were just opportunities for learning something new...\n\n15. According to the text, mistakes give us chances to ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"know the truth\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"learn something new\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"do some experiments\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"teach a child a lesson\"}]','B',NULL,'根据最后一段 \"mistakes were just opportunities for learning something new\"，直接对应选项 B。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1313,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】\nVolunteers are people who work without being paid. They do the work because they want to. We need volunteers because there are many things that need to be done in society which the Government can\'t afford to pay for.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ①:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Definition of volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How volunteers are organized\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"How volunteers contribute to society\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Why people want to be volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"An organization sending volunteers abroad\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"An organization delivering meals to the elderly\"}]','A',NULL,'第一段主要介绍了志愿者是什么（Definition），即无偿工作的人。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1314,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】\nVolunteers are motivated by a desire to help others and to make the world a better place. Statistics suggest that more than one million people do voluntary work in New Zealand. Some volunteers do the kind of work that they are particularly interested in, but perhaps haven\'t had the chance to do during their working lives. Others make use of their professional skills and experience.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ②:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Definition of volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How volunteers are organized\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"How volunteers contribute to society\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Why people want to be volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"An organization sending volunteers abroad\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"An organization delivering meals to the elderly\"}]','D',NULL,'第二段提到志愿者受帮助他人的愿望驱动（motivated by a desire...），解释了人们想成为志愿者的原因。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1315,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】\nVolunteers contribute to society in a number of ways. For example, some give their time to help preserve the natural environment. While there are government-run projects to maintain national parks and forests, the projects would not succeed without volunteers. Some environmental organizations rely solely on voluntary labor.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ③:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Definition of volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How volunteers are organized\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"How volunteers contribute to society\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Why people want to be volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"An organization sending volunteers abroad\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"An organization delivering meals to the elderly\"}]','C',NULL,'第三段首句即主题句“Volunteers contribute to society in a number of ways”，讲述志愿者如何贡献社会。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1316,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】\n\"Meals on Wheels\" is a voluntary organization run by the Red Cross. It delivers meals to elderly people who are unable to cook for themselves. Every year volunteer drivers deliver a million meals. This enables elderly people to remain in their own houses.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ④:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Definition of volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How volunteers are organized\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"How volunteers contribute to society\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Why people want to be volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"An organization sending volunteers abroad\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"An organization delivering meals to the elderly\"}]','F',NULL,'第四段介绍了“Meals on Wheels”这个组织，它给老年人送餐（delivers meals to elderly people）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1317,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】\nVolunteer Service Abroad was started in 1962. It sends volunteers to poor countries. To be a volunteer you should be between the ages of 25 and 77, of good health and have a skill or ability that is requested by the country. Volunteers spend two years helping the local people improve their lives. Two years is a long time, but when they return, many volunteers say, \"It was the best two years of my life.\"\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ⑤:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Definition of volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How volunteers are organized\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"How volunteers contribute to society\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Why people want to be volunteers\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"An organization sending volunteers abroad\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"An organization delivering meals to the elderly\"}]','E',NULL,'第五段介绍了“Volunteer Service Abroad”，这是一个派遣志愿者去贫穷国家的组织（sends volunteers to poor countries）。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1318,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】Volunteers are people who work without being paid. They do the work because they want to. We need volunteers because there are many things that need to be done in society which the Government can\'t afford to pay for.\n\nVolunteers are motivated by a desire to help others and to make the world a better place. Statistics suggest that more than one million people do voluntary work in New Zealand. Some volunteers do the kind of work that they are particularly interested in, but perhaps haven\'t had the chance to do during their working lives. Others make use of their professional skills and experience.\n\nVolunteers contribute to society in a number of ways. For example, some give their time to help preserve the natural environment. While there are government-run projects to maintain national parks and forests, the projects would not succeed without volunteers. Some environmental organizations rely solely on voluntary labor.\n\n\"Meals on Wheels\" is a voluntary organization run by the Red Cross. It delivers meals to elderly people who are unable to cook for themselves. Every year volunteer drivers deliver a million meals. This enables elderly people to remain in their own houses.\n\nVolunteer Service Abroad was started in 1962. It sends volunteers to poor countries. To be a volunteer you should be between the ages of 25 and 77, of good health and have a skill or ability that is requested by the country. Volunteers spend two years helping the local people improve their lives. Two years is a long time, but when they return, many volunteers say, \"It was the best two years of my life.\"\n\n21. People do voluntary work because they want to ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"help others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"leaving their homes\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cooking for the elderly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"using their professional skills\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"find their experience rewarding\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"preserve the natural environment\"}]','A',NULL,'根据文章第二段第一句 \'Volunteers are motivated by a desire to help others...\' 可知，志愿者工作的动力是想要帮助他人。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1319,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】(同上)\n\n22. Some volunteers help others by ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"help others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"leaving their homes\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cooking for the elderly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"using their professional skills\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"find their experience rewarding\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"preserve the natural environment\"}]','D',NULL,'根据文章第二段最后一句 \'Others make use of their professional skills and experience.\' 可知，有些志愿者通过利用他们的专业技能来帮助他人。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1320,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】(同上)\n\n23. Some organizations rely on volunteers to help ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"help others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"leaving their homes\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cooking for the elderly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"using their professional skills\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"find their experience rewarding\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"preserve the natural environment\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第三段内容，提到环保项目需要志愿者，\'Some environmental organizations rely solely on voluntary labor.\' 且前文提到 \'help preserve the natural environment\'。',1,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1321,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】(同上)\n\n24. The elderly can have their meals delivered without ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"help others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"leaving their homes\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cooking for the elderly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"using their professional skills\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"find their experience rewarding\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"preserve the natural environment\"}]','B',NULL,'根据文章第四段关于 \'Meals on Wheels\' 的描述，送餐服务让老人能够待在自己家里 (\'remain in their own houses\')，即不用离开家就能吃到饭。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1322,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Volunteers】(同上)\n\n25. Many volunteers returning from poor countries ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"help others\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"leaving their homes\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"cooking for the elderly\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"using their professional skills\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"find their experience rewarding\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"preserve the natural environment\"}]','E',NULL,'根据文章最后一段，志愿者回国后说 \'It was the best two years of my life.\'，说明他们觉得这段经历很有价值/有回报 (rewarding)。',2,'英语二2',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1323,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','Planting a garden is a lot like having a family. Both require a great deal of work, __(31)__ as they grow and as the seasons __32__. As summer days lengthen, your plants become __33__ on you, much like your children depend on you for food and drink. Like a __34__ child asking for drink of water, your plants do the same. Their bent body issues a demand much the way your child requests milk or juice. Getting enough water, they would thrive soon.\n\nYou might also find you have to __35__ the space around your plants, much like you pick up toys and clothes that have been thrown in your kid\'s room. Similarly, roses need to be pruned (修剪), and weeds need to be pulled. To keep children healthy, parents protect their children against disease with __36__, and gardeners do the same with insect repellent (驱虫剂). To nourish (滋养) them, parents __37__ children vitamins, and gardeners use fertilizer, as both promote healthy growth.\n\nAs children grow up, they need less care. However, here\'s where the similarity ends. While plants die or become __38__ during winter, children __39__ maintain an important role in the family, and parents will find their __40__ does not come to an end.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"help\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"clean\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"change\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"inactive\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"dependent\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"still\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"strong\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"give\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"responsibility\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"thirsty\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"especially\"}]','L',NULL,'根据句意“两者都需要大量的工作，尤其是在它们生长和季节变化时”，此处表示强调，选 especially。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1324,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · What Makes Us Different】\nThe reason Earth differs (differ) from all the other __(41)__ (planet) in the universe is because of you and me. At first, we were living in caves, then came the ice age, then the meltdown, and __42__ (final), what we are today. We and Earth as a whole have changed so much. The only thing that hasn\'t changed is our greed and __43__ (jealous).\nWhile we were in caves, we fought for food. While we were living on the ice, we fought for __44__ (warm), clothing, and food. Now, we are __45__ (fight) over land. Why do we fight for land that was never in our __46__ (possess)? Wars, big or small, take place every day. Earth is a single nation. All the land masses on it belong to the planet, not to us. Everyone is the same, regardless of race, gender, or religion. We are all deserve to be __47__ (treat) equally. We are all also unique, but that doesn\'t make us any __48__ (little) human than the next person.\nIf we can start by __49__ (pay) a compliment (赞美) to a different person each day, our world will be __50__ (friendly) to live in. If we at least help one person in need and let room for love to grow in our hearts, the world will be a better place.','[]','planets',NULL,'根据句意“地球与宇宙中所有其他行星不同”，other后接名词复数形式。',1,'英语二2',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1325,4,NULL,'WRITING','请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇 100 词左右的英文短文。\n\n某英文报社正在举办题为“Spring is Coming”的征文活动。请你根据下述写作要点提交一篇英文短文应征：\n• 简要描写春天的景象。\n• 介绍人们在春天里的各种活动。','[]',NULL,'[\"描述春天的自然景象（如天气变暖、花草发芽等）\", \"列举人们的活动（如放风筝、野餐、植树等）\", \"表达喜爱之情或总结全文\"]','',2,'英语二2',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:38:35','2026-10-18 19:38:35'),(1326,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nPeople usually think leasing a car can save money.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第二段第一句 \'Most people think about leasing because they believe it will cost them less money.\'（大多数人考虑租赁是因为他们相信这能让他们花更少的钱），可知人们通常认为租车能省钱。',1,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1327,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nLeasing a car costs less in the long term.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第一段 \'Leasing can end up being just as expensive as buying.\' 和第二段 \'They\'re right—it is cheaper, but only in the short term.\'，说明长期来看租车并不便宜，甚至可能一样贵。',1,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1328,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nMore people like to lease cars than before.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章中提到了很多人想租车的原因，但并没有将现在的人数与过去进行对比，也未提及趋势变化。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1329,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nPeople can lease a car they cannot afford.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第三段第一句 \'Many people want to lease because they can drive a more expensive car than they might otherwise be able to afford.\'，说明人们可以租得起那些买不起的更贵的车。',1,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1330,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nYoung people prefer to lease the latest models of cars.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章提到人们喜欢租最新款的车（\'allows you to drive the latest models\'），但没有特别指出是“年轻人”（Young people）更喜欢这样做。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1331,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nFord Explorer is the most popular model in the leasing market.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文章仅以 Ford Explorer 为例说明可以用同样的价格租到更好的车，并未提及它是市场上最受欢迎的车型。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1332,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nPeople often pay more than they expect for a lease.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第四段第一句 \'Furthermore, people who lease cars are often shocked by how much they must pay when the lease is over.\'，shocked 暗示了费用超出预期。',1,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1333,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nPeople need to pay for each mile they drive during the lease.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第四段第二、三句 \'Most leases limit you to a certain number of miles. If you go over that, you must pay for each mile.\'，只有超过限制里程的部分才需要付费，而不是每一英里都要付钱。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1334,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nLeasing companies pay for repairs to the leased cars.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第四段倒数第二句 \'In addition, when you lease, you have to pay for regular maintenance and repairs to the vehicle.\'，明确指出租客必须自己支付维修费。',1,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1335,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · To Lease(租赁)or Not to lease】\nThe author advises people to buy an affordable car.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章最后一段 \'Remember: whatever model you can afford to buy, it is yours after you make the payments.\'，作者建议购买自己能负担得起的车。',1,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1336,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Small Business Mental Health】\n(见 passages 字段)\n\n11. One reason to have one\'s own business is that one can have more _______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"flexible working hours\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"support from others\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"available resources\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"life experience\"}]','A',NULL,'虽然本页截取的文本未直接提及此点，但根据此类文章（关于小企业主心理健康）的常规逻辑及上下文推断，拥有自己的企业通常被认为能提供更灵活的工作时间（flexible working hours），这也是人们选择创业的主要原因之一。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1337,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Small Business Mental Health】\n(见 passages 字段)\n\n12. A small business owner usually has _______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"a more colorful life\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"a bigger profit\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"less stress from work\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"longer working time\"}]','D',NULL,'文中提到 \'I couldn\'t separate myself from my business\'（我无法将我自己与我的生意分开），暗示了小企业主往往工作时间长、压力大。结合常识和选项，D项符合文意。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1338,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Small Business Mental Health】\n(见 passages 字段)\n\n13. Fawkner\'s business ran into trouble because _______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"it was taken over by her husband\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"she had a serious mental problem\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"it was hit by the financial crisis\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"she started a mental health program\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第二段第一句 \'When her successful business struggled due to the global financial crisis...\'（当她的成功生意因全球金融危机而陷入困境时……），可知原因是金融危机。',1,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1339,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Small Business Mental Health】\n(见 passages 字段)\n\n14. Fawkner didn\'t feel so alone because _______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"she had her family around\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"she could watch DVD at work\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"others had similar experiences\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"the counselor was helpful to her\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第四段 \'The stories on the DVD in the program were so helpful. I was crying because I didn\'t feel so alone.\'（项目DVD里的故事很有帮助。我哭了，因为我不再感到那么孤独。）这里的语境是指她看到了其他有类似经历的人的故事，从而产生了共鸣，不再觉得只有自己这样。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1340,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Small Business Mental Health】\n(见 passages 字段)\n\n15. According to Fawkner, small business owners need more _______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"financial aid\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"technical knowledge\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"management skills\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"mental health assistance\"}]','D',NULL,'文章最后一段提到 \'For Fawkner, small business owners are overlooked... small business owners are struggling on their own.\'（在Fawkner看来，小企业主被忽视了……他们独自挣扎）。整篇文章都在讨论小企业主的心理健康问题及其缺乏支持，因此她认为需要更多的心理健康援助。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1341,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】\n❶ The most important secret to happiness is to be grateful for the good things in your life—whatever may be your financial position. Instead of appreciating material wealth, be thankful for the loved ones in your life and enjoy the little pleasures of life that come your way.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ❶:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help people in need\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Have a healthy lifestyle\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Do something creative\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Better your social relationships\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Be thankful for what you have\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Learn to understand and forgive\"}]','E',NULL,'第一段主要讲述幸福最重要的秘诀是感恩生活中美好的事物，即“Be thankful for what you have”。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1342,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】\n❷ The next most important secret is to develop relationships. Increasing social contacts helps boost brain power. Therefore, work towards improving your relationships and take time off to get in touch with friends. This will lift some burden off your shoulders, especially when you share your thoughts and feelings. Socializing can give you an added boost to your moods.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ❷:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help people in need\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Have a healthy lifestyle\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Do something creative\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Better your social relationships\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Be thankful for what you have\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Learn to understand and forgive\"}]','D',NULL,'第二段主要讲述发展人际关系的重要性，建议改善关系并与朋友保持联系，对应选项“Better your social relationships”。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1343,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】\n❸ Thirdly, do not hold a grudge (怨恨) against anyone. Instead, learn to be kind, generous, and forgiving towards others, even to the person who hurt you. Be sympathetic and understanding, and try not to criticize others. Focus on the positives of a person instead of the negatives, for none of us is born perfect. It will keep your heart and mind free and peaceful.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ❸:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help people in need\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Have a healthy lifestyle\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Do something creative\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Better your social relationships\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Be thankful for what you have\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Learn to understand and forgive\"}]','F',NULL,'第三段建议不要怀恨在心，要学会宽容、理解和原谅他人，对应选项“Learn to understand and forgive”。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1344,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】\n❹ Besides, involve yourself in some creative process, be it dancing, writing or drawing. This can bring out the hidden talent in you to achieve magical happiness. Or pick up new skills and feel the great sense of satisfaction by carrying out certain tasks which you otherwise would never have felt.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ❹:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help people in need\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Have a healthy lifestyle\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Do something creative\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Better your social relationships\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Be thankful for what you have\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Learn to understand and forgive\"}]','C',NULL,'第四段提到参与创造性的过程（如跳舞、写作或绘画），对应选项“Do something creative”。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1345,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】\n❺ Finally, follow a daily regular sleep-wake cycle to keep you energetic and happy. Exercise regularly or practice relaxation techniques like deep breathing and yoga (瑜伽). Ensure you get eight to nine hours of sleep every day and have a well-balanced diet.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ❺:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Help people in need\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Have a healthy lifestyle\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Do something creative\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Better your social relationships\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Be thankful for what you have\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Learn to understand and forgive\"}]','B',NULL,'第五段强调规律作息、锻炼和健康饮食，这些都是健康生活方式的体现，对应选项“Have a healthy lifestyle”。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1346,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】Some people are naturally blessed with a cheerful character. They spread warmth and sunshine wherever they go. They attract people like bees to honey. So what is it that makes these people so different from others?\n\nA cheerful character makes you ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"more intelligent\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"even if you are poor\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"different from others\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"even when you are hurt\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to develop your potential\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to gain more material wealth\"}]','C',NULL,'根据文章第一段最后一句 \'So what is it that makes these people so different from others?\' 可知，开朗的性格让你与众不同。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1347,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】❶ The most important secret to happiness is to be grateful for the good things in your life—whatever may be your financial position. Instead of appreciating material wealth, be thankful for the loved ones in your life and enjoy the little pleasures of life that come your way.\n\nEnjoy the pleasures of life ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"more intelligent\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"even if you are poor\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"different from others\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"even when you are hurt\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to develop your potential\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to gain more material wealth\"}]','B',NULL,'根据文章第二段 \'whatever may be your financial position\'（无论你的经济状况如何）以及 \'Instead of appreciating material wealth\'（不要欣赏物质财富），暗示即使贫穷也要享受生活中的乐趣。选项 B \'even if you are poor\' 符合语境。',2,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1348,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】❷ The next most important secret is to develop relationships. Increasing social contacts helps boost brain power. Therefore, work towards improving your relationships and take time off to get in touch with friends. This will lift some burden off your shoulders, especially when you share your thoughts and feelings. Socializing can give you an added boost to your moods.\n\nSocializing can make you ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"more intelligent\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"even if you are poor\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"different from others\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"even when you are hurt\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to develop your potential\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to gain more material wealth\"}]','A',NULL,'根据文章第三段 \'Increasing social contacts helps boost brain power\'（增加社交有助于提升脑力），即让你更聪明 (more intelligent)。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1349,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】❸ Thirdly, do not hold a grudge (怨恨) against anyone. Instead, learn to be kind, generous, and forgiving towards others, even to the person who hurt you. Be sympathetic and understanding, and try not to criticize others. Focus on the positives of a person instead of the negatives, for none of us is born perfect. It will keep your heart and mind free and peaceful.\n\nTry to forgive ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"more intelligent\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"even if you are poor\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"different from others\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"even when you are hurt\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to develop your potential\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to gain more material wealth\"}]','D',NULL,'根据文章第四段 \'forgiving towards others, even to the person who hurt you\'（原谅他人，甚至是伤害你的人），对应选项 D \'even when you are hurt\'。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1350,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Secrets for a Happier You】❹ Besides, involve yourself in some creative process, be it dancing, writing or drawing. This can bring out the hidden talent in you to achieve magical happiness. Or pick up new skills and feel the great sense of satisfaction by carrying out certain tasks which you otherwise would never have felt.\n\nCreative activities enable you ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"more intelligent\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"even if you are poor\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"different from others\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"even when you are hurt\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"to develop your potential\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"to gain more material wealth\"}]','E',NULL,'根据文章第五段 \'bring out the hidden talent in you\'（激发你隐藏的才能），对应选项 E \'to develop your potential\'（开发你的潜能）。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1351,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','Cultural differences can take many forms. I have noticed many differences in French culture compared to English culture, from the way people dress, to their attitudes towards food, to what they do for fun. One thing that has struck me in particular in France is people\'s personal interactions with each other. __(26)__\n\nFirstly, it\'s the kissing. Everyone kisses each other on the cheek. It\'s a greeting, instead of saying \"hi\" or \"hello\". ____(27)____ Everyone participates in the kissing ritual, the young, the old, male, female strangers and friends. I kiss my friends. I kiss the teachers at the school. And even if I\'m in a hurry, I am still expected to make time to give acquaintances a quick kiss on the cheek as I rush past. I don\'t mind it. ____(28)____ It quickly turns strangers into acquaintances, and acquaintances into friends.\n\nAnother thing that I\'ve noticed is that people in France are much more open with people they don\'t know. ____(29)____ In France, however, on long train journeys people have often started a conversation with me for no reason. They have a chat simply to pass the time. And I really enjoy being able to share a part of my life and my story with someone else.\n\nWhatever impressions you may have about French people, I have found that they are, for the most part, open and at ease talking to strangers. ____(30)____','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"In fact, I quite like it.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They differ a lot from those in the UK.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Often the kiss is a substitute for words.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"This makes me more comfortable with them too.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Britons often greet each other with hugs and kisses.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"In England, you talk to a stranger only if completely necessary.\"}]','B',NULL,'前文提到法国文化中的个人互动给作者留下了深刻印象，后文开始具体描述法国的亲吻礼。选项 B \'They differ a lot from those in the UK.\'（它们与英国的有很大不同）承接上文提到的英法文化差异，并引出下文对法国独特习俗的描述。',2,'英语二3',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1352,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · Success for 99 Cents】How do you sell things in a time when the economy is down and people just don\'t want to __(31)__? Try the 99 cent approach.\nSteve Jobs, former __32__ of Apple Computers, tried it and __33__ saved the music industry. He __34__ a standard price of 99 cents for each song that he wanted to sell on iTunes and built a successful music download company.\nIn the 1960s, Dave Gold __35__ a store that sold alcoholic drinks in southern California. He sold wine in three __36__ categories: $0.79, $0.99 and $1.49. When he saw that the 99 cent wine did best, he started selling the other two at the same price and sales went up. In 1982, he started __37__ 99 cent stores across the US. Today the company is __38__ almost 500 million dollars and has 280 shops.\nWhy does a 99 cent price tag (标签) make so much success? Researchers have found out that the price ending with 99 shows a __39__ price for consumers. It looks less and consumers __40__ feel that they can get something back.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"owned\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"market\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"set\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"worth\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"finally\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"several\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"buy\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"usually\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"boss\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"sell\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"lower\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"price\"}]','G',NULL,'根据句意“人们不想买”，选 buy。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1353,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Learning From Mistakes】Lots of people dare not make mistake (mistake). They fear they will be laughed at or __(41)__ (blame) by others. They fear they will lose their money and __42__ (belonging) or be under heavy stress But risks are __43__ (possible) to avoid and they do pave the way towards success. Have you ever __44__ (hear) of anyone who achieves success without','[]','blamed',NULL,'被动语态 be laughed at or (be) blamed。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1354,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Learning From Mistakes】Lots of people dare not make mistake (mistake). They fear they will be laughed at or __41__ (blame) by others. They fear they will lose their money and __42__ (belonging) or be under heavy stress But risks are __43__ (possible) to avoid and they do pave the way towards success. Have you ever __44__ (hear) of anyone who achieves success without making any mistakes?\nSo it is only __(45)__ (nature) that making mistakes should be considered a must. You shouldn\'t worry about that as you __46__ (probable) get lots of advantages out of your mistakes. By making mistakes, you can at least distinguish between the correct and the __47__ (correct) parts of what you did. Robert Stevenson once said: \"Our business in life is not to be __48__ (success), but to continue to fail in good spirits.\"\nYou needn\'t worry about anything as long as you keep on going by __49__ (wise) learning from your mistakes and __50__ (try) even harder.','[]','natural',NULL,'此处作表语，应填形容词形式。',1,'英语二3',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1355,4,NULL,'WRITING','某英文报社正在举办题为“Green Transportation”的征文活动，请你根据下述写作要点提交一篇英文短文应征：\n● 你怎样理解绿色出行？\n● 你会选择哪种绿色出行方式？\n● 给出理由。\n\n请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇 100 词左右的英文写作任务。','[]',NULL,'[\"解释绿色出行的概念（环保、低碳的交通方式）；\", \"说明自己选择的交通方式（如步行、骑自行车、乘坐公共交通等）；\", \"阐述选择该方式的理由（如减少污染、锻炼身体、节省费用等）。\"]','',3,'英语二3',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 19:46:34','2026-10-18 19:46:34'),(1356,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】\nThere\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\n1. French women are more stylish in the eyes of American women.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据文章第一段 \'They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate.\'（她们有一种美国女性长期以来一直试图模仿的时尚和酷的感觉），可知在美国人眼中法国女性更时尚。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1357,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nCaudalie is an American beauty brand.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第一段中 \'Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie...\' 可知，Caudalie 是一个法国美容品牌，而不是美国的。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1358,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nThomas thinks that beauty is a privilege for the young.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到 Thomas 认为美是一种长期的投资（lifelong and active investment），并没有提及美是年轻人的特权。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1359,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nThomas went to America to promote her beauty products.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第二段 \'In 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand.\' 可知她去美国是为了拓展品牌，即推广产品。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1360,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nAmerican women base their idea of beauty on pleasure.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第二段 \'She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure.\' 可知美国人的美容观念更多是关于痛苦而非快乐。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1361,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nFrench women share Thomas\' notion of beauty.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第二段末尾 \'In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\' 可知她和法国女性持有相同的美容观念。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1362,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nFrench women invest more in beauty products than before.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到法国人将美容视为一种终身投资（lifelong and active investment），但并未比较现在和以前在美容产品上的投入多少。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1363,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nAmerican women prefer a quick solution to their beauty problems.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据第三段 \'Thomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix\".\' 以及第四段提到的 \'tendency toward the quick solution\' 可知美国女性倾向于快速解决方案。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1364,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nAmerican women like Thomas\' beauty products.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到 Thomas 去美国拓展品牌并会见客户，但没有明确说明美国女性是否喜欢她的产品。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `question` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `type`, `stem`, `options`, `answer`, `answer_points`, `analysis`, `difficulty`, `source`, `source_year`, `score`, `status`, `ai_analysis`, `ai_analysis_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES (1365,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · A Long-term Investment or a Quick Fix】There\'s something about French women. They have a stylish and cool feel that American women have long been trying to imitate. The two countries have quite different approaches to beauty. Mathilde Thomas, co-founder of French beauty brand Caudalie, will explain the subject in her new book, The French Beauty Solution. She said the key to French beauty is the belief that \"beauty is something to give you pleasure. Because when you feel good, you look good.\"\n\nIn 2010, she went to the U.S. to expand her brand. She traveled all over the country meeting customers. She found that the American concept of beauty was more about pain than pleasure. Many women said they made their beauty choices based on the notion of \"no pain, no gain.\" They thought they had to suffer to be beautiful. In contrast, she and French women believe the notion of beauty should be pleasing to you.\n\nThomas\' book discusses how women in the U.S. are all about the \"quick fix.\" This means they will try a product that will instantly solve a beauty problem. They don\'t care if it hurts, is expensive, or is damaging in the long run. That\'s quite different from the French view of beauty. In the book, Thomas sees the French view as an essential and pleasing part of the day. It is also a lifelong and active investment that makes you look and feel good.\n\nIn the book, Thomas says, \"Our beauty routine is based on prevention and upkeep. And it is viewed as an essential, ongoing investment. What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution. Millions of American women consider beauty a priority in their daily routine. However, many of their habits are either too expensive, too painful, or simply not effective.\"\n\nAmerican women\'s beauty routine is based on prevention.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'根据最后一段 \'Our beauty routine is based on prevention... What I saw here was much more of a tendency toward the quick solution.\' 可知预防是法国人的习惯，而美国人倾向于快速解决。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1366,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Travel and Life】it was too late. One 86-year-old lady I talked to had spent her life close to home. With a sad look in her eyes, she told me: \"I always wanted to go to Hawaii, but I never made it. Oh, it\'s too late for me.\" \n\nI can hear some people saying: That\'s all well and good, but how can we afford it? The elders counter that argument by saying that travel is so rewarding that it should take precedence over other things younger people spend money on. The key is travel\'s value specifically for the young; it broadens their horizons, helps them to find a focus for their lives, and challenges them in new ways.\n\nOf course, travel is by no means only for the young. Seeing the world is also important in the middle 30 years and the last 30 years. Travel is just that important to feeling like your life has been well-lived.\n\n11. The writer of this text is most probably a _______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"technician\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"librarian\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"researcher\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"consultant\"}]','C',NULL,'文章讨论了旅行对不同年龄段人群的意义，引用了与老人的对话以及关于年轻人旅行的观点，这种探讨生活方式和价值观的文章通常出自研究者或专栏作家之手。Technician（技术员）和 Librarian（图书管理员）显然不符。Consultant（顾问）也有可能，但 Researcher（研究者/调查者）更符合文中那种通过访谈（\"One 86-year-old lady I talked to...\"）来收集素材并分析社会现象的语境。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1367,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Travel and Life】it was too late. One 86-year-old lady I talked to had spent her life close to home. With a sad look in her eyes, she told me: \"I always wanted to go to Hawaii, but I never made it. Oh, it\'s too late for me.\" \n\nI can hear some people saying: That\'s all well and good, but how can we afford it? The elders counter that argument by saying that travel is so rewarding that it should take precedence over other things younger people spend money on. The key is travel\'s value specifically for the young; it broadens their horizons, helps them to find a focus for their lives, and challenges them in new ways.\n\nOf course, travel is by no means only for the young. Seeing the world is also important in the middle 30 years and the last 30 years. Travel is just that important to feeling like your life has been well-lived.\n\n12. What can we infer about the old woman and her husband?','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They had many regrets in their life.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They traveled a lot before retirement.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"They made a big mistake in their work.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"They delayed travel until it was too late.\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第一段中老妇人的话 \"I always wanted to go to Hawaii, but I never made it. Oh, it\'s too late for me.\"（我一直想去夏威夷，但我从未成行。噢，对我来说太晚了。）可以推断出他们一直推迟旅行，直到为时已晚。选项 A 说有很多遗憾，虽然可能属实，但 D 更具体地对应了文中关于“旅行”这一主题的遗憾。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1368,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Travel and Life】it was too late. One 86-year-old lady I talked to had spent her life close to home. With a sad look in her eyes, she told me: \"I always wanted to go to Hawaii, but I never made it. Oh, it\'s too late for me.\" \n\nI can hear some people saying: That\'s all well and good, but how can we afford it? The elders counter that argument by saying that travel is so rewarding that it should take precedence over other things younger people spend money on. The key is travel\'s value specifically for the young; it broadens their horizons, helps them to find a focus for their lives, and challenges them in new ways.\n\nOf course, travel is by no means only for the young. Seeing the world is also important in the middle 30 years and the last 30 years. Travel is just that important to feeling like your life has been well-lived.\n\n13. According to Para.4, the elders think that younger people should _______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"give priority to travel\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"make time for their families\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"find a focus for their lives\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"work hard to save money\"}]','A',NULL,'题目问的是第四段（注：根据排版，这里指的应该是包含 \"The elders counter...\" 的那一段，即图片中的第二段正文）。文中提到 \"The elders counter that argument by saying that travel is so rewarding that it should take precedence over other things younger people spend money on.\"（长辈们反驳说，旅行非常有价值，应该优先于年轻人花钱的其他事情。）\"take precedence over\" 意为“优先于”，对应选项 A \"give priority to travel\"。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1369,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Travel and Life】it was too late. One 86-year-old lady I talked to had spent her life close to home. With a sad look in her eyes, she told me: \"I always wanted to go to Hawaii, but I never made it. Oh, it\'s too late for me.\" \n\nI can hear some people saying: That\'s all well and good, but how can we afford it? The elders counter that argument by saying that travel is so rewarding that it should take precedence over other things younger people spend money on. The key is travel\'s value specifically for the young; it broadens their horizons, helps them to find a focus for their lives, and challenges them in new ways.\n\nOf course, travel is by no means only for the young. Seeing the world is also important in the middle 30 years and the last 30 years. Travel is just that important to feeling like your life has been well-lived.\n\n14. The 86-year-old lady feels sad as she can no longer _______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"stay in Hawaii\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"go on a tour\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"live close to home\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"take care of herself\"}]','B',NULL,'根据第一段，老妇人想去夏威夷但没去成，现在觉得太晚了。她感到悲伤是因为无法再去旅行了。选项 B \"go on a tour\"（去旅行）符合文意。选项 A 是去夏威夷待着，虽然相关，但核心是她没能实现旅行的愿望；选项 C 和 D 文中未提及作为悲伤的原因。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1370,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Travel and Life】it was too late. One 86-year-old lady I talked to had spent her life close to home. With a sad look in her eyes, she told me: \"I always wanted to go to Hawaii, but I never made it. Oh, it\'s too late for me.\" \n\nI can hear some people saying: That\'s all well and good, but how can we afford it? The elders counter that argument by saying that travel is so rewarding that it should take precedence over other things younger people spend money on. The key is travel\'s value specifically for the young; it broadens their horizons, helps them to find a focus for their lives, and challenges them in new ways.\n\nOf course, travel is by no means only for the young. Seeing the world is also important in the middle 30 years and the last 30 years. Travel is just that important to feeling like your life has been well-lived.\n\n15. The writer of the text thinks that travel is a _______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"great midlife activity\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"challenge for the old\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"lifestyle for the young\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"lifelong engagement\"}]','D',NULL,'文章最后一段指出 \"travel is by no means only for the young\"（旅行绝不仅仅是年轻人的事），并且提到在人生的中间30年和最后30年看世界也很重要。这表明作者认为旅行贯穿人的一生，是一种终身的投入（lifelong engagement）。选项 A、B、C 都只涵盖了部分人群或片面观点。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1371,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】A pet treatment can solve all sorts of problems, says animal expert Arden Moore. Spending time around animals, like bird-watching, being accompanied by a therapy dog, or playing with a pet spider, can be good to your well-being. “There’s something about the animal kingdom that enables us to enjoy life a little better,” she says.\n\nTask 1: Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 1.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Animals help reduce your stress.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Animals improve human relationships.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Animals make your life more enjoyable.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Animals can change your way of life.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Animals help improve your eating habits.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Animals help lower your blood pressure.\"}]','C',NULL,'第一段提到与动物相处能让我们更享受生活（enjoy life a little better），对应选项 C。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1372,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】According to Moore, petting your cat or dog makes the animal happy, and it relaxes you as well. It is especially so when you are under some stress. “Give your dog or cat a head-to-tail rub by running hand over hand through the body,” she says. Your touch relaxes the animal. It also releases feel-good hormones(荷尔蒙) in you, and reduces your heart rate.\n\nTask 1: Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 2.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Animals help reduce your stress.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Animals improve human relationships.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Animals make your life more enjoyable.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Animals can change your way of life.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Animals help improve your eating habits.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Animals help lower your blood pressure.\"}]','A',NULL,'第二段主要讲抚摸宠物能让你放松，特别是在压力大时（under some stress），对应选项 A。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1373,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】Talking with animals may lower your blood pressure and improve your overall health. Moore suggests engaging animals in “happy talk,” or speaking in a cheerful tone. She says, “Happy talk or laughter around animals releases hormones in humans. Then, your blood pressure will be lowered. And animals will feel better too.”\n\nTask 1: Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 3.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Animals help reduce your stress.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Animals improve human relationships.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Animals make your life more enjoyable.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Animals can change your way of life.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Animals help improve your eating habits.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Animals help lower your blood pressure.\"}]','F',NULL,'第三段首句即点明主题：与动物交谈可能降低血压（lower your blood pressure），对应选项 F。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1374,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】Eating beside an animal may improve your eating habits. “In nursing homes, if there’s a fish tank where people are eating, seeing those fish actually motivates some residents to eat,” says Moore. The result of recent research supports the view. It shows that the people who ate near their pets improved some of their eating patterns.\n\nTask 1: Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 4.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Animals help reduce your stress.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Animals improve human relationships.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Animals make your life more enjoyable.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Animals can change your way of life.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Animals help improve your eating habits.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Animals help lower your blood pressure.\"}]','E',NULL,'第四段首句指出在动物旁边吃饭可能改善饮食习惯（improve your eating habits），对应选项 E。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1375,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】A good relationship with your animal friends may lead to better relations with humans. According to a study at the University of Michigan School of Nursing, observing animals in nature can teach valuable characteristics like patience, and help restore mental energy. Taking care of an animal can also teach responsibility and stimulate feelings of trust, openness, and companionship.\n\nTask 1: Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 5.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Animals help reduce your stress.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Animals improve human relationships.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Animals make your life more enjoyable.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Animals can change your way of life.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Animals help improve your eating habits.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Animals help lower your blood pressure.\"}]','B',NULL,'第五段首句说明与动物的良好关系可能导致更好的人际关系（better relations with humans），对应选项 B。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1376,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】A pet treatment can solve all sorts of problems, says animal expert Arden Moore. Spending time around animals, like bird-watching, being accompanied by a therapy dog, or playing with a pet spider, can be good to your well-being. “There’s something about the animal kingdom that enables us to enjoy life a little better,” she says.\n\nAccording to Moore, petting your cat or dog makes the animal happy, and it relaxes you as well. It is especially so when you are under some stress. “Give your dog or cat a head-to-tail rub by running hand over hand through the body,” she says. Your touch relaxes the animal. It also releases feel-good hormones(荷尔蒙) in you, and reduces your heart rate.\n\nTalking with animals may lower your blood pressure and improve your overall health. Moore suggests engaging animals in “happy talk,” or speaking in a cheerful tone. She says, “Happy talk or laughter around animals releases hormones in humans. Then, your blood pressure will be lowered. And animals will feel better too.”\n\nEating beside an animal may improve your eating habits. “In nursing homes, if there’s a fish tank where people are eating, seeing those fish actually motivates some residents to eat,” says Moore. The result of recent research supports the view. It shows that the people who ate near their pets improved some of their eating patterns.\n\nA good relationship with your animal friends may lead to better relations with humans. According to a study at the University of Michigan School of Nursing, observing animals in nature can teach valuable characteristics like patience, and help restore mental energy. Taking care of an animal can also teach responsibility and stimulate feelings of trust, openness, and companionship.\n\nTask 2\n21. Playing with your pet is good ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in nature\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"if you keep a pet\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to your well-being\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"when you talk with it\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"you’ll have a better appetite\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"your heart rate will be reduced\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第一段 \'Spending time around animals... can be good to your well-being\'，可知玩耍对身心健康有益。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1377,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】A pet treatment can solve all sorts of problems, says animal expert Arden Moore. Spending time around animals, like bird-watching, being accompanied by a therapy dog, or playing with a pet spider, can be good to your well-being. “There’s something about the animal kingdom that enables us to enjoy life a little better,” she says.\n\nAccording to Moore, petting your cat or dog makes the animal happy, and it relaxes you as well. It is especially so when you are under some stress. “Give your dog or cat a head-to-tail rub by running hand over hand through the body,” she says. Your touch relaxes the animal. It also releases feel-good hormones(荷尔蒙) in you, and reduces your heart rate.\n\nTalking with animals may lower your blood pressure and improve your overall health. Moore suggests engaging animals in “happy talk,” or speaking in a cheerful tone. She says, “Happy talk or laughter around animals releases hormones in humans. Then, your blood pressure will be lowered. And animals will feel better too.”\n\nEating beside an animal may improve your eating habits. “In nursing homes, if there’s a fish tank where people are eating, seeing those fish actually motivates some residents to eat,” says Moore. The result of recent research supports the view. It shows that the people who ate near their pets improved some of their eating patterns.\n\nA good relationship with your animal friends may lead to better relations with humans. According to a study at the University of Michigan School of Nursing, observing animals in nature can teach valuable characteristics like patience, and help restore mental energy. Taking care of an animal can also teach responsibility and stimulate feelings of trust, openness, and companionship.\n\nTask 2\n22. When you’re petting your pet, ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in nature\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"if you keep a pet\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to your well-being\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"when you talk with it\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"you’ll have a better appetite\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"your heart rate will be reduced\"}]','F',NULL,'根据第二段 \'It also releases feel-good hormones... and reduces your heart rate\'，可知抚摸宠物会降低心率。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1378,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Anim