 \"E\", \"text\": \"you’ll have a better appetite\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"your heart rate will be reduced\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第三段 \'And animals will feel better too\'（在谈论与动物说话之后），可知当你对它说话时它会感到快乐。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1379,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】A pet treatment can solve all sorts of problems, says animal expert Arden Moore. Spending time around animals, like bird-watching, being accompanied by a therapy dog, or playing with a pet spider, can be good to your well-being. “There’s something about the animal kingdom that enables us to enjoy life a little better,” she says.\n\nAccording to Moore, petting your cat or dog makes the animal happy, and it relaxes you as well. It is especially so when you are under some stress. “Give your dog or cat a head-to-tail rub by running hand over hand through the body,” she says. Your touch relaxes the animal. It also releases feel-good hormones(荷尔蒙) in you, and reduces your heart rate.\n\nTalking with animals may lower your blood pressure and improve your overall health. Moore suggests engaging animals in “happy talk,” or speaking in a cheerful tone. She says, “Happy talk or laughter around animals releases hormones in humans. Then, your blood pressure will be lowered. And animals will feel better too.”\n\nEating beside an animal may improve your eating habits. “In nursing homes, if there’s a fish tank where people are eating, seeing those fish actually motivates some residents to eat,” says Moore. The result of recent research supports the view. It shows that the people who ate near their pets improved some of their eating patterns.\n\nA good relationship with your animal friends may lead to better relations with humans. According to a study at the University of Michigan School of Nursing, observing animals in nature can teach valuable characteristics like patience, and help restore mental energy. Taking care of an animal can also teach responsibility and stimulate feelings of trust, openness, and companionship.\n\nTask 2\n24. Eating near your pet, ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in nature\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"if you keep a pet\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to your well-being\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"when you talk with it\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"you’ll have a better appetite\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"your heart rate will be reduced\"}]','E',NULL,'根据第四段 \'Eating beside an animal may improve your eating habits... motivates some residents to eat\'，可知在宠物旁吃饭能增进食欲。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1380,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · Benefits of Spending Time with Animals】A pet treatment can solve all sorts of problems, says animal expert Arden Moore. Spending time around animals, like bird-watching, being accompanied by a therapy dog, or playing with a pet spider, can be good to your well-being. “There’s something about the animal kingdom that enables us to enjoy life a little better,” she says.\n\nAccording to Moore, petting your cat or dog makes the animal happy, and it relaxes you as well. It is especially so when you are under some stress. “Give your dog or cat a head-to-tail rub by running hand over hand through the body,” she says. Your touch relaxes the animal. It also releases feel-good hormones(荷尔蒙) in you, and reduces your heart rate.\n\nTalking with animals may lower your blood pressure and improve your overall health. Moore suggests engaging animals in “happy talk,” or speaking in a cheerful tone. She says, “Happy talk or laughter around animals releases hormones in humans. Then, your blood pressure will be lowered. And animals will feel better too.”\n\nEating beside an animal may improve your eating habits. “In nursing homes, if there’s a fish tank where people are eating, seeing those fish actually motivates some residents to eat,” says Moore. The result of recent research supports the view. It shows that the people who ate near their pets improved some of their eating patterns.\n\nA good relationship with your animal friends may lead to better relations with humans. According to a study at the University of Michigan School of Nursing, observing animals in nature can teach valuable characteristics like patience, and help restore mental energy. Taking care of an animal can also teach responsibility and stimulate feelings of trust, openness, and companionship.\n\nTask 2\n25. You may develop your patience by watching animals ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"in nature\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"if you keep a pet\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"to your well-being\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"when you talk with it\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"you’ll have a better appetite\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"your heart rate will be reduced\"}]','A',NULL,'根据第五段 \'observing animals in nature can teach valuable characteristics like patience\'，可知观察自然中的动物可以培养耐心。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1381,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · What is Green Tourism?】The aim of green tourism is to protect the environment and culture of an area. There are many choices for green tourism worldwide.\n\nThe number of tourists has been increasing these days. It makes green tourism a must in some areas. In order to protect the environment, it might seem wiser to ban tourists to these areas. But many areas need the income from tourism for their local economy. Green tourism offers the best solution to both. __(26)__ At the same time, it keeps local businesses growing.\n\nGreen tourism might not mean a vacation spent with little or no comfort. _27_ Green tourism resorts exist in almost every style and taste. From recycling systems to tree houses, there are many vacation choices.\n\nOn a green holiday, people study the local plants and culture. _28_ Guides, tours and wildlife-viewing platforms help people experience a lot. But little or no impact is made on the environment. Sometimes, tourists can take an active part in improving the local area. They can work to protect the wildlife in the area. They can help to build a school. _29_ These vacations can be a lot of work. But people find them very rewarding and interesting.\n\nNowadays, green tourism is becoming more popular. _30_ More areas will take steps to have less of an impact on the environment, allowing tourists to enjoy the beauty that these areas have to offer for many years to come.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They also learn ways to protect them.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It protects the environment of an area.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"They can do other things that are good for the area.\"}]','B',NULL,'前文提到绿色旅游是解决环保和经济需求的最佳方案，后文说同时保持当地商业增长。选项 B“它保护了该地区的环境”与前文的“solution to both”呼应，且符合逻辑。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1382,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · The Word \"Try\"】\nThe word \"try\" is a small word yet it has an amazing impact upon us. If someone says, \"I\'ll try to do that,\" you __(31)__ that they will not put their whole __(32)__ into it, and may not even do it at all. How __(33)__ do you use the word \"try\" when talking about the things that __(34)__ to you?\n\nThink about something that you would like to __(35)__, say it to yourself in two __(36)__ ways, and see how you feel. Firstly say, \"I\'ll try to...\", and __(37)__ say, \"I will do...\"\n\nThe latter makes you feel __(38)__ than the former, right? It gives you a sense of __(39)__. Listen to the people around you. When they say they will try, notice if it gets done or not. Eliminate the word \"try\" from your __(40)__ and see how your life improves.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"matter\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"different\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"determination\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"only\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"achieve\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"know\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"smart\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"next\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"often\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"better\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"dictionary\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"heart\"}]','F',NULL,'根据句意“如果你说‘我试试’，你会知道他们不会全力以赴”，此处应填动词 know。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1383,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Communication in Groups】\nThe number of people in a group influences (influence) the quality of communication. Consider the __(41)__ (differ) between communication between two friends and communication in a group. When two friends talk, there are __(42)__ (simple) two people sending and receiving messages. In a group, there are several people __(43)__ (do) the same thing. Each idea one expresses must be __(44)__ (understand) by all others. Thus, the __(45)__ (great)','[]','difference',NULL,'the 后面接名词形式，differ 的名词是 difference。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1384,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【Communication in Groups】The number of people in a group influences (influence) the quality of communication. Consider the __(41)__ (differ) between communication between two friends and communication in a group. When two friends talk, there are __(42)__ (simple) two people sending and receiving messages. In a group, there are several people __(43)__ (do) the same thing. Each idea one expresses must be __(44)__ (understand) by all others. Thus, the __(45)__ (great) the number of people in a group, the fewer __(46)__ (contribution) a member may make. So, you may think that small groups would be better. However, with too few members, a group has __(47)__ (limit) resources. This __(48)__ (affect) the advantage of groups for making a __(49)__ (decide). Also, in a very small group, the members may be __(50)__ (willing) to criticize others. So, I believe that five to seven members is the ideal size for a group.','[]','contributions',NULL,'fewer修饰可数名词复数，故填 contributions。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1385,4,NULL,'WRITING','某英文报社正在举办题为“Starting from Ourselves to Save Electricity”的征文活动。请你根据下述写作要点提交一篇英文短文应征，内容包括：\n• 当前我国电力资源短缺。\n• 如何从小事做起，节约用电。','[]',NULL,'[\"描述当前我国电力资源短缺的现状。\", \"提出具体的节约用电措施（如随手关灯、使用节能电器等）。\", \"呼吁大家从自己做起，从小事做起。\"]','',3,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1386,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】The first record of a public place serving coffee dates back to 1475. Kiva Han was the first coffee shop, located in Istanbul, Türkiye.\n\nKiva Han was the world\'s oldest coffee house.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'根据原文，Kiva Han是第一家咖啡店（first coffee shop），且时间可追溯到1475年，因此它是世界上最古老的咖啡馆。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1387,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】It was even legal in Türkiye for a woman to divorce her husband if he could not supply her with enough coffee.\n\nTurkish men often bought coffee as a gift for the marriage proposal.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'原文提到如果丈夫不能提供足够的咖啡，妻子可以合法离婚，但并未提及土耳其男人经常买咖啡作为求婚礼物。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1388,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】The idea of adding cream and sugar to coffee came into fashion in Europe around 1529...\n\nIt was in Europe that people started to add cream to coffee.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'原文明确指出在咖啡中添加奶油和糖的想法是在欧洲开始流行的。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1389,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】An Austrian... introduced the idea of filtering(过滤) coffee, as well as softening coffee with milk and sugar.\n\nThe Turkish people enjoyed having their coffee black.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'原文提到奥地利人引入了加奶加糖的喝法，暗示之前可能不加，但并没有直接陈述土耳其人喜欢喝黑咖啡这一事实。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1390,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】Vienna was invaded by the Turkish army. They left many bags of coffee beans behind when they fled the city.\n\nCoffee beans were first brought to Europe as a gift from Türkiye.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'原文说咖啡豆是土耳其军队逃离维也纳时留下的（left behind），而不是作为礼物带来的。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1391,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】The idea of adding cream and sugar to coffee came into fashion in Europe around 1529, when the first coffee house in Europe was established.\n\nBefore 1529, there were many coffee houses in Europe.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'原文指出1529年建立了欧洲第一家咖啡馆，所以在此之前不可能有很多咖啡馆。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1392,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】A jar with a sign reading \"To Insure Prompt Service\" sat on the counter. You put a coin in the jar to be served quickly.\n\nThe British started tipping in order to get served more quickly.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'原文解释了小费（tips）一词源于“为了确保快速服务”（To Insure Prompt Service），顾客投币是为了快点被服务。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1393,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】The British called their coffee houses \"penny universities,\" because that was the price for the coffee and the social upper-class of businessmen were found there.\n\nMany coffee houses were opened in British universities.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'原文称咖啡馆为“便士大学”是因为花一个便士喝咖啡就能接触到上流社会的商人，学到东西，并不是说大学里开了很多咖啡馆。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1394,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】The role of the American coffee houses was the same as that in England: hotspots for the business community.\n\nAmerican businessmen often met at coffee houses.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'原文提到美国咖啡馆的角色与英国相同，是商业社区的热点场所（hotspots for the business community），意味着商人们常在那里聚会。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1395,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The History of Coffee Houses】And who could forget the most popular coffee house chain of all, Starbucks? They opened their first store in 1971, in Seattle...\n\nStarbucks opened its first coffee house in 1652.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'原文明确说明星巴克的第一家店开在1971年，而1652年是英国第一家咖啡馆开业的时间。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1396,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The History of Cats】10,000 years ago, farmers began storing grain. The grain attracted mice. Cats could help out with that.\n\nThe same type of cats also ruled in Ancient Egypt. They left their traces in statues and paintings. Researchers wondered how these two separate lines led to today\'s worldwide success of cats. Unlike other archaeologists(考古学家), Eva-Maria Geigl studied DNA instead of bones.\n\nCombining the genetic information with other records, the researchers figured out the cats\' paths. After cats befriended(亲近) the Near East farmers, they began to appear on farms in other places. One example is a 9,500-year-old cat buried in a human grave on the island of Cyprus. There were no wild cats on the island. They must have come from somewhere else. Humans must have brought them on a boat.\n\nA second wave of cats began living with humans in Egypt 2,500 years ago. The new study shows that during Roman times, these Egyptian cats also began expanding through the Mediterranean(地中海). They mixed with the Near East cats and then went farther. They went through Europe and into Southwest Asia.\n\nWhen the Viking age began, the expansion of Egyptian cat families exploded. It was likely due to the popularity of using ship cats to kill rats. \"Rats on ships not only eat and spoil the food, they also destroy the ropes, so rats could be a disaster for sailors,\" says Geigl. \"Cats prevent these types of disasters.\"\n\n11. The first cats were believed to come from ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Egypt\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"the Far East\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"the Near East\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"East Asia\"}]','C',NULL,'根据文中第三段第一句 \'After cats befriended the Near East farmers...\' 可知，第一批猫被认为来自近东地区。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1397,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The History of Cats】10,000 years ago, farmers began storing grain. The grain attracted mice. Cats could help out with that.\n\nThe same type of cats also ruled in Ancient Egypt. They left their traces in statues and paintings. Researchers wondered how these two separate lines led to today\'s worldwide success of cats. Unlike other archaeologists(考古学家), Eva-Maria Geigl studied DNA instead of bones.\n\nCombining the genetic information with other records, the researchers figured out the cats\' paths. One example is a 9,500-year-old cat buried in a human grave on the island of Cyprus. There were no wild cats on the island. They must have come from somewhere else. Humans must have brought them on a boat.\n\nA second wave of cats began living with humans in Egypt 2,500 years ago. The new study shows that during Roman times, these Egyptian cats also began expanding through the Mediterranean(地中海). They mixed with the Near East cats and then went farther. They went through Europe and into Southwest Asia.\n\nWhen the Viking age began, the expansion of Egyptian cat families exploded. It was likely due to the popularity of using ship cats to kill rats. \"Rats on ships not only eat and spoil the food, they also destroy the ropes, so rats could be a disaster for sailors,\" says Geigl. \"Cats prevent these types of disasters.\"\n\n12. How does Geigl study the spread of cats?','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"By following their traces.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"By analyzing their statues.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"By examining their bones.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"By testing their DNA.\"}]','D',NULL,'根据文中第二段最后一句 \'Unlike other archaeologists..., Eva-Maria Geigl studied DNA instead of bones.\' 可知她是研究DNA的。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1398,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The History of Cats】10,000 years ago, farmers began storing grain. The grain attracted mice. Cats could help out with that.\n\nThe same type of cats also ruled in Ancient Egypt. They left their traces in statues and paintings. Researchers wondered how these two separate lines led to today\'s worldwide success of cats. Unlike other archaeologists(考古学家), Eva-Maria Geigl studied DNA instead of bones.\n\nCombining the genetic information with other records, the researchers figured out the cats\' paths. After cats befriended(亲近) the Near East farmers, they began to appear on farms in other places. One example is a 9,500-year-old cat buried in a human grave on the island of Cyprus. There were no wild cats on the island. They must have come from somewhere else. Humans must have brought them on a boat.\n\nA second wave of cats began living with humans in Egypt 2,500 years ago. The new study shows that during Roman times, these Egyptian cats also began expanding through the Mediterranean(地中海). They mixed with the Near East cats and then went farther. They went through Europe and into Southwest Asia.\n\nWhen the Viking age began, the expansion of Egyptian cat families exploded. It was likely due to the popularity of using ship cats to kill rats. \"Rats on ships not only eat and spoil the food, they also destroy the ropes, so rats could be a disaster for sailors,\" says Geigl. \"Cats prevent these types of disasters.\"\n\n13. The cat found in the Cyprus grave was probably ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"born on the island\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"brought to the island\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"the world\'s first wild cat\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"the world\'s first pet cat\"}]','B',NULL,'根据文中第三段最后两句 \'There were no wild cats on the island... Humans must have brought them on a boat.\' 可知这只猫是被带到岛上的。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1399,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The History of Cats】10,000 years ago, farmers began storing grain. The grain attracted mice. Cats could help out with that.\n\nThe same type of cats also ruled in Ancient Egypt. They left their traces in statues and paintings. Researchers wondered how these two separate lines led to today\'s worldwide success of cats. Unlike other archaeologists(考古学家), Eva-Maria Geigl studied DNA instead of bones.\n\nCombining the genetic information with other records, the researchers figured out the cats\' paths. After cats befriended(亲近) the Near East farmers, they began to appear on farms in other places. One example is a 9,500-year-old cat buried in a human grave on the island of Cyprus. There were no wild cats on the island. They must have come from somewhere else. Humans must have brought them on a boat.\n\nA second wave of cats began living with humans in Egypt 2,500 years ago. The new study shows that during Roman times, these Egyptian cats also began expanding through the Mediterranean(地中海). They mixed with the Near East cats and then went farther. They went through Europe and into Southwest Asia.\n\nWhen the Viking age began, the expansion of Egyptian cat families exploded. It was likely due to the popularity of using ship cats to kill rats. \"Rats on ships not only eat and spoil the food, they also destroy the ropes, so rats could be a disaster for sailors,\" says Geigl. \"Cats prevent these types of disasters.\"\n\n14. The cats in Southwest Asia were originally from ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Egypt\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Cyprus\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Europe\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"the Mediterranean\"}]','A',NULL,'根据文中第四段 \'A second wave of cats began living with humans in Egypt... These Egyptian cats also began expanding... They went through Europe and into Southwest Asia.\' 可知源自埃及。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1400,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · The History of Cats】10,000 years ago, farmers began storing grain. The grain attracted mice. Cats could help out with that.\n\nThe same type of cats also ruled in Ancient Egypt. They left their traces in statues and paintings. Researchers wondered how these two separate lines led to today\'s worldwide success of cats. Unlike other archaeologists(考古学家), Eva-Maria Geigl studied DNA instead of bones.\n\nCombining the genetic information with other records, the researchers figured out the cats\' paths. After cats befriended(亲近) the Near East farmers, they began to appear on farms in other places. One example is a 9,500-year-old cat buried in a human grave on the island of Cyprus. There were no wild cats on the island. They must have come from somewhere else. Humans must have brought them on a boat.\n\nA second wave of cats began living with humans in Egypt 2,500 years ago. The new study shows that during Roman times, these Egyptian cats also began expanding through the Mediterranean(地中海). They mixed with the Near East cats and then went farther. They went through Europe and into Southwest Asia.\n\nWhen the Viking age began, the expansion of Egyptian cat families exploded. It was likely due to the popularity of using ship cats to kill rats. \"Rats on ships not only eat and spoil the food, they also destroy the ropes, so rats could be a disaster for sailors,\" says Geigl. \"Cats prevent these types of disasters.\"\n\n15. Who contributed most to the spread of cats during the Viking age?','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Researchers.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Painters.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Farmers.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Sailors.\"}]','D',NULL,'根据文中最后一段提到的 \'ship cats\', \'rats could be a disaster for sailors\' 以及维京时代航海背景，可知是海员(sailors)促进了猫的传播。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1401,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · The Pony Express】\n① In 1848, gold was found in California. Thousands of people rushed there. But the train line to California wasn\'t finished until 1869. It took a long time to ride a horse from California to Missouri. What would you do if you wanted to send a message? Well, you could use the Pony Express.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ①:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The end of riders\' business\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The fastest message service\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The comfortable home station\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The effective system to send mail\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Safe delivery despite the tough ride\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Need of message exchange in the gold rush\"}]','F',NULL,'第一段提到淘金热（gold rush）导致人们涌向加州，且当时交通不便，引出传递信息的需求。选项 F \'淘金热中交换信息的需要\' 符合段意。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1402,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · The Pony Express】\n② In 1860 and 1861, the Pony Express was the fastest way to get news to and from the West. The road was around 2,000 miles long. It took most people weeks or months to ride that far. The Pony Express could make it in just 10 days. Those speeds were unheard of then. How did they do it? Well, they had a good system.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ②:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The end of riders\' business\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The fastest message service\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The comfortable home station\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The effective system to send mail\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Safe delivery despite the tough ride\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Need of message exchange in the gold rush\"}]','B',NULL,'第二段首句即指出 \'the Pony Express was the fastest way to get news...\'，强调其速度之快。选项 B \'最快的消息服务\' 符合段意。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1403,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · The Pony Express】\n③ The Pony Express had 184 stations along the road. The stations were about 10 miles apart. This is about how far a horse could run before tired. The rider would switch to a new horse at each station. Every 75~100 miles, the rider would get to a home station, where riders would rest. Before resting, he would give his mail bag to a new rider. The mail never stopped moving, while the horses and riders rested.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ③:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The end of riders\' business\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The fastest message service\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The comfortable home station\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The effective system to send mail\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Safe delivery despite the tough ride\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Need of message exchange in the gold rush\"}]','D',NULL,'第三段详细描述了驿站设置、换马、交接邮件的流程，展示了其运作机制。选项 D \'寄递邮件的有效系统\' 符合段意。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1404,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · The Pony Express】\n④ It was tough to ride for the Pony Express. Each rider had to weigh less than 125 pounds. Speed was the key. Most riders were teenage boys. They rode up to 100 miles a day. The ride could be dangerous. Attacks by local people were common. But in its running time, the Pony Express lost only one mail bag.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ④:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The end of riders\' business\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The fastest message service\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The comfortable home station\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The effective system to send mail\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Safe delivery despite the tough ride\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Need of message exchange in the gold rush\"}]','E',NULL,'第四段提到骑行艰难（tough）、危险（dangerous），但只丢失了一个邮包（lost only one mail bag）。选项 E \'尽管骑行艰难仍安全送达\' 符合段意。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1405,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · The Pony Express】\n⑤ The Pony Express filled an important role for a time, but it did not last. The Civil War started in 1861. Things got worse when the first telegraph line to California was finished later that year. People could send messages by telegraph instantly. Soon the Pony Express closed. But the story of the brave riders lives on.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ⑤:','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The end of riders\' business\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The fastest message service\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The comfortable home station\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The effective system to send mail\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Safe delivery despite the tough ride\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"Need of message exchange in the gold rush\"}]','A',NULL,'第五段讲述了电报的出现导致 Pony Express 关闭（closed）。选项 A \'骑手业务的终结\' 符合段意。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1406,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · The Pony Express】\nIn 1848, gold was found in California. Thousands of people rushed there. But the train line to California wasn\'t finished until 1869. It took a long time to ride a horse from California to Missouri. What would you do if you wanted to send a message? Well, you could use the Pony Express.\n\nIn 1860 and 1861, the Pony Express was the fastest way to get news to and from the West. The road was around 2,000 miles long. It took most people weeks or months to ride that far. The Pony Express could make it in just 10 days. Those speeds were unheard of then. How did they do it? Well, they had a good system.\n\nThe Pony Express had 184 stations along the road. The stations were about 10 miles apart. This is about how far a horse could run before tired. The rider would switch to a new horse at each station. Every 75~100 miles, the rider would get to a home station, where riders would rest. Before resting, he would give his mail bag to a new rider. The mail never stopped moving, while the horses and riders rested.\n\nIt was tough to ride for the Pony Express. Each rider had to weigh less than 125 pounds. Speed was the key. Most riders were teenage boys. They rode up to 100 miles a day. The ride could be dangerous. Attacks by local people were common. But in its running time, the Pony Express lost only one mail bag.\n\nThe Pony Express filled an important role for a time, but it did not last. The Civil War started in 1861. Things got worse when the first telegraph line to California was finished later that year. People could send messages by telegraph instantly. Soon the Pony Express closed. But the story of the brave riders lives on.\n\n21. People rushed to California ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"only ten days\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"for a better life\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"a couple of months\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"be young and brave\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"switch horses and riders\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"after the outbreak of the Civil War\"}]','B',NULL,'根据常识及文中提到的淘金热背景，人们涌向加利福尼亚是为了更好的生活（gold rush）。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1407,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · The Pony Express】(同上)\n\n22. To ride 2,000 miles took the Pony Express ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"only ten days\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"for a better life\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"a couple of months\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"be young and brave\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"switch horses and riders\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"after the outbreak of the Civil War\"}]','A',NULL,'文中第二段提到 \'The Pony Express could make it in just 10 days.\'。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1408,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · The Pony Express】(同上)\n\n23. There were adequate stations to ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"only ten days\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"for a better life\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"a couple of months\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"be young and brave\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"switch horses and riders\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"after the outbreak of the Civil War\"}]','E',NULL,'文中第三段描述了驿站的作用：骑手换马（switch to a new horse），在家庭驿站换人休息（give his mail bag to a new rider）。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1409,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · The Pony Express】(同上)\n\n24. Most riders had to ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"only ten days\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"for a better life\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"a couple of months\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"be young and brave\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"switch horses and riders\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"after the outbreak of the Civil War\"}]','D',NULL,'文中第四段提到 \'Most riders were teenage boys\' (young) 且 \'The ride could be dangerous... Attacks... were common\' (brave)。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1410,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · The Pony Express】(同上)\n\n25. The telegraph appeared ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"only ten days\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"for a better life\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"a couple of months\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"be young and brave\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"switch horses and riders\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"after the outbreak of the Civil War\"}]','F',NULL,'文中最后一段提到 \'The Civil War started in 1861. Things got worse when the first telegraph line to California was finished later that year.\'。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1411,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Work is a Blessing】\nI grew up in Lakeland, LA, one of 12 children. We all lived on my parents\' farm. We grew cotton, corn and had a large garden, but it didn\'t bring in much cash. __(26)__ We milked 65 cows at 5 in the morning and again at 2 in the afternoon, seven days a week.\n\nOne Saturday before daylight, I remember complaining to my father and grandfather about having to milk those cows. My father said, \"You know, boy, to work is a blessing.\" __(27)__ However, it took many years before it sank in.\n\nGoing to college was a rare privilege for a kid from Lakeland. __(28)__ So I joined the ROTC program to help pay for college. And what started out as an obligation to the Army became a way of life that I stayed committed to for 37 years, three months and three days.\n\nIn the late 1980s, during a visit to Bangladesh, I saw a woman with a baby on her back, breaking bricks with a hammer. I asked a Bangladesh military officer why they weren\'t using a machine, which would have been a lot easier. __(29)__ Breaking those bricks meant she could earn enough money to feed herself and her baby that day. And as bad as that woman\'s job was, it was enough to keep a small family alive. __(30)__','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I don\'t think I will ever quit working.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"However, I still wanted to go to college.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"He told me a machine would put that lady out of work.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I had a feeling I had been told something really important.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"It reminded me of my father\'s words: To work is a blessing.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"So when I was 12, I got a part-time job helping to milk cows.\"}]','F',NULL,'前文提到家里缺钱，后文提到挤奶的具体时间，选项 F 提到 12 岁时找了一份帮忙挤奶的兼职工作，承上启下。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1412,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Work is a Blessing】(同上)','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I don\'t think I will ever quit working.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"However, I still wanted to go to college.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"He told me a machine would put that lady out of work.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"I had a feeling I had been told something really important.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"It reminded me of my father\'s words: To work is a blessing.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"So when I was 12, I got a part-time job helping to milk cows.\"}]','D',NULL,'父亲说了一句富有哲理的话，作者当时虽然抱怨，但有一种直觉觉得这是很重要的话（something really important），随后才说花了很多年才真正理解（sank in）。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1413,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · The Impact of Artificial Intelligence (人工智能) on Jobs】\nAs you grew up, there\'s a good chance you heard the saying \"go to a good school, get a good job, and make lots of money.\" On the surface, that seems like __(31)__ advice. After all, college graduates, on __32__, earn almost $1 million more in their lifetime than those with __33__ a high school education.\n\nPerhaps you were encouraged to earn a professional degree to __34__ a high-paying job like a doctor, dentist, lawyer or something __35__. This also seems like great advice. A professional degree holder __36__ earns more than $2 million more in their lifetime than the average college graduate. But that was then, not now.\n\nThanks to rapid __37__ in artificial intelligence, jobs are falling to machines. And it\'s not just blue-collar jobs that are being taken __38__ by automation (自动化). It\'s white-collar professions as well.\n\nThe safe, high paying jobs of the past are starting to look much less secure. If you\'re currently in one of the professions of finance, __39__ or law, or going to school to get into these fields, you should __40__ twice before continuing.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"get\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"called\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"similar\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"think\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"medicine\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"over\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"average\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"valuable\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"only\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"use\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"usually\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"development\"}]','H',NULL,'句意：表面上看，这似乎是宝贵的建议。valuable (宝贵的/有价值的) 符合语境。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1414,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Dutch King\'s Secret Life】\nNext time you fly, the pilot might (may) be a king. Dutch King Willem-Alexander has __(41)__ (secret) been flying planes twice a month for twenty-one __42__ (year). His passengers were __43__ (aware) of this. The 50-year-old king __44__ (get) his military pilot\'s license with the Dutch Air Force in his twenties. He loved flying and __45__ (become)','[]','secretly',NULL,'修饰动词 been flying，需用副词形式 secretly。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1415,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Dutch King\'s Secret Life】... a commercial pilot. The king is now __(46)__ (train) to fly Boeing 737 because he wants to upgrade his skills.\n\nThe king said flying could relieve his pressure. He explained: \"You can\'t take your problems from the ground into the skies. You can leave them aside __47__ (complete) and concentrate on something else. That is the most __48__ (relax) part of flying.\" He said it was easy to keep his secret. Few people __49__ (know) he was their pilot. He always welcomed passengers on behalf of the captain and the crew. So far he has never __50__ (tell) passengers his name.','[]','being trained',NULL,'考查被动语态和进行时。主语 The king 与 train 之间是被动关系，且句中有 now，表示现在正在进行的动作，故用现在进行时的被动语态 be being done。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1416,4,NULL,'WRITING','某英文报社正在举行题为“No Smoking in Public Places”的征文活动。请你根据下述写作要点提交一篇英文短文应征：\n• 公共场所吸烟有什么危害？\n• 你能为公共场所禁烟做些什么？','[]',NULL,'[\"阐述公共场所吸烟的危害（如二手烟对他人健康的损害、引发火灾等）。\", \"说明个人能采取的行动（如自己不在公共场所吸烟、劝阻他人吸烟、宣传禁烟知识等）。\", \"语言流畅，逻辑清晰，字数在100词左右。\"]','',3,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1417,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · The Magic of Tidying Up】If you haven\'t worn your shoes lately, thank them for their hard work and consider letting them go. \"It is natural for me to say thank-you to the goods that support us,\" says Marie Kondo, the author of The Life-Changing Magic of Tidying Up. Her method of connecting with belongings that \"spark joy\" and saying goodbye to the rest is popular all over the world.\n\nKondo\'s method encourages a one-time rapid and dramatic organizing event. For her, tidying is to thank anything that doesn\'t \"spark joy\" and send them to a more appreciative owner. The results can be life-changing. People suddenly find themselves surrounded by things that provide clarity(简洁). Even her book, Kondo says, should be thrown away when it\'s no longer needed.\n\nKondo suggested starting with clothes, then books, then documents, and last and most difficult, photos and mementos(纪念品). Instead of deciding what to get rid of, she says, the focus should be on what to keep: things that spark joy or are truly necessary.\n\nAfter joyfully sending away mountains of unneeded or unloved belongings, Kondo turns to organizing what is left. The key is storing things mostly in drawers, arranged so that everything can be seen at a glance and nothing is stacked. So T-shirts and socks (the ones you\'ve kept because they make you happy) are rolled and arranged beautifully.\n\nKondo has been fond of tidying since she was five, enjoying arranging shoes and pencils while other kids played outside. She believes the inside of a house should be a place where there are no unnecessary things, and our thoughts become clear. It is the place where we appreciate all the things that support us. It is where we review and rethink about ourselves.\n\n1. Kondo wrote a book to help people make their home tidy.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中提到她是《The Life-Changing Magic of Tidying Up》的作者，且该书内容关于整理和丢弃不需要的物品，故推断她写书是为了帮助人们整理家居。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1418,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','2. The Life-Changing Magic of Tidying Up is a bestseller.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中仅提到她的方法在世界各地很受欢迎（popular all over the world），并未明确提及该书是畅销书（bestseller）。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:08','2026-10-18 21:59:08'),(1419,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','3. Kondo\'s method encourages slow and gradual organizing.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'第二段第一句明确指出：\'Kondo\'s method encourages a one-time rapid and dramatic organizing event.\'（鼓励一次性快速且戏剧性的整理活动），与题干中的\'slow and gradual\'相反。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1420,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','4. Most people throw Kondo\'s book away after reading it.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到 Kondo 说即使是她自己的书，不再需要时也应该扔掉，但这是一种建议或原则，并未陈述大多数人读完书后真的把书扔掉了这一事实。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1421,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','5. Kondo says clothes are the items to be thrown away first.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'第三段提到 \'starting with clothes\'，但紧接着解释 \'Instead of deciding what to get rid of... the focus should be on what to keep\'。即从衣服开始整理，目的是决定保留哪些，而不是先扔掉衣服。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1422,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','6. Deciding what to send away is more important than what to keep.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'第三段最后一句指出 \'the focus should be on what to keep\'（重点应该放在保留什么上），这与题干所述相反。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1423,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','7. T-shirts should be kept one upon another in drawers.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'第四段提到收纳的关键是 \'nothing is stacked\'（没有东西堆叠），并举例 T-shirts 是 \'rolled and arranged beautifully\'（卷起来漂亮地排列），而非上下堆叠。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1424,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','8. Kondo became interested in tidying at the age of five.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'最后一段第一句明确说明：\'Kondo has been fond of tidying since she was five...\'（Kondo 从五岁起就喜欢整理……）。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1425,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','9. Kondo\'s own house is small but clean.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中提到了她对房屋整理的理念，但没有描述她自己房子的大小或具体状况。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1426,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','10. Kondo believes a well-organized house makes people\'s mind clear.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文章最后一段提到：\'She believes the inside of a house should be a place where there are no unnecessary things, and our thoughts become clear.\'（她认为屋内应是一个没有多余物品的地方，这样我们的思绪会变得清晰。）',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1427,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Nanay】Nanay had always been a part of my life. I believed grandmothers lived forever.\nShe taught me many lessons, though I often ignored them. Nanay urged me never to accept second-best. For her, “good enough” was never enough, from the grades you bring home from school to the service you receive in restaurants.\nWhen I was 13, Nanay sent me to Manila to attend high school, and I stayed there for university. I came back each summer, but after I got married the visits became less frequent. Soon all of her grandchildren had moved out. Nanay was left on her own. In her letters to me, she wrote of how lonely she was, but I never made the effort to spend more time with her.\nNanay died last year. She was 83. After the funeral, I went to our old house. Grandmother had kept so many things from my childhood: the toys; the letters I wrote home in my high school and university years, either asking for more rice or thanking her for sending fruit. Photos of her grandchildren were on display in the living room.\nWhen I visited her grave and reflected on all her birthdays I had allowed to pass, I was filled with sorrow. I thought about all the stories she never got a chance to tell me, about her life, about the girl she once had been, about the town I left behind. It occurred to me that perhaps she did not tell me because I did not know how to ask.\n\n11. The author was left in the care of Nanay because ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"his parents worked far away\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Nanay loved children\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"he wanted to stay with Nanay\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Nanay was a good teacher\"}]',NULL,NULL,'根据文中信息无法直接推断出作者被留给Nanay照顾的具体原因（通常是因为父母工作远，但文中未明确提及此点，仅提到Nanay送他去马尼拉上学）。若需作答，A为常见背景推测，但严格依据文本可能无解或需结合前文缺失部分。此处留空。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1428,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','12. In his childhood, the author thought that Nanay was ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"friendly\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"unkind\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"lonely\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"patient\"}]',NULL,NULL,'文中提到“I believed grandmothers lived forever”，并未直接描述童年时作者认为Nanay是friendly/unkind/lonely/patient中的哪一种。虽然Nanay对他要求严格（never accept second-best），但这不等于unkind。此题依据本页文本难以确定唯一答案，留空。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1429,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','13. According to the author, Nanay ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"ignored teaching the children\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"received little education\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"urged him to work for the best\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"preferred to live on her own\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第二段“Nanay urged me never to accept second-best.”可知，Nanay督促他追求最好，故选C。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1430,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','14. The author felt sad because he missed ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"the stories about Nanay\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Nanay’s funeral\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"the photo display of Nanay\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Nanay’s lessons\"}]','A',NULL,'根据最后一段“I thought about all the stories she never got a chance to tell me... I was filled with sorrow.”可知，作者悲伤是因为错过了听Nanay讲故事的机会，故选A。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1431,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','15. The tone of the text can be described as ______ .','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"humorous\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"joyful\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"critical\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"regretful\"}]','D',NULL,'文章表达了作者对祖母去世的悲痛，以及对自己生前未能多陪伴祖母、未能询问祖母故事的深深遗憾（sorrow, regret），故基调是后悔的（regretful），选D。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1432,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','Before losing weight, you\'d better ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"into fat\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"harm the liver\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"seek advice from a doctor\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"3 units of alcohol every day\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a lack of minerals and vitamins\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"4 glasses of water each day\"}]','D',NULL,'',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1433,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','The unused energy will be accumulated ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"into fat\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"harm the liver\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"seek advice from a doctor\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"3 units of alcohol every day\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a lack of minerals and vitamins\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"4 glasses of water each day\"}]','A',NULL,'',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1434,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','You should reduce drinks rich ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"into fat\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"harm the liver\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"seek advice from a doctor\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"3 units of alcohol every day\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a lack of minerals and vitamins\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"4 glasses of water each day\"}]','B',NULL,'',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1435,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','Women are advised to drink ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"into fat\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"harm the liver\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"seek advice from a doctor\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"3 units of alcohol every day\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a lack of minerals and vitamins\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"4 glasses of water each day\"}]','E',NULL,'',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1436,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','Longtime overdrinking may ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"into fat\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"harm the liver\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"seek advice from a doctor\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"3 units of alcohol every day\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a lack of minerals and vitamins\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"4 glasses of water each day\"}]','C',NULL,'',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1437,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','Missing breakfast may cause ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"into fat\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"in sugar\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"harm the liver\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"seek advice from a doctor\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"3 units of alcohol every day\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a lack of minerals and vitamins\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"4 glasses of water each day\"}]','F',NULL,'',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1438,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · Enjoy Yourself and Improve Your English】One student I knew in Tanzania was the daughter of a school teacher. On the first day of the long school holidays, a whole set of graded English books arrived at her house. __(26)__ The daughter read them all, starting from the easiest and working up to the most difficult. The holidays passed quickly and when the new school term started, she was far ahead of her classmates in English.\n\n__(27)__ I think there are three. First, learning a new language takes time and practice. It is the same with any skill, like swimming. There are no quicker ways.\n\nSecond, successful learning means moving from the easy to the difficult. __(28)__ You have to play very simple tunes before you move on, step by step, to more complex ones.\n\n__(29)__ The student was not trying to improve her English, though her English did improve. She liked the stories and was using them to pass the time. She became better at English without knowing it. Her brain was learning the language while she was concentrating on the stories.\n\nHowever, many students give two main reasons for not reading much. __(30)__ I am afraid this reason is very weak and simply not true. The other reason is that they do not enjoy it. This reason is stronger. In fact it can be divided into two. You may not enjoy reading because either the language is difficult, or the stories are boring.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One is that they have no time.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why don\'t students read more?\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"What lessons does this story teach us?\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Her mother had bought them for the school.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Third, reading stories in a new language is enjoyable.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"This is just like learning to play the piano.\"}]','D',NULL,'根据上下文，书到了家里，后面提到女儿读了这些书。选项 D \'Her mother had bought them for the school\'（她妈妈为学校买的）解释了书的来源，符合语境。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1439,4,NULL,'WORD_FILL','【原文 · My Little Niece】My little niece, a ten-month-old baby, is the most lovely child I have ever seen. Her face is like a red apple and her eyes are like __(31)__ stars. When you carry her in your arms, she likes to put her arms around your neck. All the __32__ in the family love her very much and often try to make her smile. But quite __33__ it is she who makes us __34__. Once I winked (眨眼) at her and she smiled. When I did it again, she watched me __35__: Then she tried to imitate. While I closed one eye to wink, she had to close __36__ eyes at the same time, and then __37__ opened them again. And that was her way to wink. We all __38__ into laughter. When we looked at her again, she was staring at us, puzzled, as if she were __39__, \"What are you laughing at?\" We all love this __40__ little baby.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"laugh\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"both\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"drink\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"grown-ups\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"attentively\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"asking\"}, {\"key\": \"G\", \"text\": \"cute\"}, {\"key\": \"H\", \"text\": \"flowers\"}, {\"key\": \"I\", \"text\": \"burst\"}, {\"key\": \"J\", \"text\": \"often\"}, {\"key\": \"K\", \"text\": \"bright\"}, {\"key\": \"L\", \"text\": \"quickly\"}]','K',NULL,'形容星星通常用 bright（明亮的）。eyes are like bright stars. 眼睛像明亮的星星。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1440,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Observing the Nature】Nature is __(41)__ (amazing) complex, Every day many different things happen in','[]','amazingly',NULL,'修饰形容词 complex 需要用副词形式。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1441,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Observing the Nature】Nature is amazingly (amazing) complex, Every day many different things happen in nature. Look around and observe. What do you see happening?\n__(41)__ (Live) things grow and die as __42__ (season) change. In nature, even the quietest place is not empty, because insects fill the air. Nature is so __43__ (vary) that there are millions of kinds of plants and animals to study. Time and patience are __44__ (need) to learn from nature. And that\'s __45__ (particular) true of the study of animals.\nYou can\'t just press a button on a bird and have it tell you how fast it can fly. And monkeys don\'t wear signs __46__ (tell) you how they take care of their young. To learn these things, you have to observe.\n__47__ (Scientist) observe animals in different ways. And each of them __48__ (give) the world something through their observations. Some help us make sense of the __49__ (nature) world. Others help us see the __50__ (important) of protecting it.','[]','Living',NULL,'此处作定语修饰名词things，表示“有生命的”，应填形容词形式。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1442,4,NULL,'WRITING','请根据所提供材料中的要求完成一篇 100 词左右的英文写作任务。\n某英文报社正在举行征文活动，请你以 “Uses of the Internet” 为题写一篇英文短文应征，内容包括：\n• 你常用网络做哪些事？\n• 网络对你的生活有何影响？','[]',NULL,'[\"题目：Uses of the Internet\", \"要点一：列举常用的网络功能（如学习、娱乐、社交等）\", \"要点二：阐述网络对生活的影响（如便利性、开阔视野等）\", \"字数要求：100词左右\"]','',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1443,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','【原文 · Do You Love Your Dog More Than Humans?】Elizabeth Anderson once had a dog named Grace. She and her husband cared for Grace and tried to keep her out of trouble. They took her on vacations and enjoyed her company around the house. When Grace died at age 14, they were deeply upset. Because Grace was a dog, \"I was unable to talk to anyone about this great grief.\" says Anderson.\n\"But it\'s common to feel that way after the loss of a dog,\" says Stanley Coren, a professor of psychology. \"Our relationship with dogs is simple. Some might call it true love.\"\nThe bond between people and their dogs is a lot like love. In one recent study, when the dogs and their owners just looked at each other, they both had a higher level of the hormone(荷尔蒙) associated with love. \"It is very natural to form a bond between dogs and humans,\" says Takefumi Kikusui, author of the study. \"But we found the same can\'t be said for humans and wolves.\"\n\"Dogs are man\'s best friend,\" says Coren. \"We\'ve trained them to be that way. We invented the dog to fit in our lives. For 14,000 years, we\'ve been creating an animal which understands our communications and we understand its communications. They have a bond with us.\" For example, if a person points to something in a distance, a dog will look in the direction of the finger, just like a human. But what about a wolf? \"It would simply look at the finger,\" Coren says.\nFor Anderson, dogs are more lovable than humans. She says: \"They try their best to please us. They want to do whatever we want to do. Their love is not limited. They are good at all the things we enjoy in a relationship.\"\n\nGrace became a member of Anderson\'s family at 14.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文中提到 \'When Grace died at age 14\'，说明 Grace 是在 14 岁时去世的，而不是在 14 岁时成为家庭成员。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1444,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Anderson enjoyed her time with Grace.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中第一段提到 \'They took her on vacations and enjoyed her company around the house.\'，说明 Anderson 享受和 Grace 在一起的时光。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1445,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Grace died in an accident.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中只提到 \'When Grace died at age 14\'，并没有说明死因是意外事故，也没有排除其他原因，属于未提及信息。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1446,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Coren does not understand people\'s grief over the loss of their dogs.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文中第二段提到 Coren 说 \'But it\'s common to feel that way after the loss of a dog\'，这表明他理解这种悲伤情绪是正常的，即他理解人们的悲痛。题目说他不懂，故为 False。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1447,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','The bond between humans and dogs can be compared to love.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中第三段第一句明确指出 \'The bond between people and their dogs is a lot like love.\'（人与狗之间的纽带很像爱）。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1448,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Dogs have the hormone associated with love.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中第三段提到研究结果：\'when the dogs and their owners just looked at each other, they both had a higher level of the hormone... associated with love.\'，说明狗体内确实有这种与爱相关的激素水平升高。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1449,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Kikusui knows why wolves are different from dogs.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','NG',NULL,'文中 Kikusui 提到了人类与狼之间没有同样的纽带 (\'we found the same can\'t be said for humans and wolves\')，但并未解释为什么狼和狗不同，或者他是否知道原因。这属于未提及信息。',3,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1450,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Man started to train dogs 14,000 years ago.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','T',NULL,'文中第四段提到 \'We\'ve trained them to be that way... For 14,000 years, we\'ve been creating an animal...\'，暗示了训练/创造过程持续了 14,000 年，即始于 14,000 年前。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1451,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','A wolf understands human communications.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文中第四段举例说明狗能理解人的指向动作，而关于狼则说 \'But what about a wolf? \"It would simply look at the finger,\"\'，这意味着狼不理解这个沟通信号，只是看着手指本身。因此狼不理解人类的沟通方式。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1452,4,NULL,'READING_JUDGE','Anderson finds humans more lovable than dogs.','[{\"key\": \"T\", \"text\": \"True\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"False\"}, {\"key\": \"NG\", \"text\": \"Not Given\"}]','F',NULL,'文章最后一段明确写道 \'For Anderson, dogs are more lovable than humans.\'（对 Anderson 来说，狗比人更可爱），题目说法相反。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1453,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Marta Garcia: Inspired by Technology】Marta Garcia is a high school senior. In the past years she has been working on a variety of projects. The projects are part of her work with Techbridge, a nonprofit organization. Techbridge was set up in 2000 to increase the number of women in science, technology, engineering and math (STEM). It offers a range of after-school activities for students.\n\nTechbridge focuses on learning by doing. It attracts Marta\'s interest. \"When I was a kid,\" says Marta, \"I wasn\'t into English. I was really into technology and math. My older sister was in Techbridge. She encouraged me to join. It was something for me to do after school. I found it pretty fun.\"\n\nMarta has created a complex music-making machine. Her latest project is a digital piano, which shows how far her STEM skills have advanced. Marta\'s instructors have been following her progress closely. \"I\'ve seen her master STEM skills,\" says Techbridge CEO Linda Kekelis. \"She\'s very confident to face challenges. She isn\'t afraid of temporary setbacks.\"\n\nMarta plans to attend Smith College this fall. She is still drawn to math and technology. But she does not want to be limited to one particular course of study.\n\n\"I\'m not sure what I want to do after college graduation,\" says Marta. \"I know a STEM career is an option.\" The future will be filled with jobs that require STEM skills. So her love of technology and her experience with Techbridge will serve her well.\n\n11. Techbridge was set up to ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"train women teachers\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"offer jobs for students\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"teach STEM at school\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"help girls learn STEM\"}]','D',NULL,'根据第一段中 \'Techbridge was set up in 2000 to increase the number of women in science, technology, engineering and math (STEM).\' 可知，该组织旨在增加女性在STEM领域的数量，即帮助女孩学习STEM。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1454,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Marta Garcia: Inspired by Technology】Marta Garcia is a high school senior. In the past years she has been working on a variety of projects. The projects are part of her work with Techbridge, a nonprofit organization. Techbridge was set up in 2000 to increase the number of women in science, technology, engineering and math (STEM). It offers a range of after-school activities for students.\n\nTechbridge focuses on learning by doing. It attracts Marta\'s interest. \"When I was a kid,\" says Marta, \"I wasn\'t into English. I was really into technology and math. My older sister was in Techbridge. She encouraged me to join. It was something for me to do after school. I found it pretty fun.\"\n\nMarta has created a complex music-making machine. Her latest project is a digital piano, which shows how far her STEM skills have advanced. Marta\'s instructors have been following her progress closely. \"I\'ve seen her master STEM skills,\" says Techbridge CEO Linda Kekelis. \"She\'s very confident to face challenges. She isn\'t afraid of temporary setbacks.\"\n\nMarta plans to attend Smith College this fall. She is still drawn to math and technology. But she does not want to be limited to one particular course of study.\n\n\"I\'m not sure what I want to do after college graduation,\" says Marta. \"I know a STEM career is an option.\" The future will be filled with jobs that require STEM skills. So her love of technology and her experience with Techbridge will serve her well.\n\n12. Marta Garcia works with Techbridge to ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"develop her interest\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"finish her education\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"improve her English\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"please her older sister\"}]','A',NULL,'根据第二段 \'It attracts Marta\'s interest.\' 以及她觉得这很有趣（\'I found it pretty fun.\'），可知她在Techbridge工作是为了发展她的兴趣。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1455,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Marta Garcia: Inspired by Technology】Marta Garcia is a high school senior. In the past years she has been working on a variety of projects. The projects are part of her work with Techbridge, a nonprofit organization. Techbridge was set up in 2000 to increase the number of women in science, technology, engineering and math (STEM). It offers a range of after-school activities for students.\n\nTechbridge focuses on learning by doing. It attracts Marta\'s interest. \"When I was a kid,\" says Marta, \"I wasn\'t into English. I was really into technology and math. My older sister was in Techbridge. She encouraged me to join. It was something for me to do after school. I found it pretty fun.\"\n\nMarta has created a complex music-making machine. Her latest project is a digital piano, which shows how far her STEM skills have advanced. Marta\'s instructors have been following her progress closely. \"I\'ve seen her master STEM skills,\" says Techbridge CEO Linda Kekelis. \"She\'s very confident to face challenges. She isn\'t afraid of temporary setbacks.\"\n\nMarta plans to attend Smith College this fall. She is still drawn to math and technology. But she does not want to be limited to one particular course of study.\n\n\"I\'m not sure what I want to do after college graduation,\" says Marta. \"I know a STEM career is an option.\" The future will be filled with jobs that require STEM skills. So her love of technology and her experience with Techbridge will serve her well.\n\n13. Linda Kekelis is impressed by Marta Garcia\'s ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"knowledge\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"interests\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"confidence\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"instructions\"}]','C',NULL,'根据第三段Linda Kekelis的话：\'She\'s very confident to face challenges.\' 可知她对Marta的信心印象深刻。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1456,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Marta Garcia: Inspired by Technology】Marta Garcia is a high school senior. In the past years she has been working on a variety of projects. The projects are part of her work with Techbridge, a nonprofit organization. Techbridge was set up in 2000 to increase the number of women in science, technology, engineering and math (STEM). It offers a range of after-school activities for students.\n\nTechbridge focuses on learning by doing. It attracts Marta\'s interest. \"When I was a kid,\" says Marta, \"I wasn\'t into English. I was really into technology and math. My older sister was in Techbridge. She encouraged me to join. It was something for me to do after school. I found it pretty fun.\"\n\nMarta has created a complex music-making machine. Her latest project is a digital piano, which shows how far her STEM skills have advanced. Marta\'s instructors have been following her progress closely. \"I\'ve seen her master STEM skills,\" says Techbridge CEO Linda Kekelis. \"She\'s very confident to face challenges. She isn\'t afraid of temporary setbacks.\"\n\nMarta plans to attend Smith College this fall. She is still drawn to math and technology. But she does not want to be limited to one particular course of study.\n\n\"I\'m not sure what I want to do after college graduation,\" says Marta. \"I know a STEM career is an option.\" The future will be filled with jobs that require STEM skills. So her love of technology and her experience with Techbridge will serve her well.\n\n14. The word \"setbacks\" (Para. 3) most probably means \"________\".','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Advances\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"difficulties\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"activities\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"Projects\"}]','B',NULL,'句意为“她不害怕暂时的挫折”。Setback意为挫折、阻碍，与difficulties（困难）意思相近。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1457,4,NULL,'READING_CHOICE','【原文 · Marta Garcia: Inspired by Technology】Marta Garcia is a high school senior. In the past years she has been working on a variety of projects. The projects are part of her work with Techbridge, a nonprofit organization. Techbridge was set up in 2000 to increase the number of women in science, technology, engineering and math (STEM). It offers a range of after-school activities for students.\n\nTechbridge focuses on learning by doing. It attracts Marta\'s interest. \"When I was a kid,\" says Marta, \"I wasn\'t into English. I was really into technology and math. My older sister was in Techbridge. She encouraged me to join. It was something for me to do after school. I found it pretty fun.\"\n\nMarta has created a complex music-making machine. Her latest project is a digital piano, which shows how far her STEM skills have advanced. Marta\'s instructors have been following her progress closely. \"I\'ve seen her master STEM skills,\" says Techbridge CEO Linda Kekelis. \"She\'s very confident to face challenges. She isn\'t afraid of temporary setbacks.\"\n\nMarta plans to attend Smith College this fall. She is still drawn to math and technology. But she does not want to be limited to one particular course of study.\n\n\"I\'m not sure what I want to do after college graduation,\" says Marta. \"I know a STEM career is an option.\" The future will be filled with jobs that require STEM skills. So her love of technology and her experience with Techbridge will serve her well.\n\n15. Marta Garcia\'s experience with Techbridge will ________.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"help her finish university\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"benefit her in the future\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"limit her to a STEM job\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"let her take fewer courses\"}]','B',NULL,'根据最后一段 \'So her love of technology and her experience with Techbridge will serve her well.\' 可知这段经历对她未来有好处（serve her well = benefit her）。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1458,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n① More and more people choose to make a five-year career plan. They think that the plan can help them to learn where they would like to go in the future. In fact, with a five-year plan, you can document the progress you have already made in your chosen career. You can also learn where you are likely to be heading in the future.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ①','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The first step to make a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The reason for changing a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The right time to apply for desired jobs\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The necessity to get some career advice\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"The importance of having a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"The abilities to fulfill a career plan\"}]','E',NULL,'第一段主要讲述了越来越多人制定五年职业规划，以及该计划能帮助他们了解未来方向、记录进步等好处，即拥有职业规划的重要性。故选 E。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1459,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n② The initial step is to think about an end goal. This can help you to gain focus on your career. When you are setting your end goal, make sure that you do not choose a job purely based on its salary. Though salaries for the job may be high now, demand often changes over time.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ②','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The first step to make a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The reason for changing a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The right time to apply for desired jobs\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The necessity to get some career advice\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"The importance of having a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"The abilities to fulfill a career plan\"}]','A',NULL,'第二段首句指出“The initial step is to think about an end goal”（第一步是思考最终目标），整段围绕制定职业规划的第一步展开。故选 A。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1460,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n③ The next step is to get an adviser. An adviser is generally a person who has achieved success in the career that you wish to take. Ideally, an adviser can give you sound career advice. Make sure that you choose your adviser carefully as they may provide you with great insight.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ③','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The first step to make a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The reason for changing a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The right time to apply for desired jobs\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The necessity to get some career advice\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"The importance of having a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"The abilities to fulfill a career plan\"}]','D',NULL,'第三段建议“get an adviser”（找一位顾问），并说明顾问能提供职业建议（career advice）。故选 D。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1461,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n④ Next, you will need to think about the abilities that you will need to fulfill your career plan. Assess your current work experience and past education; figure out any specific skills or knowledge you already have; identify any gaps that you will need to fill in order to meet your end goal; and list any opportunities that you can take to improve the skills or knowledge that you have identified.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ④','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The first step to make a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The reason for changing a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The right time to apply for desired jobs\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The necessity to get some career advice\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"The importance of having a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"The abilities to fulfill a career plan\"}]','F',NULL,'第四段开头提到要思考实现职业规划所需的“abilities”（能力），后续内容也是关于评估技能和知识。故选 F。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1462,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n⑤ Finally, you will need to identify the jobs that you would like to take. If you feel that you already have the required skills and knowledge, apply for them. Even if you fail to get one, you will gain some invaluable knowledge from the interview.\n\nTask 1: Paragraph ⑤','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The first step to make a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The reason for changing a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"The right time to apply for desired jobs\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"The necessity to get some career advice\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"The importance of having a career plan\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"The abilities to fulfill a career plan\"}]','C',NULL,'第五段以“Finally”开头，建议确定想要从事的工作，并在具备条件时去申请（apply for them）。选项 C 中的“apply for desired jobs”与此对应。故选 C。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1463,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n① More and more people choose to make a five-year career plan. They think that the plan can help them to learn where they would like to go in the future. In fact, with a five-year plan, you can document the progress you have already made in your chosen career. You can also learn where you are likely to be heading in the future.\n\nA career plan can give you ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"the salary alone\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"to write it well\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"get well prepared\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"to find an adviser\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"offer some useful knowledge\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a clear future direction\"}]','F',NULL,'根据文章第一段 \'They think that the plan can help them to learn where they would like to go in the future\'，即职业计划能给你明确未来的方向。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1464,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n② The initial step is to think about an end goal. This can help you to gain focus on your career. When you are setting your end goal, make sure that you do not choose a job purely based on its salary. Though salaries for the job may be high now, demand often changes over time.\n\nWhen you choose a job, you should not focus on ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"the salary alone\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"to write it well\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"get well prepared\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"to find an adviser\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"offer some useful knowledge\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a clear future direction\"}]','A',NULL,'根据文章第二段 \'make sure that you do not choose a job purely based on its salary\'，即不要仅仅关注薪水。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1465,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n③ The next step is to get an adviser. An adviser is generally a person who has achieved success in the career that you wish to take. Ideally, an adviser can give you sound career advice. Make sure that you choose your adviser carefully as they may provide you with great insight.\n\nTo gain career guidance, you should try ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"the salary alone\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"to write it well\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"get well prepared\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"to find an adviser\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"offer some useful knowledge\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a clear future direction\"}]','D',NULL,'根据文章第三段 \'The next step is to get an adviser... Ideally, an adviser can give you sound career advice\'，即为了获得职业指导，应该尝试找一位顾问。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1466,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n④ Next, you will need to think about the abilities that you will need to fulfill your career plan. Assess your current work experience and past education; figure out any specific skills or knowledge you already have; identify any gaps that you will need to fill in order to meet your end goal; and list any opportunities that you can take to improve the skills or knowledge that you have identified.\n\nTo fulfill a career plan, you should ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"the salary alone\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"to write it well\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"get well prepared\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"to find an adviser\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"offer some useful knowledge\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a clear future direction\"}]','C',NULL,'根据文章第四段内容，为了实现职业计划，需要评估经验、技能并填补空白，这属于做好充分准备（get well prepared）。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1467,4,NULL,'SECTION_MATCH','【原文 · How to Create a Five-Year Career Plan】\n⑤ Finally, you will need to identify the jobs that you would like to take. If you feel that you already have the required skills and knowledge, apply for them. Even if you fail to get one, you will gain some invaluable knowledge from the interview.\n\nA job interview can ______.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"the salary alone\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"to write it well\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"get well prepared\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"to find an adviser\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"offer some useful knowledge\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"a clear future direction\"}]','E',NULL,'根据文章第五段 \'you will gain some invaluable knowledge from the interview\'，即面试能提供有用的知识。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1468,4,NULL,'SENTENCE_FILL','【原文 · What Does Happiness Mean?】Happiness in life differs for all of us. __26__ Very often we are happy, but we just don\'t realize it. If you think about what actually makes you happy, you might find you have those things already around you.\n\nYour happiness depends entirely on you. __27__ It is something inside you that you have to find and work towards. You can take positive action and make changes to your life or yourself in order to achieve happiness.\n\n__28__ The first step for you to do so is to look at your feelings and ask yourself questions such as \"if I could be enjoying something in my life, what would it be?\" and \"what makes me feel satisfied in my life right now?\" Once you understand what your idea of happiness is, you can build on what you have now or focus on changing your life to what you would like it to be.\n\nThe important thing to do is to examine your feelings by way of the answers you give to your questions. __29__ You should also focus on the good or bad feelings you get from your questions and answers.\n\nHappiness is something that is already right there inside you. You just have to realize what it is and bring it out to start enjoying life. It can be found in family life, work, relationships, nature or a pet, to name just a few. __(30)__ The point is where to look. You should look in the right direction, that is, your inner self.','[{\"key\": \"A\", \"text\": \"No one else can give it to you.\"}, {\"key\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You should examine them honestly.\"}, {\"key\": \"C\", \"text\": \"Happiness is easy to define.\"}, {\"key\": \"D\", \"text\": \"You should understand what happiness means to you.\"}, {\"key\": \"E\", \"text\": \"Actually, it can be found in anything and any situation.\"}, {\"key\": \"F\", \"text\": \"What makes one person happy may not bring happiness to another.\"}]','E',NULL,'前文提到幸福可以在家庭、工作、人际关系等中找到，后文说关键在于往哪里看。选项 E \'实际上，它可以在任何事物和任何情况下找到\' 承上启下，符合语境。',2,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,2.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1469,4,NULL,'CLOZE_TRANSFORM','【原文 · Does Watching TV Relieve Stress?】After a tough day, you may possibly (possible) turn on the TV, Getting __(41)__ (lose) in your favorite show seems like an _42_ (effect) way to relax. But it may make things worse.\nIt is _43_ (general) believed that watching TV can _44_ (able) people to relax. It provides a temporary escape from stresses. However, the same can\'t be _45_ (say) for those who are busy and _46_ (tire). Those people can feel guilty about _47_ (spend) so much time in front of the TV. They tend to see it as a form of procrastination (拖延). In other _48_ (word), they are avoiding other important things out of _49_ (lazy). They feel they are giving in to TV. That feeling _50_ (keep) them from relaxing.','[]','lost',NULL,'get lost in 是固定搭配，意为“沉迷于……”。',1,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,1.5,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09'),(1470,4,NULL,'WRITING','某英文报社正在举办题为“Online Shopping”的征文活动。请你根据下述写作要点提交一篇英文短文应征。\n● 你所了解的网上购物情况。\n● 你对网上购物的看法。','[]',NULL,'[\"描述网上购物的现状（普及程度、主要商品等）\", \"阐述对网上购物的看法（优缺点分析）\", \"总结观点或提出建议\"]','',3,'自考英语专升本试题',NULL,30.0,'DRAFT',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-18 21:59:09','2026-10-18 21:59:09');

